window.AKK_EASTERN_PALACES_DEVOUT_YET_AMOROUS_CONSORT_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_EASTERN_PALACES_DEVOUT_YET_AMOROUS_CONSORT_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1","paragraphs":["In the spring of the nineteenth year of the Pingyuan era, the palace was holding its triennial selection of consorts.","The Crown Prince had been married for six years, yet had few children. This time, four new women were bestowed upon the Eastern Palace.","Shen Yanshui was one of them.","“Shen-jiejie, you’ve been bestowed upon His Highness the Crown Prince!”","Though the voice beside Shen Yanshui had been lowered, it still carried barely suppressed excitement. Shen Yanshui pressed down the disappointment in her heart, along with a trace of confusion.","How had she ended up in the Crown Prince’s Eastern Palace?","Xu Qingle watched her expression and asked hesitantly in a soft voice, “Shen-jiejie, are you... unhappy?”","Shen Yanshui turned to her and smiled, her eyes curving like crescent moons. “No. I’m simply too happy and didn’t know how to react for a moment.”","Forget it. The Crown Prince it was. The imperial edict had already been issued—what else could she do?","In her previous life, the apocalypse had arrived when she was in college.","Fortunately, she had been lucky enough to awaken a wood-element ability.","Even after transmigrating, her wood-element ability had remained with her.","It was just that the power she had once wielded as easily as her own limbs could now only be faintly sensed. Not only was it exceedingly weak, she could not use it at all.","Fortunately, in this life she had been reborn as a young lady of the Duke of Loyalty’s residence in the Great Yong Dynasty. She did not need an ability to get by.","Although she was a daughter born of a concubine, her stepmother was not particularly harsh. The legitimate and illegitimate children of the household were all provided with adequate food, clothing, and necessities.","Thus, she had spent sixteen years lying around peacefully at home, with plenty to eat and drink. Since the world around her was no longer filled with the dangers of the apocalypse, she had gradually let go of her obsession with her ability.","Some time ago, under her stepmother’s arrangements, she had begun meeting potential marriage candidates.","She had been exceptionally obedient and compliant about it.","The Great Yong Dynasty greatly valued lavish dowries.","Her biological father was, at any rate, the duke of a hereditary noble house, while her stepmother was the legitimate daughter of a marquis’s family. Both of them cared deeply about appearances.","They certainly would not shortchange her when it came to her dowry.","Only... she had never expected something to go awry midway.","Three years ago, her elder sister, who had entered the palace, had already become pregnant. Then, news suddenly came that she had miscarried.","The miscarriage had damaged her health, leaving her unable to conceive again.","After the household received the letter her elder sister had sent, it took only a few days for her stepmother to call off the marriage that had been verbally agreed upon for her.","Her stepmother had also summoned her for a private conversation. Her meaning, both explicit and implied, was that Shen Yanshui should enter the palace to help her elder sister compete for the Emperor’s favor and bear him a child. In return, she would enjoy a comfortable life in the future.","Shen Yanshui was naturally unwilling. Who would want to serve an old man? And not just any old man, but the old Emperor, who held the power of life and death over everyone.","But her refusal had been useless.","She did not particularly care.","Who said that entering the palace meant she had to enter the old Emperor’s harem?","So, during the period when she was learning palace etiquette, she had put some effort into finding out about the princes who had reached a suitable age but remained unmarried.","In the end, she had chosen the Fifth Prince.","The Fifth Prince had been blind since birth, making it impossible for him to inherit the throne. He was destined to spend his life as a wealthy prince. No matter which prince eventually ascended the throne, none of them would target the Fifth Prince.","Wealth, good food, security—everything she wanted was guaranteed. It was practically perfect!","During this period, she had made two appearances before Consort Liang.","Judging by Consort Liang’s attitude toward her over the past few days, Shen Yanshui had thought she had succeeded.","She had never expected to end up in the Crown Prince’s Eastern Palace.","Xu Qingle stared blankly for a moment at the faint smile on Shen Yanshui’s face.","Shen Yanshui wore a lotus-colored plain silk, narrow-sleeved top beneath a sky-blue half-sleeved robe. Her hair was arranged in a tassel coiffure. Her skin was as smooth and pale as jade, her brows like spring mountains, and her pair of bright, peach-blossom eyes seemed to brim with feeling. Even when she was not smiling, they were enough to make it difficult for anyone to look away.","Her crow-black lashes were long, thick, and elegantly curved. Her eyes were clear and luminous, as though washed by rain. Even as a woman herself, Xu Qingle could not help feeling her cheeks grow warm and her heart race as she looked at her.","Gazing at Shen Yanshui’s nearly flawless face, she blushed and said softly, “With Shen-jiejie’s beauty, His Highness the Crown Prince will surely value and favor you.”","Shen Yanshui gently squeezed her hand and smiled without replying for a moment.","Her elder sister currently lived in Consort Lan’s Jingfu Palace and was one of Noble Consort Lan’s people.","Noble Consort Lan and the Crown Prince’s birth mother—now Her Majesty the Empress—were mortal enemies.","It was said that after the Empress had fallen seriously ill two years ago, she had never truly recovered.","Even during this selection, the Empress had only appeared at the very beginning.","The rest of the proceedings had been handled jointly by Consorts Xian, Liang, Shu, and De, with Noble Consort Lan taking charge.","The Crown Prince was the Empress’s only son, while Noble Consort Lan’s two sons, the Fourth Prince and the Eighth Prince, had both come of age.","The Fourth Prince was even only a year younger than the Crown Prince.","Shen Yanshui was beginning to wonder whether Noble Consort Lan had deliberately arranged for her to enter the Eastern Palace simply to disgust the Empress and the Crown Prince.","Or perhaps Noble Consort Lan intended to turn her into an informant and pawn later on?","She had no idea. At any rate, no one had secretly approached her so far.","Her elder sister had summoned her to Jingfu Palace twice.","But from what her elder sister had said, both explicitly and implicitly, she merely wished to reassure Shen Yanshui while turning her into a tool for bearing children.","In any case, to anyone watching, she was probably a pawn Noble Consort Lan had placed in the Eastern Palace.","Forget about receiving the Crown Prince’s favor. As long as the Crown Prince did not vent his anger on her—and preferably treated her as though she were invisible—she would be perfectly content.","Shen Yanshui raised her eyes to Xu Qingle and said with a smile, “I’ve heard that the Seventh Prince is known for his filial piety. In the future, you should simply serve Consort Wan together with His Highness the Seventh Prince.”","Xu Qingle’s delicate, lovely face flushed slightly. She nodded earnestly. “Yes. I’ll remember everything Shen-jiejie has told me.”","She had been bestowed upon the Seventh Prince as a secondary consort and would marry him at the end of the year.","“Have all of you young ladies finished packing?” a matron in the Palace of Gathered Elegance asked with a smile. Her voice and manner were noticeably more respectful than usual.","Before today, they had been candidates studying palace etiquette, their fates still uncertain.","But now, some had been eliminated, while others were future imperial princesses by marriage. There were also some who could already be addressed as “Young Lady.”","The imperial edict had been issued. All that remained was for the palace maids and eunuchs to lead them to their respective destinations.","*","“What did you say? Fourth Sister has entered the Eastern Palace?!”","A startled cry rang out from the rear hall of Jingfu Palace.","Lady Shen wore a plain silk robe, and her hair had not yet been arranged. Her originally lovely face was now pale and slightly gaunt. She had been reclining sideways against a cushioned couch, but at those words, she instinctively straightened.","She looked at her personal maid, Xiang Mo, in astonishment. “How could it be the Eastern Palace? Are you certain you didn’t hear incorrectly?”","Xiang Mo wore a maid’s narrow-sleeved, round-collared robe of green patterned fabric. A goose-yellow sash encircled her waist, and a pale-green ribbon tied her hair into twin hanging buns. At that moment, she furrowed her brows, bowed, and answered in a low voice, “In reply to Your Ladyship, this servant made careful inquiries. There is absolutely no mistake. Fourth Miss Shen was indeed bestowed upon the Crown Prince by His Majesty.”","The astonishment on Lady Shen’s face did not fade. Instead, it was joined by even greater pallor. She pressed one thin hand against the small table, gripping it so tightly that her knuckles turned white. As though she had lost her soul, she murmured, “How could it be the Crown Prince...?”","Two months ago, after her miscarriage, she had begun suffering one nightmare after another.","She dreamed that after her miscarriage, she gradually lost the Emperor’s favor.","She dreamed that the Emperor died suddenly.","She dreamed that the Crown Prince unexpectedly contracted an epidemic, beyond the help of medicine and unable to be saved.","In the end, it was the Sixth Prince who ascended the throne...","As a former imperial consort who had long since lost the Emperor’s favor and had no child to rely on, she was ultimately sent to a temple, where she endured half a lifetime beside the green lamps and ancient Buddha.","The legitimate younger sister who had been lazy and useless since childhood, Shen Yanshui, married a newly appointed Presented Scholar and ultimately received the rank of a First-Rank Lady of Imperial Mandate, gaining both honor and prestige.","A month ago, after comparing the events in her dreams with reality and confirming them one by one, she had begun to believe everything in that nightmare.","She had then sent a letter to her mother.","Why had she met such a miserable end in her previous life, while Fourth Sister could so effortlessly obtain wealth, honor, and glory?","Lady Shen’s expression grew uncontrollably ugly, revealing a jealousy of which she herself was unaware.","Lady Shen touched her lower abdomen. No matter what happened in the future, if she could raise a child of her own, it would serve as a safeguard—a way out for her later on.","Only with that reason would Father and Mother send Fourth Sister into the palace.","But she had clearly mentioned it to the Noble Consort, and Her Ladyship had not refused. Why, then, had Fourth Miss Shen ended up entering the Eastern Palace?","She remembered that after the Crown Prince died, the Sixth Prince had not ascended the throne immediately. The Crown Prince still had a legitimate son.","At the time, the court had been filled with calls to establish the Crown Prince’s eldest legitimate son as the Crown Heir, simply because the Crown Prince represented the orthodox line of succession.","But the Crown Prince’s eldest legitimate son had been in poor health. In the end, it was still the Sixth Prince who ascended the throne...","“...Mistress? Mistress?”","Xiang Mo’s face was full of concern.","Seeing her muttering as though possessed, her complexion growing paler by the moment, Xiang Mo hurried forward to support her.","Lady Shen clutched Xiang Mo’s sleeve tightly with one hand. Her chest heaved rapidly as she stared at her and asked in haste, “Do you know which consort selected Fourth Sister?”","Xiang Mo quickly replied, “To answer you, Mistress, it was the Noble Consort.”","Lady Shen’s hand suddenly tightened, and her expression became even more unpleasant.","Seeing this, Xiang Mo could not help frowning worriedly. She comforted her, “Mistress, please don’t worry. The imperial physicians said that as long as you take proper care of yourself, your health will gradually recover. It is not as though you are completely unable to bear children.”","“The child you give birth to yourself will naturally be far better than one born from Fourth Miss Shen. Why place all your hopes on Fourth Sister?”","“I heard that Consort Shu also injured her health after giving birth to the Sixth Prince. After recuperating for several years, did she not go on to give birth to the Seventh Princess? Mistress, your good days are still ahead of you.”","Lady Shen listened to her words, brows knitted as she pondered for a moment. At last, her expression gradually eased.","How could she have forgotten? Consort Shu and the still-unnoticed Sixth Prince were the truly crucial ones.","Besides, Xiang Mo was right. She was not entirely incapable of bearing children; in her dream, it was only after her miscarriage that she spent her days drowning in tears and gradually lost the Emperor’s favor.","She still had plenty of time. She could plan everything slowly.","It was just a pity about Fourth Sister...","After the Crown Prince died, Fourth Sister would probably meet the same fate she had suffered in her previous life, would she not?","Perhaps her fate would be even worse than Lady Shen’s."]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: Meeting the Crown Princess","paragraphs":["From the Palace of Gathered Elegance to the Eastern Palace’s Palace of Everlasting Celebration, Shen Yanshui walked in the middle of the group, silent all the way.","Among the Crown Prince’s wives and concubines, aside from the Crown Princess, the ranks followed the ancestral system. In descending order, they were Liangdi, Liangyuan, Chenghui, Zhaoxun, and, at the very bottom, Fengyi.","Of the four newcomers, she had been given the rank of Zhaoxun.","Above her were a Liangyuan and a Chenghui, while below her was a Fengyi.","After thinking over the family backgrounds of the other women, she realized that, apart from herself, not one came from a family of military nobles or generals. Their fathers and elder brothers were almost all civil officials.","This did not surprise her. The Great Yong Dynasty’s preference for civil officials over military men was hardly a recent development.","After passing through several covered corridors, they heard the eunuch leading them exchange a few cheerful words with the palace maids at the entrance. Before long, their party was ushered inside.","Looking up, Shen Yanshui saw a main hall five bays wide, flanked by side rooms on either side. The courtyard was paved entirely with gray bricks, their intricate patterns spreading out like rippling water.","At the center of the courtyard stood an artificial mountain assembled from Taihu stones. Its unusual contours were elegant and graceful, while a clear stream trickled melodiously down between the rocks. Several clusters of exotic flowers grew from the crevices, their names unknown to her, though they were blooming beautifully.","“This servant pays his respects to the Crown Princess. May Your Highness enjoy perfect health.”","“Rise.” A warm, gentle voice carrying a hint of laughter rang out.","The Crown Princess wore a pale violet jacket embroidered with winding flowers and edged in gold. Beneath it was a fresh-colored skirt decorated with flowers and strings of pearls. A peony crown adorned her head, along with a jeweled golden hair ornament fitted with hanging pearl strands. Her bearing was dignified and gentle, and she shone with magnificence.","As soon as she finished speaking, Hongling, the senior palace maid beside her, stepped forward with a smile. Dressed in a brown, patterned round-collared robe, she had tied her hair with a gold-dusted, color-fading ribbon adorned with a golden bead. She slipped a small purse into the eunuch’s hand.","“Thank you for your hard work today, Eunuch Zhang.”","Zhang Fu accepted the purse with a broad smile and tucked it into his sleeve. “Your Highness needn’t worry. Everyone admitted to the Eastern Palace has personally received His Majesty’s approval. They are all sure to be fine young women and will certainly not cause Your Highness any trouble. The several young ladies are still waiting outside. What does Your Highness think...?”","The Crown Princess smiled. “Then let them all come in. It is time I became acquainted with my new sisters.”","“Yes, Your Highness.”","Before long, the four women were led into the hall by Matron Zhao. They passed around a huanghuali screen embroidered with landscapes representing the four seasons.","Shen Yanshui quickly raised her eyes to glance at the Crown Princess seated at the front. She was a woman of dignified, gentle, and noble bearing.","The palace maids on either side lifted the pearl-studded brocade curtains. Matron Zhao of the Palace Administration Bureau led the women in one after another. They bent at the waist and paid their respects.","“Greetings to the Crown Princess. May Your Highness enjoy peace and good health.”","Shen Yanshui stood in the middle, her eyes lowered to the tips of her shoes as she followed the others in making a perfectly proper salute.","“Rise, all of you. There is no need for such ceremony.” The Crown Princess looked at the group of striking, radiant newcomers before her, and the flawless smile on her face stiffened for an instant.","Matron Zhao bowed and introduced them one by one. “Your Highness, this is Lady Zhang. Her grandfather is Minister Zhang of the Ministry of Rites.”","Lady Zhang had a quiet, scholarly face. She wore a sandalwood-colored long robe of plain satin, subtly embroidered with silver designs, and a jade hairpin in her hair. At a glance, she looked every inch the dignified and well-bred young lady.","The Crown Princess nodded and asked with a smile, “Then the lady beside her must be Lady Wu, daughter of Minister Wu of the Dali Temple?”","“I had long heard that Miss Wu of the Wu family was a beauty of surpassing grace, possessing the allure of a sinking fish and falling geese. Seeing you today, I find the rumors were not exaggerated. At first glance, you are so beautiful that even I nearly forgot myself.”","At those words, Lady Wu instinctively lifted her chin slightly, the corners of her lips curling upward.","She had a striking and dazzling face, wearing a pomegranate-red skirt patterned with entwined chrysanthemums. A jade hibiscus pendant hung from the sash around her waist, while gold, jade, and agate ornaments adorned her hair. She was radiant and eye-catching.","Having received the Crown Princess’s praise, she grew even more pleased with herself. With an ingratiating smile, she said, “Your Highness is too kind. My beauty is not even one ten-thousandth of the Crown Princess’s.”","Shen Yanshui stood with lowered eyes, her expression meek and proper. She seemed to feel, with perfect clarity, the instant of sudden silence that descended around them.","She could not help sighing inwardly. Lady Wu had probably tried to flatter the wrong person and ended up striking a sore spot.","Lady Wu was indeed beautiful, with bright, flamboyant features that made her a genuine beauty. But as for the Crown Princess’s appearance...","It was not bad, but compared with Lady Wu, it could only be called delicate and refined.","Hearing Lady Wu’s words, no one would take them as praise. They sounded much more like mockery.","The Crown Princess’s lips stiffened for a moment. After looking Lady Wu over, she said, “Lady Wu, did you have honey on your lips today?”","Lady Wu failed to catch the sarcasm. Beaming, she replied, “It is only because Your Highness was born with such natural beauty.”","From the corner of her eye, Shen Yanshui could almost see the Crown Princess’s lips growing rigid.","Matron Zhao gave a light cough and resumed the introductions, though this time she made them much more quickly and succinctly.","Whether the Crown Princess was exhausted from poor health or for some other reason, she did not show any particular favor toward the others.","When Matron Zhao introduced Shen Yanshui, the Crown Princess merely praised her with a sigh, saying that she had a lovely face.","She made no mention of Noble Consort Lan or Shen Yanshui’s elder sister, Lady Shen.","Seeing Lady Wu’s unfriendly gaze upon her, Shen Yanshui smiled at her, not taking it particularly seriously.","At the sight of that smile, Lady Wu immediately frowned in displeasure.","After the introductions, Shen Yanshui learned that the last of the four newcomers, Lady Lin, was the daughter of the magistrate of Xuzhou.","The Crown Princess’s palace maids brought in several cups of tea. Beginning with Lady Zhang, each woman stepped forward to offer tea to the Crown Princess.","When it was Shen Yanshui’s turn, she followed the rules, lowered her eyes, and began to present the tea. At the same time, she felt a gaze descend upon her from above.","After two breaths, the Crown Princess finally lifted the cup and lightly touched it to her lips. Her lowered eyes rested on the face before her.","Shen Yanshui’s beauty was in no way inferior to Lady Wu’s; if anything, it was even more striking. The sight made the Crown Princess deeply uncomfortable.","But when she remembered Shen Yanshui’s connection to Noble Consort Lan, that suffocating feeling eased somewhat.","Besides, the Crown Prince had never been particularly fond of women. Even if Shen Yanshui possessed beauty capable of toppling cities, what difference could it make? She still could not stir up any great waves.","After everyone had finished offering tea, the Crown Princess followed protocol and delivered several solemn admonitions. Then her expression softened, and she said with a smile, “I hope all of you will serve His Highness the Crown Prince wholeheartedly and give him many children as soon as possible.”","“Yes, Your Highness. We will remember your instruction.”","“All right. I have been feeling somewhat unwell these past few days, so I will not keep you here to talk today. I would not want to pass my illness on to you.” The Crown Princess smiled and continued, “Matron, lead the ladies to their respective courtyards so they may settle in.”","Matron Zhou respectfully replied, “Yes, Your Highness.”","*","The place where the Crown Princess lived was called the Hall of Gathered Fragrance, located in the rear hall of the Palace of Everlasting Celebration. The front hall, the Hall of Honored Roots, was where the Crown Prince discussed affairs with the officials of the Eastern Palace. The main hall of the Palace of Everlasting Celebration was where the Crown Prince usually studied and attended to his daily affairs.","Behind the Hall of Gathered Fragrance was a series of rear rooms where the Crown Prince’s consorts lived. Five small courtyards stood side by side across the rear quarters.","Matron Zhou led Shen Yanshui to the one on the far left.","With a smile, she said, “Lady Shen and Lady Liu will be living in Lotus Heart Court from now on. Lady Shen will take the eastern side room, and Lady Liu the western. If you lack anything in your daily provisions, simply send someone to inform us. This old servant will make sure everything is arranged properly for both of you.”","Shen Yanshui turned sideways to return a half-courtesy.","When it came to official ranks, the head matron serving the Crown Princess held a higher status than her, who was only a Seventh-Rank Crown Prince's Lady of Training.","She stepped forward with a warm smile, quickly supporting Matron Zhou's arm as she said, \"Thank you so much for your trouble today, Matron Zhou.\" As she spoke, she handed over a purse she had prepared long in advance.","Matron Zhou did not decline it at all. She accepted it with a smile, all the while saying that Her Ladyship was being too polite.","Seeing this, Lady Liu, who was standing beside her, suddenly slipped the gold-inlaid jade bangle off her wrist and said with a grin, \"I will surely have to rely on your guidance a great deal in the future. Please do not take offense at this small gesture.\"","Matron Zhou still accepted it with a beaming smile. After exchanging a few more polite remarks, she said, \"If the two young mistresses have no further needs, this old servant will take her leave first to report back to Her Highness the Crown Princess.\"","\"Take care, Matron.\"","It was not until Matron Zhou's figure had vanished completely from sight that Shen Yanshui withdrew her gaze, and turned to look at the several palace maids and eunuchs who had been waiting respectfully at the side.","One of the maids, dressed in a blue round-collar robe with a pale yellow sash tied around her waist, stepped forward nimbly at once, curtsied again and greeted her, \"This servant Cuiyun pays her respects to her master. The east side chamber has already been tidied up properly by us. Would Her Ladyship like to go inside first to rest for the noon nap?\"","\"Very well, lead the way,\" Shen Yanshui replied with a clear, bright laugh.","She was in no hurry to tour the small courtyard just yet. She had been walking, standing, and kneeling nonstop all morning, so she wanted to sit down and rest first, and get to know the staff assigned to serve her.","Before walking off, she looked over at Lady Liu and said politely with a smile, \"Please make yourself at home, Lady Liu. I will head in to rest first.\"","Lady Liu was momentarily dazzled by her bright, lovely smile, and unconsciously curtsied back. By the time she came to her senses, she could only catch sight of Shen Yanshui's graceful, swaying figure from behind.","All of her original mood to wander around the courtyard had vanished in an instant. She turned around and walked straight into the west side chamber.","After entering the room, Shen Yanshui glanced around at the furnishings, and found nothing particularly surprising about them. After all, she had lived a life of wealth and luxury for more than ten years.","The several maids and eunuchs behind her watched as their new master lifted her feet and headed straight for the soft couch placed under the window in the eastern warm pavilion.","Once seated, she casually pulled over two soft pillows printed with heavenly fragrance patterns, and leaned back against them. Her movements were so familiar and comfortable as she reclined lazily, as if all the strength had suddenly drained from her body, that the servants were momentarily taken aback.","Even so, their new mistress was still so stunningly beautiful that no one dared to look at her directly.","Shen Yanshui leaned against the soft couch, letting out a soft sigh of relief. She looked at the four maids and two young eunuchs before her and said with a smile, \"All of you, introduce yourselves one by one.\"","Cuiyun, the maid who had stepped forward first, was the first to kneel down. She said respectfully, \"This servant greets Her Ladyship. I am Cuiyun. I entered the palace three years ago, and used to serve in the Imperial Food Bureau.\"","The rest followed her lead, kneeling down and speaking respectfully one after another. \"This servant greets Her Ladyship. I am Liu'er. I entered the palace three years ago, and was assigned to work in the Imperial Laundry Bureau before.\"","\"This servant is Xiuzhu. I entered the palace three years ago, and was in charge of sweeping and cleaning the Imperial Garden.\"","\"This servant is Chun'er. I am fifteen years old, and have only been in the palace for a year. I have been studying palace rules and etiquette under the guidance of matrons all this time.\"","After the four maids kneeling at the front had finished introducing themselves, the two young eunuchs at the back, dressed in crow-blue narrow-sleeved round-collar gowns with side slits and wearing crow-black headscarves, spoke up.","One of them was Little Lu, eighteen years old, with a rather honest and slow-witted look on his face. He used to tend to flowers and plants in the palace of a certain Beauty, but after that Beauty was demoted and sent to the Cold Palace for violating palace rules, he was reassigned back to the Palace Eunuch Service.","The other was Little Fu, sixteen years old. He had a small round face, with two dimples showing when he smiled, and fair, clean features that made him look very delicate and endearing.","\"This servant used to be in the Pavilion of Literary Profundity, in charge of drying and airing books. I can recognize a few characters.\"","Shen Yanshui looked a little surprised when she heard that. There were not many palace maids and eunuchs in the imperial palace who could read.","\"Are any of the rest of you able to read as well?\"","As expected, the chance of finding another such useful talent one after another was very slim. Even so, she was not disappointed. She looked at all of them with her smile unchanged, saying, \"It does not matter if you cannot read. As long as you are willing to learn, that is enough.\"","After all, someone had to take care of all kinds of work, right?","Understanding the implication in her words, all of them could not help feeling overjoyed. \"Thank you for Your Ladyship's great kindness!\"","It was not that they were unwilling to learn to read, but without the explicit permission of the master they served, no one in the palace would teach the palace maids and eunuchs how to read.","And if they wanted to advance to a better position, being able to read was an essential skill.","Seeing their excited and grateful expressions, Shen Yanshui smiled. \"Do not knock your heads and hurt yourselves while kowtowing. Since this is our first meeting, you do not know my temperament very well, so I will make this clear first. I rarely lose my temper, but that does not mean I have no temper at all.\"","\"On a daily basis, all you need to do is to be loyal, fulfill your duties properly, and finish all the tasks assigned to you.\"","\"If any of you wish to seek a different path in the future, you may speak to me frankly. Since we have shared the bond of master and servant, we can part ways amicably. But...\"","As she spoke, her voice grew softer, and she continued slowly with a gentle smile, \"If anyone has improper intentions, tries to play tricks and schemes, and does anything to betray their master...\"","The several maids and eunuchs instantly tensed up, repeatedly saying that they would never dare to do such a thing.","They had not expected that their new mistress, who had seemed all smiles, gentle, and easy to approach without any haughty air from the very beginning, would say such words. It was clear that their master was not as weak and easy to bully as she appeared on the surface.","The imperial palace was a place where people always fawned on those of higher status and stepped on those of lower status. If they wanted to live a good life, they had to climb up the ranks, and that was exactly what they all hoped for.","Following a wise master who could not be fooled was far better than serving a muddleheaded one.","\"Since this servant has chosen to follow Her Ladyship, I will naturally serve Her with all my heart and loyalty, and never have any second thoughts. Please grant us new names, Your Ladyship.\" Cuiyun spoke up first, and the rest followed suit, begging their new master to bestow names upon them.","Shen Yanshui looked at their earnest expressions, motioned for them to rise to their feet, thought for a moment, and then said with a smile, \"In that case, from now on, Cuiyun will be called Chunping, in charge of the tea, snacks, food in the rooms, and the storehouse.","The other three will be named Xia'an, Qiuru, and Dongyi respectively, and they will be responsible for all sorts of matters inside and outside the rooms.","Little Fu will be called Quanfu, in charge of the storehouse keys and all external affairs. Little Lu will be renamed Quanshou, and work under Quanfu's supervision.\"","\"For the time being, all affairs in this courtyard will be managed by Chunping.\"","\"Yes, Your Ladyship,\" all of them replied promptly.","Shen Yanshui looked at them with a soft smile. Peace in the four seasons, peace and good fortune for all — that was the greatest wish she held for herself."]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: I Wonder Where His Highness Will Be Lodged Tonight","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui took in every change in the expressions of those present and merely smiled, not taking it to heart.","She was only a Shaoxun of the Crown Prince. Even if she entered the palace, she would not be allowed to bring along the maid who had served her since childhood.","Fortunately, before entering the palace, she had already managed to claw back from her legal mother part of the dowry that had originally been prepared for her.","Even without the Crown Prince’s favor, that fairly substantial sum of money should be enough to ensure she lived comfortably without worrying about food or drink.","After all, there were very few people in this world who could bring themselves to turn down money.","“Chunping, bring me writing materials.”","“Yes.”","Chunping moved swiftly and soon had an entire set of brushes, ink, paper, and inkstone laid out. It was clear that she knew the placement of everything in the room by heart.","Shen Yanshui turned to Quanfu and smiled. “Can you write?”","“Replying to Your Ladyship, I can write a little. It’s just that my handwriting is rather crude, and I fear it may offend your eyes.”","Shen Yanshui felt half her worries ease at once. After having him write a few characters for her to inspect, she realized he had been far too modest. He was well beyond merely being able to read and write.","After questioning him carefully, she learned that Quanfu had acquired his literacy because he had taken an old eunuch who had worked in the Zhaowen Library for over a decade as his adoptive father.","The reason he was now serving in the Eastern Palace was that his adoptive father had fallen ill some time ago. Thinking he might not have much time left, the old eunuch had asked Quanfu what he wanted to do and then called in a favor to have him assigned to work in the Eastern Palace.","Shen Yanshui understood.","She then instructed him to register and inventory everything in the room. Turning to Chunping, she said, “First, follow Quanfu and learn to read. The two of you will manage the storeroom together. From now on, whenever anything enters or leaves the storeroom, both of you must count and verify it, then sign for it.”","She did not expect there to be anything particularly valuable. At present, her most precious possessions were the two thousand taels in banknotes hidden on her person, along with some loose silver for daily expenses.","Still, some rules had to be established from the beginning.","The two of them hurriedly agreed. After Quanfu withdrew, Chunping brought over a cup of hot tea and asked respectfully, “My lady, shall I send someone to the kitchens to bring our meal?”","The wealthy and influential households of the Great Yong Dynasty generally ate three meals a day. The palace kitchens, however, operated according to set hours. One could not simply eat whenever one pleased unless one was willing to pay extra.","Shen Yanshui raised a hand and pushed open the window behind her. Daylight poured in, and the spring sunshine enveloped her, warming her from head to toe and making her feel somewhat languid.","She glanced at the sky outside and realized she was getting hungry. “Go and order the meal. Oh, and have them bring plenty of meat. Something sour and spicy to stimulate the appetite—not anything too bland. If it isn’t included in my allotted provisions, pay for it separately.”","Once she had eaten, she could look around the entire courtyard, take a walk to aid digestion, and then go to sleep. It was a perfect plan.","She was in the middle of imagining it when she noticed Chunping gazing at her with an expression that clearly said she wanted to speak but hesitated.","“What is it?”","Chunping bowed uncertainly. “Replying to Your Ladyship, today is the first day the new consorts have entered the Eastern Palace. If you eat something overly sour and spicy, and His Highness the Crown Prince happens to come by, you might lose some propriety in his presence...”","Not only did the palace maids and eunuchs serving their masters have to keep their clothes neat and ensure they had no unpleasant odors that might offend the noble masters and mistresses, but the consorts and lesser ladies of each palace also had to make sure they carried no strong or disagreeable scents whenever they were required to attend someone.","Shen Yanshui smiled. “There’s no need to worry. Everyone says His Highness the Crown Prince is exceptionally proper and attaches great importance to rules. I have two women ranked above me, after all. It won’t be my turn today.”","Not to mention her relationship with her elder legitimate sister.","She had heard that the Crown Prince’s maternal uncle, the General of Agile Cavalry, had recently clashed repeatedly with the civil officials at court. She guessed the Crown Prince’s mood had been poor lately. It would be best if he did not come.","After hearing this, Chunping thought it made sense and said no more. She went outside to give the orders. However, when instructing Dongyi, she paused to think, then added a few more reminders before finally handing her the money and telling her to collect the meal from the Eastern Palace kitchens together with Quanshou.","*","“Your Highness, it is already the hour of the Monkey. Shall I have the evening meal brought in?”","The cautious yet earnest voice of Zheng Yuande sounded outside the study of the Dunben Hall.","The doors and windows of the study were tightly shut, leaving the room somewhat dim.","A tall man with a straight back and refined, gentle features sat alone behind a rosewood desk, his face expressionless.","He wore a white jade crown and a dark robe with wide sleeves and a round collar, embroidered with subtle silver patterns. A leather belt encircled his waist. His features were scholarly and elegant, yet an aura of noble severity radiated from him, making anyone who looked at him feel intimidated.","“No need.” Cui Yu’s voice was calm as he lowered his eyes to the book before him.","Outside the study, Zheng Yuande was frantic with worry. He stamped his feet in agitation.","“Oh, how can that do, Your Highness? You haven’t eaten properly all day. I beg you, please have at least a little food. What will happen if you make yourself ill from hunger?","“If Her Majesty the Empress finds out, she certainly won’t let this servant off. Your Highness, please take pity on this servant and save me...”","Zheng Yuande’s voice carried a distinctly tearful note, making him sound especially pitiful.","“Too noisy.” Cui Yu furrowed his brows in annoyance.","Zheng Yuande immediately raised his chubby hands to cover his mouth, not daring to say another word.","Yet inwardly, he let out a heavy sigh. He knew His Highness was troubled because of His Majesty’s reprimand of the General of Agile Cavalry, which had ruined his appetite.","But no matter what the matter was, His Highness still had to eat at regular hours. How could this continue?","Just as he was worrying over it, his eyes suddenly lit up. He looked at the person approaching with undisguised anticipation.","“Miss Hongling, what brings you here? Has Her Highness the Crown Princess sent you to invite His Highness to dine with her?”","Hongling gave him a courteous curtsy and smiled. “Greetings, Eunuch Yuande. Her Highness has sent this servant to invite His Highness the Crown Prince to the Xifang Hall for dinner. She has something to discuss with him.”","Upon hearing this, Zheng Yuande smiled so broadly that his teeth nearly disappeared from view. He immediately went into the study to report to His Highness.","In the Xifang Hall, dishes were being arranged in an orderly fashion.","The Crown Princess asked, “Has the rain-before-the-grain Longjing His Highness prefers been brewed?”","“Replying to Your Highness, this servant prepared it some time ago.”","As soon as she finished speaking, the Crown Princess heard the familiar sounds announcing the Crown Prince’s arrival.","First came a series of quick, light footsteps. Only afterward did the steady, unhurried sound of his stride reach them.","The Crown Princess watched the tall, straight figure approaching her, as elegant as green bamboo, his features refined and scholarly. Pressing her lips into a smile, she stepped forward and curtsied.","“Your Highness, I pay my respects.”","Cui Yu’s expression remained tranquil. He raised a hand and gave a token gesture of support. “There is no need for formalities.” His deep, even voice revealed none of his emotions.","Seeing his calm, impassive face, the Crown Princess could not help feeling disappointed.","She naturally took the seat beside him. Cui Yu then turned his head toward her and asked, “Crown Princess, what was it you wished to discuss?”","At his courteous yet distant form of address, the smile on the Crown Princess’s face stiffened almost imperceptibly. It lasted only a moment before she returned to normal.","After three years, she had long since realized that although the Crown Prince possessed exceptionally refined and handsome features, he was truly cold and taciturn by nature.","He was not like this only with her; he treated the other women of the Eastern Palace the same way.","Even so, she had never been able to rid herself of a trace of unwillingness.","He was the Crown Prince, the heir to the empire, but he was also her husband. Why couldn’t he be a little more gentle and considerate with her?","Yet her expression remained composed and gracious. With a smile, she said softly, “There’s no need to hurry. The eunuch in charge of the kitchen told me that Your Highness hasn’t summoned a meal all day, and I was worried about your health. Why don’t you eat something first?”","At that, Cui Yu nodded.","Zheng Yuande, who had been waiting nearby, finally let out a sigh of relief when he saw the Crown Prince pick up his chopsticks.","It wasn’t long, however, before the Crown Prince put down his bowl and chopsticks after eating only a few mouthfuls and half a bowl of chicken congee.","Zheng Yuande: “...”","That wasn’t even enough to count as the two bites His Highness usually ate.","Seeing this, the Crown Princess promptly set down her chopsticks as well. Cui Yu glanced at her. “I had some pastries in the study earlier, so I’m not hungry now. You needn’t worry about me.”","The Crown Princess dabbed at the corner of her mouth and smiled. “Thank you for your consideration, Your Highness. I’m already full as well.”","Cui Yu glanced at her but said nothing more.","After rinsing their mouths, the two of them took their seats on a luohan couch in the eastern warm chamber, with a rosewood tea table between them. The Crown Princess personally brewed a cup of tea. Her fingers were long and slender, and her nails were painted in layers of dazzling crimson.","“This is the pre-Qingming Longjing tea newly delivered by the Imperial Food Bureau this year. Would Your Highness care to try it?”","Cui Yu raised his hand and accepted the cup. After taking a small sip, he said, “Not bad.”","The Crown Princess smiled. “I’m glad Your Highness likes it.”","Just then, Qinghe came to report that the young prince had awakened and was fussing to see the Crown Princess.","The Crown Princess turned toward the Crown Prince and said with a smile, “Quickly, bring Zhang’er here.”","Before long, Qinghe entered with the wet nurse, who was carrying the young prince.","After paying their respects, the wet nurse did not dare raise her head. With the utmost deference, she handed the child to the Crown Princess, who had reached out to take him.","The Crown Princess held the child and chatted merrily as she teased him for the Crown Prince to see.","This was Cui Yu’s only son, as well as his eldest legitimate son, so naturally Cui Yu valued him greatly. At the sight of the child before him, his expression softened unconsciously.","The boy was only a little over two by traditional reckoning, and he had been frail and frequently ill since birth. Even now, one glance was enough to tell that he was thin and not particularly robust.","He still looked as though he had only just awakened, and Cui Yu’s brows instinctively drew together.","After watching him for a while, he asked about the child’s health in recent days.","The Crown Princess handed the child back to the wet nurse, then replied with a loving smile, “Your Highness needn’t worry. With Physician Zhang attending to him, Zhang’er’s health has already improved considerably. He will certainly grow up safe and healthy.”","The slight furrow between Cui Yu’s brows eased.","Seeing this, the Crown Princess smiled again and told him a few amusing stories about the child’s recent antics. However, the Crown Prince merely listened without saying anything further, and the smile at the corners of her lips gradually faltered. Her fingers tightened around the silk handkerchief hidden in her sleeve.","After a moment, she changed the subject. “I specifically invited Your Highness here today to discuss the matter of the palace women newly bestowed by Imperial Father.”","Cui Yu raised his eyes to look at her.","The Crown Princess continued, “All four younger sisters were personally inspected and approved by Imperial Father, and they have now all been settled in their residences.”","“Lady Zhang has been placed in the main hall of Bamboo Fragrance Residence, while Lady Wu has been assigned to the main hall of Begonia Courtyard.”","After saying this, the Crown Princess asked with a smile, “May I ask where Your Highness intends to spend the night?”","Cui Yu set down the teacup in his hand and turned to look at her. His voice was calm and emotionless. “There are four of them, are there not? What of the other two?”","The Crown Princess was slightly taken aback. Looking at his expression, she smiled and replied gently, “The other one, Lady Shen, is the daughter of the Duke of Loyalty and Righteousness. She has been placed together with Lady Liu in the eastern and western side chambers of Lotus Heart Court.”","The Crown Prince suddenly asked, “What does the Crown Princess think of... Lady Shen?”","His abrupt question left the Crown Princess stunned for a moment. Then, without meaning to, she recalled Lady Shen’s beautiful face—one so unforgettable that anyone who saw it would have difficulty looking away.","She frowned instinctively. Had the Crown Prince met Lady Shen? Otherwise, why would he suddenly bring her up?","After a pause, she replied with a smile, “Lady Shen comes from a family of nobility. Her father and brothers are all military men, and she is a daughter born of a concubine, so the rules in her family were inevitably somewhat lax. Although she has learned some proper etiquette since entering the palace, it has only been a short while, and there are still shortcomings in her words and behavior.”","“I was thinking of disciplining her a little before allowing her to attend upon Your Highness.”","Cui Yu’s brows drew together almost imperceptibly. His cold phoenix eyes swept over her. A moment later, he rose calmly and said, “There’s no need. Lady Shen will do.”"]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: First Encounter","paragraphs":["Zheng Yuande: ...... Doesn't the Crown Princess pay any attention to the recent court affairs at all?","The corners of his mouth twitched a few times as he listened to the Crown Princess chatting and laughing with the Crown Prince as if no one else was around.","The atmosphere had been perfectly pleasant just a moment ago, but the Crown Princess had truly, of her own accord, poured oil straight onto the fire for His Highness.","The General of Agile Cavalry, the Crown Prince's young maternal uncle, had been back in the capital for three months, and during that time, those idle, overfed civil officials would seize any chance they got to submit a memorial accusing him of some offense.","That would have been bad enough on its own.","A few days prior, it was the old man from the Privy Council who had first rudely bumped into the General of Agile Cavalry, then even made outrageous, disrespectful remarks about the General, which led the General to beat him.","But the end result was that the General was impeached by the civil officials and imperial censors, and in the end, His Majesty reprimanded and admonished him, even stripping the General of his post as the military governor of Zhenguo Army!","The Crown Prince had stood up to speak in the General's defense, and for that, he had been reprimanded by His Majesty twice in the past few days.","Right now, the Crown Prince probably could not bear to hear anything about the divide between civil and military officials.","But in the Great Yong Dynasty, the tradition of valuing civil officials over military officials had long been so deeply rooted that it had become second nature to everyone in the court and the commonalty, even ordinary civilians.","If civil and military officials happened to cross paths on the road, even a military officer of higher rank would have to make way for a civil official who was one or two grades lower than them. This had already become an established unwritten rule.","But the Crown Prince and the General of Agile Cavalry were only five years apart in age, and the two had shared a deep, close bond since childhood.","When the Crown Princess heard that the Crown Prince was planning to go to Lady Shen's courtyard, she froze for a split second, and a twinge of jealousy rose unconsciously in her heart.","Yet she still smiled with dignified grace and said, \"Your Highness, Lady Shen does not understand proper etiquette as well as the several talented ladies who come from scholarly families. I am afraid she might end up offending you...\"","The Crown Prince suddenly cut in, \"Does not understand proper etiquette?\" His tone was slightly heavy, the thin, sharp corners of his eyes drooped slightly, and his dark, pitch-black eyes revealed no emotion at all.","The Crown Princess was slightly stunned, and before she could react, she saw that he had already stood up, said that there were still matters to attend to in the front hall, and left.","His expression looked no different from his usual one.","It made her unable to help but wonder... if that glance he had given her just now had only been her imagination.","She rose to curtsy, \"I see Your Highness off, Your Highness.\"","Matron Zhou, who was standing at her side waiting for the others to leave, then whispered, \"Your Highness, this old servant has heard that the entire front court has been in an uproar over the recent incident where the General of Agile Cavalry beat a court official in the street. The Crown Prince is likely in a bad mood because of this matter.\"","The Crown Princess knitted her brows in dissatisfaction. \"Military generals with high merit that overshadow the sovereign are bound to make His Majesty, the Emperor, wary. His Highness's uncle is so undisciplined, does not know how to behave low-key, and keeps causing trouble for His Highness everywhere. Why doesn't the old Duke Fengguo and the old matriarch of the Fengguo Manor discipline him...\"","Matron Zhou sighed and said, \"The old Duke Fengguo now only has the Duke Fengguo, who is disabled in both legs, and this youngest son, who is in good health. He was born when the old Duke was already advanced in age, so it is only natural that he is too reluctant to discipline him strictly.","\"This old servant thinks... perhaps it is because the General of Agile Cavalry has not yet taken a wife and started a family, that he remains so unstable in his actions at his age.\"","The Crown Princess pursed her lips, frowned and thought for a moment, then said, \"What Matron said makes sense. I should speak to the Empress later, and ask her to persuade His Highness's uncle to get married as soon as possible.\"","But as a younger generation, arranging a marriage for an elder would, after all, look rather inappropriate.","She would have to send a message to her own mother, and let her mother find an opportunity to bring it up to the Empress.","Seeing that she still looked deeply troubled, Matron Zhou comforted her, \"Your Highness, there is no need to worry. You already have the little imperial grandson under your protection. No matter which courtyard the Crown Prince visits, no matter which person in the rear palace gains His favor, no one's favor can ever shake your position. We only need to sit back and watch the drama unfold with peace of mind.\"","The Crown Princess knitted her brows, her heart still filled with displeasure, but as the Crown Princess, His Highness currently only had one son and one daughter under his knees, and the imperial descendants were far too few. She could not monopolize the Crown Prince all to herself...","Otherwise, the voices from outside calling her jealous would be enough to drown her out.","Worse still, she had to maintain the demeanor of a virtuous, magnanimous Crown Princess to build an even better reputation for herself.","She could only force the unwillingness in her heart down by telling herself that even when the Crown Prince went to other people's courtyards, he would still keep his usual cold, distant manner, and would never treat anyone with any special favor.","*","The clouds merged like a jade disc, the sunlight faded away, and the night sky was dotted with tiny stars.","Zheng Yuande saw that the time was just about right, so he stepped forward softly and whispered, \"Your Highness, it is almost time to light the palace lanterns. Which courtyard does Your Highness plan to stay for the night tonight?\"","Although the Crown Prince had said in front of the Crown Princess earlier that he was going to Lady Shen's place, he still asked one more cautious question, not daring to make the decision on his own.","Cui Yu frowned slightly, closed the book he was holding, stood up, brushed the dust off his sleeves, and said in a deep, solemn voice, \"Let's go.\"","\"Understood, Your Highness.\" Zheng Yuande quickly lifted the palace lantern and led the way ahead.","*","\"Master, here are the golden crispy chicken, peach blossom pastries, and donkey-hide gelatin silver ear milk drink you asked for.\" Chunping took the food box from Quanshou, quickly walked around the folding screen, and entered the eastern warm pavilion.","Shen Yanshui had long been sitting at the round table waiting eagerly. Now, seeing Chunping walk in, her pair of peach blossom eyes sparkled, almost glowing as they fixed on the food box in her hand.","\"Hurry up and set them all out.\" She had never expected that the diet kitchen in the Eastern Palace could make such delicious food, far better than the food she had eaten in the Xiuzhen Palace back then, and even better than the food the chefs in her father's marquis manor made.","Now that she had tasted such wonderful food, how could she ever go back to the old way?","At Shenshi, around 4 p.m., she had eaten a wonderful late meal, including spicy shrimp and jade thick soup, crispy deep-fried pork, and wine-steamed lamb slices, which had made her feel so happy she almost floated off the ground.","With cooking skills like this, she could stay in the Eastern Palace for a hundred years without ever wanting to leave!","The only drawback was that it cost a little more silver, but other than that, it was absolutely perfect.","It was almost the time of Xu, a little after 8 p.m., the perfect hour for a midnight snack.","In the west side hall opposite, Lady Liu, who had dressed up elaborately and was sitting restlessly, heard the movement from across the courtyard and could not help asking, Yinping, what is going on outside? Could it be that the Crown Prince has arrived?","Deep down, she knew very well that the Crown Prince would most likely not visit her place today, but what if he did?","A tiny sliver of hope lingered in her heart, so much so that she could barely bring herself to take a few bites of her dinner.","Yinping knew very well that if the Crown Prince had arrived, the noise would not be what they had just heard, but she still obeyed her mistress's order to go outside and take a look. She then came back to report, \"Mistress, according to Yinye, the people in the courtyard opposite just sent someone to the diet kitchen to fetch a midnight snack, and it has just been brought in.\"","Lady Liu could not believe her ears. \"A midnight snack?\"","\"How can she even have an appetite for a midnight snack at this hour?\" As she spoke, she curled her lip slightly, thinking to herself that as expected, someone from a military family would have no proper manners and be completely unrefined.","Did she know full well that His Highness would not visit her place tonight? So she had just given up on herself and stopped caring about appearances?","She quickly pushed those thoughts aside, but still could not resist urging her servants to send someone to keep watch outside the courtyard.","*","The moment the Crown Prince stepped onto the corridor in front of the back cover house, the hearts of all the mistresses in every courtyard and room in the rear palace instantly lifted.","Among all of them, Lady Zhang and Lady Wu were the most nervous.","Everyone knew that the Crown Prince was always extremely strict with etiquette and abided by the rules. Logically speaking, his first night after arriving at the rear palace should have been spent in Lady Zhang's courtyard.","Lady Wu, Wu Chenghui, had always been proud of her own beauty, and today, after receiving praise from the Crown Princess, she was at the height of her elation and arrogance, with no intention of thinking otherwise. When she learned that the Crown Prince was heading in the direction of her courtyard, she was instantly filled with both surprise and smug delight. She hurriedly leaned over her dressing mirror to check if there was anything amiss with her face and attire, all the while urging her servants, \"Come, let us go wait for the Crown Prince at the courtyard gate.\"","\"Understood!\" The servants waiting on her were also rarely excited. If their mistress won the Crown Prince's favor tonight, they would gain a fair amount of prestige moving about the Eastern Palace from then on.","But just moments after stepping out, before Lady Wu could even reach the gate, the maid who had been brimming with excitement earlier came hurrying back with a pale, troubled look on her face. Facing her mistress, who was already dressed in ornate, lavish attire, the maid spoke carefully, stammering a little, \"Mistress... the Crown Prince has entered... the adjacent Lotus Heart Courtyard.\"","The bright smile that had been on Lady Wu's face instantly vanished, her expression darkening completely.","*","Shen Yanshui was just savoring a mouthful of sweet, rich donkey-hide gelatin and silver fungus milk beverage when she heard the commotion outside the courtyard. When Chunping came rushing in almost tripping over her own feet to report that the Crown Prince had already arrived at the courtyard entrance, and with the sound of successive greetings of respect rising from every other courtyard, Shen Yanshui nearly choked on her sip of milk.","There was no time to tidy things up. She took a deep breath and hurried to the gate, where she could faintly make out the tall, broad-shouldered, long-legged figure of a man walking toward her at an unhurried pace, surrounded by eunuchs standing bowed on both sides. She did not even have time to lift her head to get a clear look at the newcomer's face before she hurriedly curtsied in greeting.","\"This humble wife Shen greets the Crown Prince. May Your Highness enjoy peace and good health.\" She was uncharacteristically a little nervous.","Her entire attention was fixed on the person standing only two steps away from her. By the glow of the candlelight spilling out from the room, she could even make out the patterns on the dark black leather belt at his waist, as well as the shimmering silver threads woven into his purple robe that caught the light.","Wait, what was the Crown Prince doing here? Hadn't everyone said the Crown Prince was the most strict observer of rules? Why had he come to her courtyard of all places?","Zheng Yuande could not help but think that this Lady Shen really was a free, unconstrained spirit! Not only had she not been waiting at the gate early to welcome the Crown Prince as others did, she had only hurried out to offer her greeting right as His Highness was about to step through the door.","Zheng Yuande glanced at her, and it was obvious she had not even finished dressing properly.","By all proper etiquette, even on days when the Crown Prince was not expected to visit, one should still dress neatly and wait for news of His Highness's arrangements, only extinguishing their lamps to rest once they had confirmed he would not be coming. That was the standard custom in the Eastern Palace.","Cui Yu lowered his eyes and glanced at her.","Shen Yanshui was wearing a narrow-sleeve blouse of pale lotus root pink plain silk, over which she had draped a half-sleeve gown in the color of sky-blue water. Her hair was styled in a tassel bun, tied only with a sky-blue ribbon, all other ornaments having been taken off long ago. She did not wear the heavy, elaborate makeup and lavish jewelry that the other ladies had put on.","She was as fresh as a lotus rising from clear water, unadorned and uncarved, her natural beauty shining through.","\"Rise.\"","Shen Yanshui had kept her head bowed in the greeting posture, and at the sound of his clear, steady voice, she caught a glimpse from the corner of her eye of him lifting his feet and walking past her into the room, the hem of his purple robe brushing lightly against the edge of her skirt.","She still had no idea why the Crown Prince had decided to visit her courtyard tonight, but since he was already here, after the initial shock of being caught completely off guard, she had calmed down a little.","She watched him lift the corner of his robe and settle down on the couch, and that was when she finally got a clear look at his face. Her eyes lit up instantly.","He was as handsome as a jade carving, his features as fine as a painting, his demeanor gentle and refined yet carrying an innate noble majesty. He was even more striking than she had imagined.","Cui Yu suddenly lifted his gaze to look at her. Their eyes met, and Shen Yanshui blinked those naturally charming, bright peach blossom eyes of hers, stepping forward two steps with a sincere smile as she softly explained, \"Your Highness has arrived at just the right moment. The chefs in the Changqing Palace's kitchen make such delicious food, so this humble one prepared a little late-night snack. Would Your Highness care to share it with me?\"","She spoke with a warm smile, saying what was meant to be a polite opening to ease the tension, her heart a little nervous, and a little regretful that she had only taken a few bites of the snack on the table.","Cui Yu turned his gaze to the several plates of food on the table, then noticed the way she had glanced at those dishes no less than several times in just a short moment, her little look of undisguised reluctance and craving.","He had not had any appetite to speak of at first, but seeing that obvious, endearing look on her face, he suddenly nodded in agreement.","Shen Yanshui had only meant to make conversation, to offer a gentle, respectful remark, and never expected him to actually say yes."]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: An Exploration","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui looked toward the round-faced, fair and plump eunuch standing behind him. Though he looked to be only in his twenties, he was the chief eunuch, Zheng Yuande.","There was no way she had the nerve to let the Crown Prince eat food she had already eaten.","Seeing this, Zheng Yuande was delighted and hurriedly ordered the kitchens to prepare another late-night meal that would be easy to digest.","The Crown Prince’s requested food arrived far more quickly than anything Shen Yanshui had obtained by spending her own money.","Before long, the dishes were laid out, though they were nowhere near as lavish as she had imagined. Aside from another serving of the food she had previously ordered, there was also a bowl of four-delicacy soup, a bowl of fish soup, and a bowl of chicken congee. Compared with his status, it could even be called simple.","Everything looked light and easy to digest.","She stood properly beside him, serving him food and ladling out the congee. With a smile, she said, “Your Highness, try this chicken congee. I had a bowl during dinner as well. I wonder which chef made it—it was so fragrant.”","Hearing the sincerity and delight in her voice, Cui Yu almost couldn’t help wondering whether the Eastern Palace had changed its head chef and kitchen director today.","But after tasting it, he found that it was no different from usual.","Naturally, nothing that reached his table would be poor in quality. Yet he could not sense the joy and satisfaction toward good food conveyed in her tone.","He said in a low voice, “There’s no need to stand and serve me. Sit down and eat with me.”","The moment he finished speaking, the unmistakable surprise and delight in her eyes caught his attention.","Zheng Yuande watched helplessly as Lady Shen beamed, bowed to thank His Highness, and then plopped herself down securely in her seat—she really sat down.","Shen Yanshui was indeed very happy. After all, the Crown Prince did not seem to have a bad temper, and he had not taken offense at her lack of decorum. Now he was even letting her enjoy a meal for free. How could she not be pleased?","“Mmm—so fragrant and delicious!” The moment Shen Yanshui swallowed a mouthful of fish soup, she couldn’t help widening her eyes slightly at the flavor. With a taste like this, she felt she could eat two more bowls!","Still, good food had to be shared fairly. She couldn’t neglect any of it.","After finishing a little less than half a bowl of fish soup, she had another half bowl of four-delicacy soup. The freshly prepared golden chicken couldn’t go to waste, either. As expected, food made for the Crown Prince was different—she felt even the texture of the chicken was more tender and delicious.","“Mmm!” The instant it entered her mouth, she unconsciously let out the highest praise one could give to a delicacy.","Zheng Yuande’s eyes nearly popped out of his head!","He had never seen a woman like this. The women of Changqing Palace all kept their nerves taut whenever they served His Highness. Who actually ate properly? Didn’t they all take only a couple of bites before claiming to be full?","They were afraid of making a fool of themselves in front of His Highness or leaving him with a bad impression.","He had never seen anyone eat so much—or with such relish—in the Crown Prince’s presence.","Cui Yu was rather surprised as well. He stared at her for quite some time and discovered that she was truly focused on eating.","Her pace was not slow, but her movements were not at all coarse. The satisfied, happy expression between her brows made it seem as though the food in her bowl was even more delicious than everything on the table.","When she ate the four-delicacy soup, he saw that although she finished everything in her bowl, her expression was considerably more subdued.","He lowered his eyes to the four-delicacy soup before him and suddenly felt as though it had lost all its flavor.","After finishing a piece of golden chicken, Shen Yanshui immediately reached for a second. But when she looked up, she saw that the Crown Prince beside her had stopped eating.","She became anxious at once. If he wasn’t going to eat anymore, how was she supposed to continue?","With a concerned, hopeful, and utterly sincere expression, she said, “Why aren’t you eating, Your Highness? This golden chicken is even more delicious than the piece I had earlier. I wonder how it was made—it even has a faint aroma of wine. Your Highness, you should try some too.”","Cui Yu raised his eyes to meet her earnest, expectant gaze. After pausing for a moment, he nodded.","The eunuch serving him, who had been watching his master’s expression closely, immediately picked up a piece of golden chicken and placed it in his bowl.","Seeing him start eating again, Shen Yanshui smiled at once and hurriedly took another piece of the fragrant, golden-brown chicken.","After a while, Shen Yanshui finally ate her fill. Eight-tenths full was just right. She had only just taken a bite of a peach blossom pastry no bigger than her thumb when she looked up and saw the Crown Prince beside her eating with unhurried elegance. Every one of his movements was graceful and pleasing to the eye.","Cui Yu leisurely put down his bowl and chopsticks and picked up a peach blossom pastry.","Seeing that he had eaten quite a bit as well, Shen Yanshui smiled and asked, “Your Highness, would you like to take a walk in the courtyard to aid digestion?”","“Mm.”","Cui Yu did not refuse. He had always exercised restraint, and food was no exception. But somehow, he seemed to have eaten a little too much just now.","Zheng Yuande glanced at the table and smiled broadly, having long since put everything else out of his mind. As long as His Highness was willing to eat properly, the rest did not matter.","After rinsing their mouths and washing their hands, the two of them left the eastern side hall, one following the other with a distance of about half a body between them.","Shen Yanshui looked up at the night sky. The silver moon hung high overhead, and stars glittered brightly. Moonlight spilled across the courtyard paved with bluestone, illuminating the originally dim space.","Just as she was preparing to find some topic of conversation, a deep, slightly low voice suddenly reached her ears.","“What do you usually do at home?”","Shen Yanshui glanced sideways at him. From where she stood, she could clearly see his expression. Both his voice and his manner appeared gentle and calm, yet for some reason, she felt that the Crown Prince was not in a particularly good mood.","She instinctively became more cautious and replied with a smile, “In answer to Your Highness, this concubine is rather foolish. I’ve been a little playful since childhood. Unlike my elder sister, who is skilled in music, chess, calligraphy, and painting, my needlework and embroidery are only passable. Usually, I enjoy fishing, tending flowers, swinging, playing cuju, and playing polo. Most importantly, I love eating all kinds of delicious food.”","The Crown Prince certainly knew all about her background. No matter what, if possible, she should first make it clear that she had nothing to do with her elder sister. Ideally, she would have him believe that she was not one of Noble Consort Lan’s people, nor anyone’s pawn.","She would be spending the rest of her life in the Eastern Palace. If she could improve her quality of life, naturally she ought to do so.","Chunping, following behind them at a respectful distance alongside Zheng Yuande, nearly blacked out twice in succession. Zheng Yuande, meanwhile, was first startled, then even more startled.","Chunping: Mistress, even if we can’t do anything, you can’t say that in front of the Crown Prince!","Zheng Yuande: What a perfect opportunity to be alone with His Highness. Instead of putting on a good showing, she had gone so far as to expose all her shortcomings without the slightest hesitation. He had truly never seen anyone like her...","She could at least have pretended a little! As for needlework and such, even if she herself was no good at it, didn’t she have servants who could do it for her?","How had everything simply tumbled out of her mouth the moment His Highness casually asked a question? Was she not a little dim-witted?","Cui Yu turned back to look at her. Seeing her smiling with her eyes curved into crescents, his brows shifted slightly. He had already realized that she liked to eat, but...","“You know how to play cuju and polo? Did your family hire tutors to teach you?”","Shen Yanshui smiled somewhat sheepishly and said softly, “To answer Your Highness, they weren’t tutors hired by my family. In fact, my parents always taught me that a woman should be chaste, composed, virtuous, and refined. They didn’t like me playing cuju or polo, so the instructors my family hired were all women who taught the qin, chess, calligraphy, painting, flower arranging, tea ceremony, and needlework.”","“I have some interest in playing the qin and painting, so I learned a little of both. As for the rest, I suppose I simply don’t have the talent, so I didn’t force myself to continue.”","As she spoke, her smile grew sincere. She did not seem to think there was anything wrong with not knowing those other skills.","Cui Yu studied the smile on her face and asked with a furrowed brow, “Since your parents forbade it, why did you learn them at all?”","Shen Yanshui tilted her head to look at him and answered with a perfectly natural smile, “Because I like them!”","Then, pressing her lips together in a smile, she added, “Besides, I would never go and tell them that I play cuju and polo. I play in secret. Other than my personal maidservants, no one else knows.”","Cui Yu’s brows lifted slightly. He did not seem to mind that she alternated between calling herself “this wife” and “I.”","The corners of Shen Yanshui’s beautiful, expressive eyes lifted with triumph. Her eyes seemed to reflect scattered stars, dazzling and bright.","She blinked and said, “They were the ones who said it themselves: a woman obeys her husband after marriage. Now that I belong to Your Highness, even if my parents found out, they can’t control me anymore.”","Looking at her lively, spirited face, Cui Yu unconsciously let out a soft laugh. The heavy stone that had long weighed on his heart seemed to loosen slightly.","He only wondered how long a pair of such lively, vibrant eyes would be able to exist in this palace.","His voice suddenly turned somber. “Then why tell me? Aren’t you afraid I might forbid it as well—or dislike it?”","Her heart trembled, and she was startled by the sudden change in his expression. But only for a brief moment. She soon realized that he was deliberately trying to frighten her.","For a moment, Shen Yanshui was at a loss for words. Yet when she considered that the Crown Prince was only about twenty, having just come of age, and saw that even with his face stern and solemn, he remained devastatingly handsome, her mood brightened again.","“Because Your Highness asked,” she murmured. Then, in a small voice, she asked, “Your Highness... do you dislike it?”","Cui Yu paused for a moment before suddenly asking, “If I disliked it, would you stop doing it from now on?”"]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: His Highness Has Never Been Fond of Women","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui lowered her head slightly and secretly glanced up at him, saying nothing.","One look at her crystal-clear eyes, in which every thought was laid bare, and Cui Yu could practically read everything on her mind. He couldn’t help finding it amusing.","At last, seeing that his mood seemed to have improved somewhat, Shen Yanshui said earnestly, “Your Highness, playing cuju and polo isn’t merely for amusement. It also helps strengthen the body and makes one less prone to illness. It accomplishes several things at once—what could be better?”","Cui Yu lowered his eyes to her eager expression. This time, he did not try to frighten her again. He smiled and said, “As you say, it is indeed a good thing. There is an open space in the garden of the Palace of Eternal Celebration. If you have nothing to do, you may go there and play.”","Shen Yanshui’s eyes lit up. “Thank you, Your Highness.”","Her voice was filled with such delight that even those who heard it couldn’t help feeling their own spirits lift.","Shen Yanshui was not merely happy because she would now be able to play cuju and polo openly.","It was because, through their brief exchange just now, she had discovered that the Crown Prince was not quite as she had imagined.","Compared with the Crown Prince of the rumors—strictly bound by rules, self-disciplined, respectful of propriety, and dignified to the point of severity—the man before her was indeed imposing and intimidating when expressionless, but he had not held her several lapses in etiquette against her.","Some of those lapses had been unintentional and caught her off guard, while others had come from the cautious little tests she had deliberately made afterward.","Naturally, this kind of Crown Prince pleased her far more than the one in the rumors. At the very least, her days in the Eastern Palace would not be too difficult.","However, the peculiar concern he had shown just now, both in his words and his expression, for cuju and polo suddenly reminded her of some scattered rumors about him from five years ago, before the emperor had formally made him Crown Prince...","In the Great Yong, the appointment of a crown prince followed ancestral custom: if there was a son born to the empress, he was to be made crown prince; if there was no such son, the eldest son would be chosen.","The current emperor, Emperor Pingyuan, had many children, but the empress had only one son among them—the third prince.","Because the third prince had been born with a congenital weakness and had often fallen ill as a child, there had been concerns that he would be unable to shoulder the responsibility of becoming the heir to the empire. Thus, he had not been made crown prince at the time.","It was only after the empress sent the young third prince to be raised for several years at her maternal family’s residence, the Duke Fengguo’s estate, that his health gradually improved.","The Duke Fengguo’s family had been hereditary nobles and military commanders for generations. By the time the third prince was a teenager, after spending several years at their residence, his martial skills had already become quite impressive. At fourteen, during a hunt at the Western Hills, he had outshone all the sons of the noble military families and single-handedly hunted a bear, winning first place.","For a time, his fame was unrivaled.","Yet it was said that because of this, the third prince had instead been harshly reprimanded and punished by Emperor Pingyuan.","As for cuju, polo, and the like, those were merely games he had long since mastered. Otherwise, she would never have dared bring them up so casually.","After he was made Crown Prince at the age of fifteen, however, the Crown Prince spoken of by those around him grew more and more composed and measured with each passing year. Several years had gone by, and she had nearly forgotten those old rumors about him in the capital.","A cool breeze swept past, and Shen Yanshui shivered instinctively.","Cui Yu reached out and took her hand. “It is getting late. Go back and rest.”","Shen Yanshui froze for a moment. Her hand, which had been somewhat chilled, was now completely enclosed in his broad, warm palm. Taking advantage of the situation, she moved closer and pressed herself tightly against his arm. The next moment, she clearly felt his arm tense for an instant, as though on instinct.","She lifted her head and blinked at him as if nothing had happened. “Your Highness, it’s warmer this way.”","Cui Yu: “...”","He raised his eyes and glanced around. Night had already fallen, and they were within his own palace. With the evening dew growing heavier, he ultimately said nothing.","Walking behind them, Zheng Yuande clicked his tongue softly.","So the Crown Prince liked this sort of empty-headed girl?","Could Lady Shen really be one of those fools blessed by sheer luck?","Just look at her background. She was already a source of considerable trouble. Noble Consort Lan and the fourth prince were both eager to pull their Crown Prince down and seize his position for themselves.","Lady Shen’s elder sister had lived in Noble Consort Lan’s Palace of Abundant Blessings ever since entering the palace. Though she was only a minor figure, she was still one of Noble Consort Lan’s people.","Wasn’t this move nothing more than an obvious attempt to disgust the Eastern Palace—a clear effort to plant a pawn there? Yet it had been approved by His Majesty himself, so the Eastern Palace could not do anything to her.","At least for the time being, the Eastern Palace could not show any dissatisfaction openly. Otherwise, Noble Consort Lan’s faction would surely stir up trouble before His Majesty again.","Even so, barring any unexpected turn of events, Lady Shen was destined to spend her entire life without favor, growing old alone.","And yet, the Crown Princess had inadvertently struck a tender spot in the Crown Prince’s heart. The Crown Prince had ignored the courtyards of the two higher-ranking ladies from distinguished families and had instead come to the residence of Lady Shen, the daughter of a noble military family.","If that wasn’t a fool’s good fortune, what was?","Shen Yanshui had no idea that others now regarded her as a fool.","After bathing and changing, she walked around the carved rosewood screen depicting lakes and mountains. To her surprise, she found that the Crown Prince was already lying on the bed with his eyes closed.","She muttered instinctively, “He fell asleep rather quickly.”","According to the rules, she should have bathed and dressed herself early, then waited in exquisite makeup for the Crown Prince’s summons. When it came time to attend him, there was no reason for a mere concubine like her to make the Crown Prince wait.","It was just that tonight had not gone according to plan.","Seeing Chunping’s anxious expression, she waved her hand and dismissed everyone. Zheng Yuande, meanwhile, had withdrawn with great tact as soon as she came out and had ordered people to prepare hot water.","Quanfu, who had been waiting respectfully with his back bent, immediately went downstairs to make the arrangements. Then, smiling obsequiously, he said in a low voice to Zheng Yuande, “Eunuch Zheng, you’ve been working hard all day as well. I’ll wait here, so why don’t you go to the tea room and rest your feet over a cup of hot tea? If His Highness needs anything, I’ll send someone to call you.”","Zheng Yuande cast him a sidelong glance. “You seem fairly quick on the uptake. In that case, this household will go rest for a while. Make sure you all keep your eyes open and be careful.”","Quanshou, who had been standing nearby, immediately bent forward and came over with a broad smile to lead the way.","Only then did Zheng Yuande’s face relax into a smile. He nodded in satisfaction.","There were plenty of people who wanted to rack their brains to curry favor with him in his position. He was not afraid of those who eagerly rushed to flatter him. What he feared were people without sense, whose eyes were fixed only on ingratiating themselves with him while forgetting who their true master was.","In Lady Shen’s residence, the maid named Chunping appeared reasonably steady. That round-faced young eunuch, on the other hand, knew how to handle people and had a sweet tongue. Yet he did not seem like the sort of shortsighted person who cared only about his own interests. Otherwise, the one he had led to the tea room would have been himself.","Inside the room, Shen Yanshui slipped forward in her soft-soled embroidered slippers. She craned her neck to look at him, finding him with his eyes closed, apparently already asleep. Unable to resist, she studied him carefully for a few moments.","His brows and eyes were deep-set, and his lashes were very long. With his eyes closed, they resembled two little fans. Looking at them made her fingertips itch, as though she wanted to reach out and touch them.","She had noticed from the side earlier that the line of his jaw was sharp yet smooth and graceful. She hadn’t expected him to look so handsome even while lying down.","Most importantly, the color and shape of his lips were beautiful too...","Cui Yu was not asleep, he was just resting his eyes in quiet repose. Just as he was about to open them, he keenly caught the sight of her gaze, which had suddenly frozen on his face. Thinking of her status, he held still for a moment.","Then... his brows drew together.","He opened his eyes abruptly, looking right at her pair of eyes that had widened in a flash, his own gaze momentarily confused, even at a loss for words.","\"What were you... doing just now?\"","Shen Yanshui withdrew the finger that had been brushing his eyelid as if nothing had happened, then kicked off her shoes, climbed onto the bed and tucked herself under the covers in one smooth motion.","Cui Yu turned over to face her, his voice slightly low and heavy. \"Speak.\"","Shen Yanshui half-hid her face under the quilt, her voice muffled and halting with obvious embarrassment. \"I thought Your Highness was already asleep, I had no idea you were still awake...\"","With his sharp, dark eyes fixed on her from such close distance, Shen Yanshui began to feel rather pressured. Sure enough, a man was far more pleasant to look at when his eyes were closed.","\"Your Highness, has anyone ever told you that you are exceptionally good-looking?\"","Seeing him frown, she tugged the quilt down a little at once, her tone utterly sincere, her eyes shining bright as she looked at him. \"I mean it truly. Just now I was looking at you, and suddenly thought the Crown Prince is so handsome, every part of you is perfect, even your eyelashes are so thick, long and curly... I have no idea what came over my finger, it seemed to have a mind of its own...\"","\"...\" Cui Yu stared at her pleading, fawning gaze, listening to this unblushing, unreserved compliment that left him stunned for a split second.","As the empress's own son, he had heard endless streams of praise around him growing up, but never anything as straightforward and unmasked as hers.","He was the Crown Prince of Great Yong, every word and action of his was watched by all in the court and beyond. No one ever paid attention to his looks, and even if they did, no one would ever dare say such a thing to his face.","Held by her unhidden, candid gaze, he turned back and lay down.","Just as Shen Yanshui let out a quiet sigh of relief, thinking the matter was over, a tall, strong, lean figure suddenly loomed over her.","Shen Yanshui: \"???\" This is so sudden!","The first time, Shen Yanshui played the part of the shy new consort, making no movements of her own, strictly following the rules the palace matrons had taught her. After all, according to palace regulations, leaving any marks on the Crown Prince's body was a serious offense that harmed his noble person.","When it ended, it had seemed a little... brief. Wait? She froze all at once. That just now... was that a special ability?!","Her heart skipped a beat, but when she tried to sense that faint strange feeling again, it vanished completely without a trace.","Cui Yu noticed that she had drifted off into a trance, and frowned in displeasure...","\"Ah...\" Shen Yanshui yelped out in surprise when his actions caught her off guard, and her thoughts were pulled back entirely to the present.","The second time, she dropped her act halfway, deciding it was time to try something different. After all... this man's skills in bed were really far from ideal.","This was supposed to be something that brought pleasure to both people, and she had no intention of suffering through it all by herself for the rest of her days.","She stretched out her arms, wrapping them softly around his shoulders, and felt his whole body go taut at once. Her palms could clearly feel the defined, firm muscles under his skin.","In the dim moonlight, she could make out the outline of his lean, strong form, not perfectly clear, but the real, solid touch under her hands told her without a doubt that his body was more perfect than any she had ever seen before.","She whispered two soft sentences right by his ear.","Cui Yu: \"...Mm.\"","Hearing his cool, reserved voice, Shen Yanshui had originally planned to take it slow that night, and make gradual adjustments later. After all, even though the palace matrons would instruct young ladies selected for the imperial harem on matters of the bed, it would be rather improper for an unmarried girl to know too much about them.","But to her surprise, he stopped relying entirely on brute force and reckless, clumsy movements right after that, and instead kept his eyes fixed intently on her face.","She responded to him tentatively.","Soon she realized he was carefully watching her reactions, and this small discovery made her feel quite happy.","Judging by Cui Yu's temperament as he had shown so far, he was by and large a rather tolerant man.","Her mind wandered off for a brief moment, only to be pulled apart by his movements, and she sank fully into the moment.","That night, to Cui Yu's own surprise, he called for water to be brought in twice.","For Zheng Yuande, the incident was nothing short of earth-shattering!","His master had never been one to favor sensual pleasures, one round of such activities at most was already the norm. This was the very first time His Highness had called for water twice in one night.","This Lady Shen is truly no ordinary woman!"]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: Golden-edge Daphne","paragraphs":["Early the next morning, at the first pale glimmer of dawn, Shen Yanshui was still deep in sleep when someone gently roused her.","Her eyes would barely open. Buried beneath the covers, she struggled to pry them open a sliver and saw a faint, hazy light filtering through the bed curtains. In a hoarse, drowsy voice, she asked, “What time is it?”","Chunping answered with a smile, “My lady, it is now three-quarters into the Hour of the Rabbit. It is time to pay our respects to the Crown Princess.”","Shen Yanshui grew a little more alert at that, though her body still did not feel quite well. Thinking of how the Crown Prince had risen at three-quarters into the Hour of the Tiger—just after four in the morning—she could not help but admire him.","Getting up so early every day, attending court, hearing matters of state... Hm?","Wait.","She suddenly jolted upright!","That familiar sensation within her body... could this be... her ability?!","She immediately dismissed everyone from the room, then, almost unable to wait, examined the strange energy that seemed to have suddenly appeared inside her.","It was real. It was not her imagination...","Opening her eyes again, she reached for a branch of half-bloomed peach blossoms from the white porcelain vase on the small table beside her bed and activated her ability.","In mere moments, the buds on the peach branch burst fully into bloom.","Shen Yanshui was overjoyed.","But what was going on? Why had her ability shown no sign of returning for more than ten years, only to suddenly reappear today?","The greatest difference from before was... she had slept with the Crown Prince?","“My lady, it is nearly time. We must not delay any longer,” Chunping reminded her softly from outside.","Shen Yanshui placed the branch back into the vase and called for the attendants to come in.","Whatever the reason, the return of her ability was unquestionably wonderful news.","Xia'an stepped quietly into the inner chamber, bowed, and raised a copper basin of warm water above her head with both hands, waiting for her mistress to rise and wash.","After Shen Yanshui had gotten up and finished washing, she glanced at the brightly colored garments prepared nearby—pomegranate red and begonia pink—and said, “Bring me the lotus-pink one. Put my hair in a small round bun, and the pearl moon crown will do.”","Xia'an, waiting at the side, hesitated for a moment before asking quietly, “My lady, would the lotus-pink one be a little too plain?”","Qiuhe murmured her acknowledgment and began carefully arranging her mistress’s hair and makeup.","Shen Yanshui smiled at Xia'an’s words. “A little plain is exactly right. Do as I said.”","“Yes, my lady,” Xia'an replied.","When it came to clothing and adornment, Shen Yanshui’s preference was simply to remain moderate. She could not dress too plainly or too modestly, lest others take her for timid and easy to bully; but neither could she stand out too much and attract unwanted attention. The fewer troubles she invited, the better.","In Great Yong, married women wore all their hair pinned up in an assortment of styles. The round bun was one of the more common ones.","Common women decorated their buns with ribbons and hairpins, while among noblewomen, ornate floral crowns had become fashionable in recent years. The pearl moon crown was one such style.","The April morning sky was still gray and dim, with a faint chill in the air. Before leaving, Shen Yanshui draped a cloak over her shoulders. The moment she stepped outside, she saw Lady Liu already waiting in the courtyard, dressed rather lightly, her slender figure appearing all the more graceful for it.","“Greetings, Sister Shen.” Lady Liu was dressed rather thinly, her lips trembling slightly from the cold. Seeing Shen Yanshui’s rosy cheeks and radiant complexion, she could not help but feel a touch of envy.","Just looking at Lady Liu made Shen Yanshui feel cold. Although, after gaining her ability, she would likely become impervious to heat and cold, the habits she had formed over so many years were not so easily changed.","“No need for such formality. Lady Liu, you should put on more layers, lest you catch a chill.”","Lady Liu tugged at the corner of her lips in a smile. “Thank you for your concern, Sister Shen, but I am not cold.”","Seeing this, Shen Yanshui said no more. She set out from Lotus Heart Court with Chunping, while Lady Liu was accompanied by a palace maid of her own. The four of them had just left the courtyard when they looked up to see another group of four approaching from the opposite end of the passageway. The two parties happened to meet before Moonlight Gate.","Shen Yanshui was the first to offer a salute, saying with a smile, “Greetings, Lady Zhang.” Lady Liu at her side and Lady Zhao, who stood beside Lady Zhang, likewise curtsied in greeting.","Lady Zhang wore a moon-white cross-collared blouse, paired with a fragrant-consort-pink pleated skirt embroidered with plum blossoms. Over it, she had draped a sky-blue, wide-sleeved open-front robe. Her hair was arranged in a single spiral bun, adorned with a white-jade plum blossom hairpin, a look that suited her refined and scholarly air perfectly.","Only her makeup seemed somewhat heavy; her complexion had been powdered a little too white.","“Lady Shen, please rise.” Lady Zhang smiled at Shen Yanshui’s strikingly beautiful face, though a faint bitterness lingered in her expression.","Though she held the highest rank among the Crown Prince’s new women, he had not visited her chambers the previous night. The thought left a bitter taste in her heart—and made her lose face as well.","For now, she could only console herself that it had been Lady Shen rather than Lady Wu.","At least Lady Shen did not appear to be the sort to be sharp-tongued, competitive, or cruel. Had Lady Wu been the one favored last night, who knew how she might have flaunted it and mocked Lady Zhang today?","After exchanging formal greetings, they said nothing further. After all, they were not yet acquainted.","Shen Yanshui glanced at Lady Zhao, who stood behind Lady Zhang. She had never met her before; then Lady Zhao must have been one of the women already in the Eastern Palace.","They passed through Moonlight Gate and rounded a long covered corridor. The main hall of Fragrant Gathering Hall lay before them. Just as they were about to remove their cloaks, all of them halted in unspoken accord.","Before the steps of the main hall stood an extraordinary tree none of them had ever seen before.","Its branches were covered in silver-white blossoms, bright as snow. The boughs bent low beneath masses of blooms, as if piled with clouds and carved from jade. When the breeze stirred, tiny petals fluttered down in a soft drift, truly resembling spring willow fluff or snow swirling through winter air.","“What... what kind of flower is this? I have never seen anything like it before,” Lady Liu exclaimed softly.","Lady Zhang’s eyes widened slightly as well. “The whole tree is white, as though it had been dusted with snow. What a remarkable sight.”","Shen Yanshui gazed at the April snow before her in equal surprise. Then she quickly noticed several pots of golden-edged winter daphne blooming unusually well beside the steps. Their emerald leaves were rimmed in gold, their purple blossoms clustered thickly together, their fragrance filling the hall.","The others noticed them as well, but before they could look more closely, maids from Fragrant Gathering Hall had already come forward. The group removed their cloaks and was led into the main chamber by a maid serving the Crown Princess.","“Your servant pays her respects to the Crown Princess. May Your Highness enjoy peace and good fortune.”","The Crown Princess wore a wisteria-purple gown with wide sleeves. A shoulder-length crown adorned with hairpins and pearls rested upon her head, lending her a dignified and graceful air. With a warm smile, she looked at the women before her and said, “We are all sisters here, so there is no need for such ceremony. Please, take your seats. Serve the tea.”","“Thank you, Your Highness.”","After the newcomers rose, they exchanged another round of greetings with those who had arrived earlier before finally taking their seats.","Shen Yanshui’s place was toward the back, close to the main hall’s entrance. Holding a cup of hot tea, she looked at the pre-rain Longjing within it and pretended to take a sip. Her lips merely brushed the surface before she stopped. She then wrapped both hands around the cup to warm them.","“One can only have the chance to taste such fine pre-rain Longjing here in Your Highness’s residence. This must be this year’s new tea, mustn’t it?” a clear, ringing voice suddenly called out.","Shen Yanshui raised her eyes and saw a woman dressed in a blue, wide-sleeved jacket. She had a plump, rounded figure, yet wore her hair simply in a round bun. Her face was filled with eager flattery as she addressed the Crown Princess.","The Crown Princess pressed her lips together and replied with an elegant, composed smile, “It was merely some tea bestowed by the Crown Prince. It is nothing particularly valuable. If you like it, you should come sit with me more often.”","“The Crown Prince treats Your Highness so well. I heard that the April Snow and Golden-Edged Daphne outside were both newly presented tributes...”","Listening to the two women exchange pleasantries, Shen Yanshui soon figured out who the speaker was.","Lady Wang. She had a daughter, a little princess who was only a year old, and had once been the Crown Princess’s maid who accompanied her upon marriage.","With an absent-minded glance around the room, Shen Yanshui noticed that every seat was occupied except the one to the Crown Princess’s lower left. That must be the place reserved for Lady Chu, the highest-ranking woman in the Eastern Palace apart from the Crown Princess.","Aside from the Crown Princess, who had given birth to a little imperial grandson, Lady Wang, the Crown Princess’s former maid, was the only woman in the Eastern Palace with a child—a daughter. There were no other offspring.","However, it was said that Lady Chu, who was greatly favored, was now pregnant.","Just as Shen Yanshui was thinking about this, she heard movement outside. The woman’s voice reached them before she herself appeared.","“What fragrance are the Crown Princess and all the younger sisters discussing?”","Shen Yanshui turned her head and saw a strikingly beautiful woman surrounded by everyone else.","The newcomer wore a pomegranate-red gown with wide sleeves and a peony crown studded with pearls. One hand rested on the arm of the nanny beside her as she walked with her heavily pregnant belly. Two palace maids led the way, followed closely by four more nannies.","Shen Yanshui took one look at this display and could not help inwardly clicking her tongue in amazement.","“Your servant pays her respects to the Crown Princess. Please forgive me for being unable to complete the proper ceremony.”","Lady Chu offered only a token curtsy before apologizing with an apologetic expression.","The Crown Princess hurriedly had someone support her and said with gentle reproach, “You are carrying a child, and the imperial physician said that this pregnancy has not been progressing well. I already excused you from paying your respects each morning. You should be resting and taking good care of yourself. Why put yourself through all this?”","Lady Chu pressed her lips into a smile. After taking her seat, she continued with a smile, “Your Highness’s kindness is engraved in my heart. Still, I ought to come and meet all the new younger sisters today. Otherwise, if we happen to meet face-to-face in the future without recognizing one another, would that not be embarrassing?”","With that, she smiled and said, “Oh, right. Your Highness, what were you and the other ladies discussing just now? I could hear how lively it was from all the way over there.”","The Crown Princess smiled. “Nothing much. We were merely talking about some of the flowers and plants outside the hall.”","The corners of Lady Chu’s mouth stiffened for a moment. They had been arranged so conspicuously, as though they were afraid no one would notice them.","She covered her lips and said, “They are indeed rather unusual. But no matter how beautiful the flowers are, how could they compare with the new sisters here? You are all so lovely that even I cannot help feeling inferior.”","Lady Wu instinctively lifted her chin with some pride, while Shen Yanshui and the others hurriedly murmured that she was too kind. Then Lady Chu suddenly changed the subject. Her gaze swept over them, pausing for a moment on Lady Wu’s face, before she smiled and asked, “I wonder which of you is Lady Shen?”","Shen Yanshui rose and lowered her head, offering a respectful curtsy. “This servant pays her respects to Lady Chu.”","Lady Chu cast her a sidelong glance, looking her up and down. Then she smiled carelessly. “You truly are a beauty in the making. No wonder His Highness has taken a liking to you.”","As she spoke, she cast a meaningful glance at Lady Zhang and Lady Wu, who were seated in front of her.","Lady Zhang lowered her head, twisting her handkerchief in both hands without daring to say a word.","Lady Wu, seated only one tea table away from Shen Yanshui, immediately flushed with humiliation and anger. Unable to restrain herself, she turned her head and glared fiercely at Shen Yanshui!","In terms of status, beauty, or talent, she had never thought herself inferior in any way to Shen Yanshui, who had nothing but her looks. So why was Shen Yanshui the one lucky enough to win His Highness’s favor first?","Seeing that Lady Wu was still glaring at her, Shen Yanshui asked with concern, “Sister Wu, what is wrong with your eyes? They are completely red. Are you feeling unwell?”","Lady Wu’s heart lurched, but embarrassment and anger quickly followed. She glared at Shen Yanshui. “What do you mean? Are you saying I’m jealous of you?”","Shen Yanshui glanced at her timidly and pressed her lips together. “Sister Wu, you misunderstand. That was not what I meant. I was only concerned that your eyes might be uncomfortable, so I asked.”","Lady Wu did not believe her. She had seen plenty of women who deliberately acted weak and pitiful like this!","“You—”","The Crown Princess smiled and said, “That is enough. Lady Shen was only showing concern for you.”","Hearing this, Lady Wu felt even more aggrieved and furious. Yet she did not dare to make another scene in front of the Crown Princess, so she could only grit her teeth and swallow her anger.","The Crown Princess turned her gaze toward Lady Shen. Her smile now appeared a little more genuine. After exchanging a few more words and introducing the newcomers to the old residents of the Eastern Palace, she said, “I must go to Kunning Palace shortly to pay my respects to Her Majesty the Empress Dowager. We shall end things here for today. There is no need for you to come for morning greetings every day from now on. Once every five days will suffice.”","“Yes.”","The women rose and curtsied before dispersing. Lady Wu had a breath of anger caught in her throat, but she could only swallow it herself, not daring to cause trouble in front of the Crown Princess.","Lady Chu was the first to leave, accompanied by the same grand retinue as when she had arrived. The others then withdrew in succession according to their rank.","Shen Yanshui slowed her pace, allowing the women of higher rank to go ahead first.","But Lady Wu was determined to have the last word. Pulling a long face, she glared at Shen Yanshui and ground out, “Don’t celebrate too soon. We’ll see how this turns out.”","Shen Yanshui remained composed, smiling as she watched Lady Wu’s retreating back. It was not until they had entered Lianxin Court and returned to their rooms that Chunping lowered her voice and asked, “Mistress, should we have someone keep an eye on Lady Wu?”","Shen Yanshui slipped off her soft-soled embroidered shoes and sat down on the couch. Hearing this, she nodded with a smile. “We can’t be deaf and blind to what goes on in the Eastern Palace, but we must also know where to draw the line. Anyone who personally serves the two little princes must not grow too close to anyone else. Have them keep their distance as much as possible in their daily dealings.”","Chunping bowed. “Yes, Mistress. I understand.”","Shen Yanshui had Qiuru remove the moon-pearl coronet and jade hairpin with its beaded tassels from her head, leaving only two dark-red ribbons to tie up her hair. The weight on her head was instantly much lighter.","She then leaned back comfortably against the couch and began mulling things over, idly fiddling with the verdant bamboo branch on the incense table.","Before yesterday, all of the Crown Prince’s wives and concubines together numbered only seven. Compared with the other princes, whose rear palaces often held twenty or even thirty women, that was not many at all—in fact, it was comparatively few.","Shen Yanshui did not particularly care. Eating well, living comfortably, and enjoying her own quiet little life was what she wanted.","When she had been bestowed upon the Eastern Palace, she had originally assumed that she would have to rely on money to get by from then on. But the Crown Prince had shown her another possibility.","Not wanting to fight tooth and nail merely to win his favor was one thing. But if his favor came her way—and could make her life more comfortable—she would not turn down such an opportunity.","Just then, Quanfu hurried into the room and reported, “Mistress, the Crown Princess has bestowed two pots of golden-edged daphne...”","At that, Shen Yanshui quickly rose and accepted the gift with due respect. As was customary, she slipped the eunuch some silver before sending away the attendants from the Crown Princess’s household. Only afterward did she learn that the Crown Princess had not bestowed gifts on her alone. Several of the more prominent secondary consorts in the rear quarters had received them as well.","The only difference was that some had received fewer pots, while others had received more.","She turned her gaze to the golden-edged daphne blooming luxuriantly beside her.","Its leaves were ringed with gold along the edges and emerald green in the middle. The flowers were tiny, clustered tightly together at the tips of the branches. Their outer petals were pale reddish-purple or pinkish-purple, while the inner petals were milky white.","They looked both elegant and sumptuous, and made a very respectable display in the room.","But Shen Yanshui knew that this flower was also called the “scent-stealing flower,” renowned for its intense fragrance.","If a pregnant woman were to smell it...","Her gaze grew slightly guarded as her fingertips brushed lightly over the clustered purple-red buds.","During pregnancy, a woman’s qi and blood naturally descend to nourish the fetus, leaving the qi in the upper body more prone to weakness.","At first, the flower’s fragrance would make her feel invigorated. But after prolonged exposure, it could cause dizziness and vertigo, making it impossible to sleep at night and leaving one’s rest unsettled, thereby depriving the fetus of nourishment.","With still longer exposure, it could lead to chest tightness, shortness of breath, palpitations, and night sweats...","The only question was whether this had been done deliberately, or whether it was merely an innocent mistake."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: Empress","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui had Quanshou place the two pots of golden-edged daphne in the courtyard, somewhere they could be seen as soon as one entered the gate. It would neither appear neglectful nor cause much inconvenience thereafter.","Unless, of course, someone happened to be particularly sensitive.","“My lady, shall I have breakfast brought in?” Chunping came forward with a smile and bowed as she asked.","Shen Yanshui’s eyes lit up, and she temporarily set the matter aside. “Yes. The dishes you suggested yesterday were all quite good. From now on, add one or two extra dishes to each meal in addition to my regular allowance. I’ll try them all first.”","As a Zhaoxun, her allotted meals were meager—only two meat dishes, two vegetable dishes, a soup, and a serving of fruit per meal. It was hardly enough to fill her stomach.","Although Chunping smiled, she replied in her usual composed manner, “You flatter me, my lady. When I was serving in the Imperial Food Bureau, I happened to hear all sorts of idle talk. I know a little about the specialties of nearly every head chef in the palace kitchens. So long as you enjoy the food, that is all that matters.”","Shen Yanshui smiled and nodded. She then had Qiuru open the cash box and sent someone to order breakfast.","Chunping smiled from the side. “My lady, I’m afraid we won’t need that money today. The servants in this palace are most prone to fawning on the powerful and trampling on the weak. You were just favored by His Highness last night. How could the kitchen staff possibly accept our money now?”","Things turned out exactly as Chunping had predicted. When Dongyi and Quanshou entered carrying two food boxes, their faces were full of unconcealed delight.","Dongyi was young. Though she could not be called flighty, neither was she particularly steady. At once, her joy showed plainly on her face as she said, “My lady, the kitchen staff not only refused to take our money today, they even sent you many extra dishes. One food box couldn’t hold them all.”","Shen Yanshui smiled but did not speak for a moment.","Looking at the two three-tiered, octagonal red sandalwood food boxes in their gaudy mother-of-pearl inlay, Chunping could not help frowning.","“My lady was favored only yesterday, and you are already behaving like this. Others will think that now our mistress has gained His Highness’s favor, she has become arrogant and conceited. They will look down on her.”","Quanshou jumped in fright. Lowering his head, he stammered, “My lady, Quanfu-gege already told me just now. I won’t dare do it again.”","When he had first been reprimanded, he had not taken it entirely to heart. He had even felt a little dissatisfied at being lectured by Quanfu, who was younger than he was.","But Chunping was different. Even before coming to serve Shen Yanshui, she had been more experienced and better connected than any of them. Now she was one of their mistress’s trusted attendants, and her words immediately made him tighten up with fear.","Seeing this, Dongyi’s face turned pale as she dropped to her knees. “Please forgive me, my lady! I—I know I was wrong!”","Shen Yanshui slowly straightened in her seat and looked at the two of them. “Call everyone else in.”","Before long, all the servants had assembled. Shen Yanshui’s expression grew stern.","“Besides what I told you yesterday, there is one more thing I wish to make clear today. My household has no place for arrogant, reckless people.”","“Not to mention that I was only favored for the first time yesterday. No one knows what the future will bring. Even if I were favored for several days, so what? Flowers do not bloom for a hundred days, and no one enjoys good fortune for a thousand. You should understand that better than anyone.”","“Yes, my lady. We will keep it firmly in mind.”","After she finished speaking, everyone’s thoughts naturally varied. Chunping and Quanfu still appeared fairly calm, and even seemed relieved.","After all, acting with restraint was much more reassuring than behaving loudly and ostentatiously.","As for Dongyi, she was still young and had not experienced much of the world. Having spent all this time at the very bottom of the palace hierarchy, she had been unable to control herself when someone suddenly flattered her and had begun to let her pride show.","It was only human nature. Someone who had lived in poverty and been looked down upon for years would likely be unable to resist showing off after suddenly winning the lottery.","Shen Yanshui understood this. In fact, she had anticipated it beforehand. After studying everyone’s reactions, she was reasonably satisfied.","Chunping had worked in the Imperial Food Bureau, a place where she had dealt with all kinds of people. She was experienced, steady, and not easily carried away. Quanfu had received proper guidance; he was clever without lacking tact.","Quanshou was timid, but honest and obedient. After this incident, he should have learned his lesson.","Xia’an and Qiuru were not as steady as Chunping, but for now they seemed dependable enough. Dongyi, however, was the youngest and therefore the most impetuous.","Seeing that Dongyi and Quanshou were trembling uncontrollably, Shen Yanshui did not continue frightening them.","“No matter the circumstances, remember to act cautiously and discreetly whenever you are outside. Do not show off, and do not cause trouble.","“But just because we do not want trouble does not mean we fear it. If anyone bullies you outside, report it to me. I will not let you be mistreated for nothing.”","“Now get up. There is no need to keep kneeling.”","“Yes! Thank you, my lady.”","Hearing her words and sensing her softened tone, Dongyi and Quanshou both breathed a sigh of relief. When they realized that their mistress truly had no intention of punishing them, they hurriedly kowtowed in thanks.","After sending the others away, Shen Yanshui kept Chunping and Quanfu behind. As she ate breakfast, she looked at them with a smile.","“Do you think I made too much of a fuss?”","“We would not dare,” the two of them replied at once, bowing their heads.","Quanfu said respectfully, “A tree that rises above the forest will be battered by the wind. My lady is wise.”","Chunping answered seriously, “It is best to correct them early and make sure they know what may and may not be done. Otherwise, they may cause trouble and resentment for you when they are outside.”","Though palace servants’ lives were worth little more than weeds, even the smallest people could sometimes play a crucial role, in ways no one could imagine. It was always better to make friends than enemies wherever possible.","Hearing this, Shen Yanshui was even more satisfied. She smiled and said, “The kitchen staff saw that I had gained His Highness’s favor and sent an extra dish or two of fresh food. There was nothing wrong with that. But in everything we do, we must keep our judgment. We must not be so easily flattered that we lose all sense of propriety and make ourselves a laughingstock.”","“Yes, my lady. We understand.”","The two bowed and withdrew. Chunping noticed that Dongyi still looked uneasy, so she called her into the room.","Dongyi’s eyes were red, and her voice trembled with tears. “Sister Chunping... I know I was wrong. Yesterday, when I went to collect the food, I bumped into a palace maid and eunuch from the neighboring courtyard. The people in the kitchen made several cutting remarks at me. Then today, after hearing a few pleasant words, I couldn’t stop myself from feeling happy. I really know I was wrong. I won’t dare do it again...”","Chunping had not expected there to be such a reason behind it. Her expression turned serious.","“It is good that you understand your mistake. Our mistress is kind and generous, which is why she did not punish you. From now on, you must act even more steadily and cautiously outside. Other than our own people, no one else is to handle our food at any point. Do you understand?”","Dongyi hurriedly nodded again and again. “I’ll remember it all!”","*","The main hall of Haoyue Study, the residence nearest the Moonlight Gate, was furnished with exquisite luxury. Gold and jade articles could be seen everywhere. Fuguang brocade, which would have been impossible to buy even for a thousand gold pieces outside the palace, had been spread over the daybed as a mattress and made into cushions. Its extravagance was self-evident.","Four pots of golden-edged daphne had been placed far away in the courtyard.","Even with the matrons sent by the Empress keeping watch over her, and imperial physicians coming to check on her health every other day, Lady Chu did not think the Crown Princess would dare to tamper with that potted flower. Still, to err on the side of caution, she had the flower placed far away from her quarters.","\"Master, that Lady Shen...\" a maid at Lady Chu's side suddenly spoke up in a soft voice.","Lady Chu rested her hand gently on her belly, first frowning slightly, then said nonchalantly, \"What's the rush? It's only been a day. Now that there are new concubines in the Eastern Palace, even if it weren't her, there would be others.\"","Among the four new women, Lady Wu was clearly a sharp, overambitious sort. For all her good looks, she was no threat at all.","As for the leading Lady Zhang and Lady Liu, whose petty schemes were written all over her face, Lady Chu did not spare them a single thought.","When it came to that Lady Shen, Lady Chu let out a soft chuckle. \"What a pity...\"","Her personal senior maid stepped forward with a cup of tea, having missed the soft murmur under Lady Chu's breath, and said with a smile, \"The most important thing now is the little imperial grandson in your belly. Once you give birth to a healthy, fine little imperial grandson, your good days are still to come. Even the Empress will surely look at you with new respect then.\"","Lady Chu stroked her belly tenderly, a look of determined triumph on her face. \"Imperial Physician Zhao has already confirmed that the child in my womb is a little imperial grandson, no doubt about it. When my son is born...\"","A look of proud glory came over her as she patted her belly gently. \"My son is bound to be bright and clever. He must strive to do well in the future, and crush that sickly boy into the dirt...\"","*","\"Your Highness, the Empress told us to bring Little Prince to her to see him long ago. We have already declined twice. If we refuse again this time... I am afraid it will make the Empress feel displeased.\"","Inside the Hall of Fragrant Gatherings, Matron Zhou pleaded in a low, earnest voice. \"The imperial physicians also said that the Empress's ailment was brought on by long-term overexertion, and it is not contagious. Little Prince has been in better health lately, so it should be quite safe.\"","But the Crown Princess rejected the idea without the slightest hesitation, frowning and saying, \"The Empress has been ill for ages and has not recovered. She knows full well that Zhang'er has been frail since he was a child, so she should be all the more careful of his health. What if he catches a chill when going out? What if the sickness passes to him?\"","\"Besides, the Empress has long disliked me because I failed to give the Crown Prince a healthy child. Now she has bestowed new concubines on the Eastern Palace, and no doubt she is eagerly looking forward to those women giving birth to heirs for the Crown Prince soon. If that's the case, why bother to trouble my son?\"","Matron Zhou's face fell, and she tried to persuade her again, \"Your Highness...\"","\"Say no more, Matron. That little life in Lady Chu's belly is the apple of the Empress's eye now. It's only been a few months, but the rewards being lavished on Lady Chu flow like water, all to prop that lowly woman up at my expense.\" The Crown Princess said coldly. \"I'd like to see just what that belly of hers can produce.\"","Seeing that the Crown Princess was full of resentment toward the Empress and stubbornly refused to yield, Matron Zhou had no choice but to give up.","...","\"Your subject greets Your Majesty, may Your Majesty live a thousand years in peace and prosperity.\" The Crown Princess stepped into the Palace of Earthly Tranquility, bowed her head, and greeted the Empress respectfully.","Seated at the top was the Empress, dressed in a plain purple informal robe with wide sleeves, no makeup on her face. Even so, one could still tell she had been strikingly beautiful in her youth, though now her face was pale and lined with exhaustion.","The Empress's eyes, which had been full of hope a moment earlier, darkened when she saw the Crown Princess and the retinue behind her.","\"Where is Zhang'er?\"","This was the first time the Empress had not told her to rise immediately. The Crown Princess felt even more certain that the Empress was deliberately making things difficult for her. Her heart filled with rising resentment, and the tone of her voice unconsciously turned stiff.","\"Replying to Your Majesty, the imperial physicians say Zhang'er's illness has not yet healed, so it is not suitable for him to go out, lest he be invaded by cold pathogenic air. Your subject did not bring Zhang'er here, and asks for Your Majesty's forgiveness.\"","Seeing the look of resentment that the Crown Princess could not hide even with her head bowed, the Empress closed her eyes for a moment, then waved her hand to dismiss her, deciding that out of sight was out of mind.","The Crown Princess's face froze slightly. She had come to pay her respects and tend to the Empress during her illness, but she had been sent away only moments after arriving. If word of this got out, her reputation and dignity would be completely ruined.","She forced a stiff smile. \"Your Majesty...\"","The Empress looked at her with a solemn, expressionless face. \"There is a concubine in the Eastern Palace who is with child now. It is your duty to look after her with all your care. You do not need to come here every day to pay me respects for the next few months.\"","At those words, the Crown Princess's face changed slightly, but looking after the heirs of the Eastern Palace was indeed the responsibility of the Crown Princess.","The Crown Princess bowed her head. \"As Your Majesty commands. But while Your Majesty's illness has not healed, and the Crown Prince is busy with government affairs, tending to Your Majesty with care and performing the duties of a daughter-in-law is what my filial piety demands. Otherwise, I would never be able to rest easy.\"","The Empress frowned, and Nanny Fan at her side said with a gentle smile, \"The Empress naturally knows of the Crown Princess's filial piety. But the imperial physicians say Her Majesty's illness requires quiet rest above all, and keeping a cheerful mind is the most important thing.\"","The Crown Princess's expression did not shift, but her hands clenched tightly under her sleeves. That old hag was implying that her visits to pay respects were making the Empress unhappy!","Nanny Fan seemed not to notice her reaction, and continued speaking in the same unhurried, pleasant tone. \"Now that the Crown Prince has very few heirs, the Crown Princess should take good care of her own health, so that she may soon give birth to another child for the Crown Prince.\"","The Empress raised a hand to rub her forehead. \"Nanny Fan is right. From now on, you only need to come to see me once every ten days. You may leave now, Crown Princess.\""]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Contradiction","paragraphs":["Only after the Crown Princess had left did Nanny Fan, who attended at the Empress’s side, sigh in displeasure. “Your Majesty, you indulge the Crown Princess far too much.”","At that, the Empress slowly opened her eyes. Frowning, she said regretfully, “Back then, when His Majesty said he wanted to choose a girl from a distinguished family for Yu’er, I thought that since Master Wenchuan was a man of noble character and upright family traditions, his granddaughter—having been taught by him from childhood—would surely be gentle, virtuous, and sensible...”","The Crown Princess’s father, Li Cheng, the Vice Censor-in-Chief, was a man of loyalty and integrity. Her mother came from Duke Wengu’s household. Though the family held no military power, its sons had always entered court through their literary achievements, which was an advantage in itself.","That was why the Empress had chosen her.","“Who could have imagined that the Crown Princess would have such a temperament?”","“The Eastern Palace has always been short of heirs and is already unstable. It is surrounded by wolves and tigers, yet as Crown Princess, instead of thinking about supporting the Crown Prince and securing the Eastern Palace, she keeps her eyes fixed only on the small patch of land that is the inner court.”","“If not for her jealousy, Lady Sun would never have miscarried after I bestowed her upon the Crown Prince, and the Crown Prince would not have become estranged from her!”","“And she actually thinks she is the cleverest person in the world, treating everyone else as fools.” The Empress sneered.","“Your Majesty, please calm down. The Crown Princess does not understand your good intentions. She simply has no blessing to appreciate them.”","The Empress sighed, her voice turning cold. “I only hope she will be clever enough this time.”","If she dared reach out against the Crown Prince’s heirs again, she must not blame the Empress for what followed.","“Your Majesty has bestowed gifts upon Lady Chu several times. In every word, you have both cautioned and reassured her. I imagine the Crown Princess should understand by now.”","Though Nanny Fan said this, she too harbored resentment toward the Crown Princess. If not for the Empress’s kindness—having personally tasted the agony of being separated from her own child and not wishing anyone else to suffer the same—what would have been wrong with taking the Little Prince to Kunning Palace and raising him there?","The Little Prince had been born a year and five months ago—nearly three by nominal reckoning—yet the Empress had only seen him twice. What grandmother in the world was unable to see her own grandson? And yet her mistress had happened to encounter such a narrow-minded woman.","Had the Crown Princess’s mother-in-law been someone other than Her Majesty—one of those high-ranking consorts skilled in underhanded schemes—who knew what sort of torment she would already have endured?","“I hope she truly understands.” The Empress pressed a hand to her brow. “By the way, I was not feeling well some time ago. Yesterday, I noticed that one of the selected candidates originally marked for the Crown Prince had been crossed out, and Noble Consort Lan had selected Lady Shen’s younger sister instead?”","Nanny Fan bowed and replied, “In answer to Your Majesty, that is indeed what happened. Noble Consort Lan deliberately delayed matters and, bypassing you entirely, submitted the list directly to His Majesty.”","The Empress was not surprised. If Noble Consort Lan did not stir up some trouble, she would have found it strange. By selecting the younger sister of Lady Shen—a pawn clearly meant to make the Crown Prince unhappy—it was obvious that Noble Consort Lan had done so deliberately.","But what angered her even more than the disgust she felt was the Emperor’s attitude.","*","After finishing his duties at the hour of Shen, Cui Yu left the Jingzhao Prefecture yamen in his crimson official robes and boarded the Eastern Palace carriage.","In the Great Yong Dynasty, the Crown Prince not only spent his days studying and attending court to hear state affairs; he also served as the Prefect of Jingzhao. It was considered another way of assessing his ability to handle government affairs.","Seated nearby, Zheng Yuande saw that his master’s expression was calm and gave away none of his emotions. He could not help but breathe a sigh of relief.","Having served his master for many years, he could still discern a thing or two. Ever since the General of Agile Cavalry had been reprimanded by His Majesty and stripped of his title as Military Commissioner of the Protecting-State Army, it had been rare to see His Highness in such a peaceful frame of mind.","At court that morning, contrary to Zheng Yuande’s expectations, he had thought His Highness would once again argue with His Majesty and plead for the General of Agile Cavalry, only to be reprimanded by the Emperor. Unexpectedly, His Highness had acted entirely out of character and had not argued on the general’s behalf again.","Cui Yu closed his eyes to rest. Suddenly, he lifted them and said, “If you have something to say, say it.” His voice was clear and steady.","With his round, fair face beaming, Zheng Yuande ingratiatingly replied, “Your Highness truly possesses divine foresight. You can tell that this servant is bursting with questions even with your eyes closed.”","Cui Yu shot him a glance.","Zheng Yuande did not dare put on airs any longer. He chuckled and said, “This servant was worried about Your Highness, but who could have expected His Majesty to praise you in open court? I saw the expressions on the Fourth Prince’s face and those of the other princes when they left the court—not one of them was smiling. It was deeply satisfying.”","Those princes had deliberately come up to needle His Highness after the Emperor reprimanded him. Now that His Highness had received the Emperor’s praise, they were the ones left fuming!","Cui Yu lowered his eyes, his voice deep and unreadable. “Arguing is useless.”","What would winning an argument accomplish?","An emperor would always be wary of a subject whose achievements threatened to overshadow the throne. Whether one was right or wrong no longer mattered.","It was simply that, before this, he had been unable to accept that his maternal uncle had guarded the frontier and fought through bloodshed, only for the military honors he had earned with his life to be stripped away as though they were nothing more than a child’s game.","He felt that it was unfair and unworthy—not only to his maternal uncle, but also to the soldiers who defended Great Yong.","Yet his position as Crown Prince, combined with the military merits his maternal uncle had earned, had already made his father wary of him. If he took a step back, perhaps his father’s suspicion and defenses would ease somewhat, making things safer for his maternal grandfather and uncle.","Since that was the case, there was no need to fight over a momentary victory.","However, as soon as he returned to the Eastern Palace, Cui Yu heard Cao Zhongda, the eunuch in charge of the front halls, quietly report several matters to him. Zheng Yuande’s expression changed slightly. Inwardly, he could not help complaining about the Crown Princess. He truly did not know what she was thinking. How could she dare act one way in public and another in private before the Empress? Her audacity was simply too great.","After hearing the report, Cui Yu’s expression remained unchanged, revealing nothing. Only a trace of coldness appeared in his previously tranquil eyes.","*","“Your Highness, please listen to this old servant’s advice. When we go to pay our respects to the Empress toward the end of the month, let us take the Little Prince with us, all right?” Matron Zhou urged in a low voice, pleading earnestly.","The Crown Princess’s face was grim, and her heart ached even more. “Did you not see how deliberately Her Majesty made things difficult for me today? Every word she spoke implied that the Crown Prince has so few heirs because of me. It is all my fault—that I failed to give His Highness a healthy son!”","Since childhood, she had been the most outstanding among her sisters. The husband she had married was also the most exalted man in the world—the Crown Prince himself. Yet she had given birth to a sickly son, leaving her unable to hold her head high before Her Majesty or anyone else.","Matron Zhou naturally felt distressed for the young mistress she had nursed and raised. But now that the girl was a daughter-in-law of the imperial family, she could no longer allow her to indulge her temper as she pleased.","She consoled her, “Your Highness, please set your mind at ease. The Little Prince is currently the only son under the Crown Prince’s name. No one else can possibly surpass him.”","“If our Little Prince can win the Empress’s affection and favor, it will benefit both us and the Little Prince. Why insist on competing with the Empress over this momentary grievance? If His Highness finds out, the one injured will be the affection between husband and wife.”","The Crown Princess’s expression shifted slightly.","As the two were speaking, familiar sounds came from outside.","The Crown Princess hurriedly straightened her clothes and makeup, then went forward at a brisk pace to greet him and offer her respects.","Cui Yu stopped before her and looked down at her face. Only after a moment did he speak, telling her to rise.","Once they had settled in before the luohan couch, the Crown Princess hurriedly ordered someone to brew a pot of hot tea and presented it to him herself. Her voice was gentle and warm with a smile. “Your Highness, have you just returned from your duties? You have been so busy with state affairs lately, but you must take care of yourself as well. Be sure not to overwork yourself and damage your health.”","Cui Yu lifted his eyes to her gentle smile, his voice slightly deep. “No need.”","The Crown Princess smiled and placed the teacup on a small table nearby. Then she asked with a smile, “Would Your Highness like to have a meal brought in?”","“No need.” After saying this, Cui Yu turned toward Matron Zhou. “Where is Zhang’er?”","At this, the smile on the Crown Princess’s face became even more genuine. She quickly turned and ordered, “Hurry and bring Zhang’er here.”","Matron Zhou was naturally pleased that His Highness the Crown Prince kept their Little Prince in his thoughts. After the wet nurse entered carrying the swaddled infant and paid her respects, she bent forward respectfully and presented the Little Prince to the Crown Prince.","Cui Yu glanced at the child, who still had his eyes closed, then told the wet nurse to carry him away so as not to wake him.","As though asking casually, he said, “I remember the Crown Princess said yesterday that Zhang’er’s health had grown much stronger recently?”","The Crown Princess’s heart tightened. Her fingers unconsciously clenched the handkerchief in her hand. “In reply to Your Highness, the physicians said that although Zhang’er’s health has improved somewhat recently, he still needs to recuperate quietly and cannot be exposed to drafts.”","“Oh? Is that so?” Cui Yu absently rubbed the cool jade ring on his thumb. “As it happens, I summoned the Imperial Physician Director here. Someone, ask Physician Lu to examine Chang’er and make sure he is in good health.”","Zheng Yuande: “Yes, Your Highness.”","The Crown Princess’s expression stiffened slightly, and she hurriedly said, “Your Highness, Zhang’er’s regular physician has always been Physician Zhang. Would it not be better to summon him instead? He is more familiar with Zhang’er’s condition.”","Cui Yu’s voice remained calm. “As the Imperial Physician Director, Physician Lu’s medical skills are naturally no inferior to Physician Zhang’s.”","The Crown Princess’s expression tightened. She lowered her head to conceal it. Every few days, the Crown Prince would ask about the child’s condition, and at first she had not found anything suspicious. But now...","Before long, Zheng Yuande entered with an elderly man whose hair and beard were gray and who wore the official robes of an Imperial Physician Director.","After paying his respects, Imperial Physician Director Lu reported, “In reply to Your Highness and Her Highness, the Little Prince’s health is somewhat weaker than that of ordinary infants his age. However, so long as he is carefully tended, he should be no different from anyone else once he grows up.”","Cui Yu asked, “Can he withstand being moved at present?”","“If curtains are hung around the Little Prince’s palanquin, it will cause no harm.”","“Thank you for your trouble, Imperial Physician Director Lu.”","After Zheng Yuande escorted him out, he had barely stepped back inside when he heard His Highness’s calm, emotionless voice.","“Someone, bring the palanquin.”","The Crown Princess’s heart turned cold and heavy. The Empress must have sent someone to tell His Highness something. Otherwise, why would he have immediately taken action the moment he returned from his duties?","How hateful!","Zheng Yuande smoothly turned around and went back out. He was deeply puzzled by the Crown Princess’s almost blatant disregard for Her Majesty the Empress.","The Empress’s illness was neither a cold nor an infectious disease. It was not contagious in the slightest. Where, then, had the Crown Princess found the courage to challenge Her Majesty’s authority again and again?","Matron Zhou instantly dropped to her knees and kowtowed as she pleaded, “Your Highness, please be magnanimous. Her Highness was simply too concerned about the Little Prince’s health, which was why she did not take him to see Her Majesty the Empress today. When Her Highness returned just now, she even told this old servant that she planned to pay Her Majesty a visit later this month. By then, the Little Prince should have recovered, and Her Highness will take him along so Her Majesty may examine him carefully.”","Cui Yu turned his gaze toward the Crown Princess, his voice turning cold. “Oh? Is that so?”","The Crown Princess’s face was stiff and pale. After a long moment, she finally bit her lip, bent her knees, and lowered her head. “Yes. That was indeed my intention. However, I acted without sufficient consideration and caused Mother Empress needless worry during her illness. I beg Your Highness to forgive me.”","Cui Yu slowly rose to his feet and looked down at her expression and demeanor. After a moment, he said in a low voice, “Mother Empress has devoted herself to making plans for you and me. Zhang’er is the Crown Prince’s legitimate eldest son. Do not disappoint Mother Empress’s painstaking efforts.”","The Crown Princess grew even more resentful at his words.","Making plans? The Empress had only one son, His Highness the Crown Prince. Was it not only natural for her to plan for him? Were her own father and brothers not likewise making arrangements for the Crown Prince in court?","And as for painstaking efforts... A cold laugh rose in her heart. Was he referring to the efforts she had made by repeatedly bestowing gifts upon Lady Chu, heedless of the dignity of the Crown Princess?","Such painstaking efforts were more than she could accept.","Yet no matter what she thought in her heart, she endured the grievance for the moment and kept it from showing on her face.","The disappointment in Cui Yu’s eyes vanished in an instant. His dark eyes were calm and utterly without ripples. He said nothing more, but turned and left."]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: Vulgar","paragraphs":["It was not until that cold, austere figure had vanished from sight that the Crown Princess finally collapsed onto the couch.","“Your Highness...”","Zheng Yuande stole a glance at his mistress’s expression, inwardly groaning bitterly. What a life they were leading!","His Highness’s mood had only just begun to improve, and now he had to hear about all the troublesome things the Crown Princess had done. Wasn’t it enough that she had already given him so much to worry about?","Cui Yu strode forward with a grave, composed expression. When he looked up, he realized that he had arrived at Lianxin Court. After pausing for only a moment, he walked in.","Shen Yanshui had heard the sudden commotion outside and hurried out to greet him. “Please forgive my lack of ceremony, Your Highness. I hope you won’t take offense.”","Cui Yu saw that she was dressed in nothing more than a simple sky-blue long skirt. She wore no headdress; her dark hair was tied with a gauze ribbon and arranged in a cloud-like coiffure. Her face was bare of powder and rouge, yet her fair cheeks glowed with a healthy flush, full of vitality. Without realizing it, he looked at her a little longer than he should have.","Shen Yanshui raised her eyes and smiled at him, just about to speak, when a light, quick set of footsteps approached. It was Lady Liu.","Though Lady Liu’s clothes were not especially luxurious, they were immaculate. Her makeup was even more exquisite, and a delicate apricot-blossom crown adorned her head, accented with silver-and-jade hair ornaments that chimed softly as she moved. Every word, gesture, smile, and frown seemed to have been measured against the strictest standards of palace etiquette, leaving not the slightest fault to find.","Even Shen Yanshui had to admire her inwardly. Lady Liu certainly had not studied those rules for nothing; she had clearly put considerable effort into them.","Unlike Shen Yanshui, who had few demands of herself and never made things difficult when she could help it—so long as she was neither outstanding nor disgraceful, that was good enough.","This was Lady Liu’s first time seeing the Crown Prince. At a single glance, she could barely control her racing heart and flushed face. Her heart pounded wildly, and she hurriedly lowered her head to conceal her reaction.","She presented the Crown Prince with her most graceful bearing and her most beautiful angle, her voice as gentle as flowing water. “This concubine, Liu, pays her respects to the Crown Prince. May Your Highness enjoy peace and good health. I arrived late—please forgive me, Your Highness.”","Listening to that melodious, lilting little voice, Shen Yanshui had to admit that its tone was rather pleasant.","Cui Yu glanced sideways at her, said, “Rise,” and then turned back to Shen Yanshui, signaling for her to continue.","Lady Liu immediately bit her lip. A sour twinge rose in her heart, and she was filled with regret and frustration.","Shen Yanshui spoke in a bright, cheerful voice. “Your Highness, the weather is fair and pleasant today. I had nothing else to do, so I rearranged the room. Would Your Highness like to go inside and take a look?”","Cui Yu nodded. When he raised his eyes, he noticed that the courtyard, which had previously been somewhat bare, now contained quite a few new additions.","Outside the window of the eastern heated chamber stood a large, lush banana plant with broad green leaves. In front of it, Shen Yanshui had used stones to build a long, winding pond about the height of a table. Its irregular edges followed the natural shapes of the stones, giving it a charmingly rustic appeal.","Shen Yanshui smiled, her eyes curving into crescents. “Although this courtyard is called Lotus Heart Court, I noticed there wasn’t a single place for growing lotuses anywhere around it. So I had the Office of Palace Affairs build this little pond. Not only have we put several fish in it, but we’ve also planted lotus seeds. Before long, we should be able to enjoy the sight of lotuses in full bloom.”","As she spoke, she saw that he showed no sign of impatience and even seemed somewhat interested, so she ushered him into the room with a smile.","She had always been especially fond of spacious, bright apartments with floor-to-ceiling windows. Back at the Earl of Zhongyi’s residence, she had arranged her own bedchamber according to her preferences from the very beginning. Now that she had moved somewhere new, she naturally intended to redecorate it as well.","The moment they entered, the view brightened.","The room’s original furnishings were no different from those of any ordinary chamber. But the heavy screens that had once separated the main hall from the eastern and western heated chambers had disappeared, leaving the space far more open—and much better ventilated.","Just then, a spring breeze swept through, carrying in the faint, fresh scent of grass and trees from outside. Even her stifled mood seemed to ease a little.","The ordinary potted plants that had stood on the narrow-waisted tall stands on either side of the entrance had been replaced with exquisitely woven bamboo baskets, each filled with flowers.","Unlike the extravagant, rare, and costly peonies, peony-like flowers, tuberoses, and begonias commonly used in the other palace chambers, these were simply an assortment of flowers and plants.","There were the most ordinary pink and white primroses, hyacinths, daffodils, and two little flowers whose names he did not know. They were not particularly precious, but they were fresh and elegant all the same, pleasing to the eye.","Incense burned within the room. Its fragrance was gentle and unhurried rather than overpowering, carrying a hint of the fresh scent of sweet orange. He could not help showing a trace of surprise and turned to ask, “What incense are you burning?”","It was not the dragon’s-breath incense, sandalwood, or pinewood scents commonly used in the palace, nor was it like the various floral fragrances favored by women. It seemed to have a faintly invigorating effect as well.","Shen Yanshui replied with a smile, “Your Highness, it’s an incense blend I made myself. I added orange peel and a little mint.”","Seeing her smiling so brightly as she spoke, Cui Yu unconsciously smiled as well. “Acceptable.”","Having received his praise, Shen Yanshui was in a good mood too.","The furnishings in the eastern heated chamber had not changed much from before. It still contained all the necessary furniture, but several soft cushions of various shapes had been added to the couch. The lattice window beside it stood wide open, with a layer of gauzy, fragrant cloud-silk curtains hanging inside that could be drawn from side to side.","At present, the curtains were half open. On the windowsill sat a delicately carved bamboo tube holding two fresh, verdant bamboo sprigs.","At another corner of the open lattice window hung a little wind chime strung with beautiful shells and pearls of various colors. Sunlight spilled across it as a gentle breeze stirred the air, sending the delicate, pleasant chimes tinkling into the room. In an instant, an atmosphere of tranquil serenity arose.","“Not bad.” Cui Yu stepped forward and sat down on the couch. His previously troubled thoughts inexplicably settled, replaced by a faint sense of calm and drowsiness.","Shen Yanshui watched the languid look that had emerged between his brows, staring at him intently for several moments.","As expected, when a man was handsome, even his lazy, relaxed expression looked exceptionally good.","Cui Yu lazily lifted his eyes and glanced at her.","Shen Yanshui blinked at once, her gaze clear and bright, her expression utterly innocent and natural. Then, with her eyes shifting coquettishly, she suddenly turned the tables on him. “Your Highness, why are you looking at me like that? You’re making me blush.”","Cui Yu: “......”","Zheng Yuande, who was waiting nearby: “???”","Although Lady Shen’s delicate, coquettish tone seemed perfectly fitting, there was somehow something a little strange about it.","Cui Yu gazed at her lively expression. He was startled at first, but then, for some inexplicable reason, he suddenly felt like laughing.","And he did let out a soft laugh.","Zheng Yuande was secretly astonished.","He turned his eyes toward the exceptionally beautiful Lady Shen, whose face always seemed to be lit by a cheerful smile, and thought to himself that it was no wonder. Anyone looking at such a pleasing smile would naturally feel a little happier as well.","This Lady Shen... seemed rather extraordinary.","“Gurgle~”","A faint sound suddenly reached both their ears. Cui Yu’s gaze instinctively dropped downward.","Shen Yanshui immediately covered her stomach.","Cui Yu looked up at her, one brow raised. “Hungry?”","Shen Yanshui nodded without hesitation. With a smile pressing at the corners of her lips, she replied, “Your Highness, I’ve been busy all day. It’s just about time for dinner now. Shall we have the meal brought in first?”","Seeing how naturally she changed expressions, Cui Yu raised a brow. Her stomach was growling loudly—something that ought to have been embarrassing—but her manner and tone were so candid that it somehow wasn’t.","“Bring in the meal.”","With the Crown Prince present, dinner was considerably more lavish than when Shen Yanshui ordered food for herself. Most importantly, she could eat as much as she wanted for free!","As a result, the smile never left her face.","The kitchen had prepared such dishes as Boiled Gold and Jade, Red-Silk Boiled Cakes—the noodles kneaded together with shrimp meat, giving them a pinkish hue, with a light yet wonderfully fresh flavor—as well as braised perch, chicken-and-vermicelli soup, three-colored shredded tripe, mutton bones, roasted venison, and several portions of seasonal greens and fruit.","At a glance, everything looked light and delicate. There was not a single chili pepper in sight, nor even the hint of a spicy aroma.","Still, she had never tried the Eastern Palace’s cooking before, so she was full of anticipation and ate with her usual enthusiasm and delight.","She sampled every dish without missing a single one. She even ate quite a lot of the mutton and mutton bones, despite never having been particularly fond of them. The only thing she managed to restrain was the urge to pick up a bone and gnaw on it directly with her hands.","She ate until she was thoroughly satisfied, putting away four hearty bowls of rice in succession. Zheng Yuande, who was serving nearby, was left dumbfounded, while Chunping’s eyes nearly twitched themselves out of their sockets from all the frantic hints she was giving.","Unfortunately, those hints were being sent to a blind woman. Shen Yanshui did not notice them at all—and even if she had, she would never have starved herself for the sake of appearances or dignity.","Cui Yu was naturally surprised as well. People of the time esteemed refined elegance, and women in particular often pursued slender figures as delicate as willow branches swaying in the breeze. As a result, they generally ate very little. Watching them eat had always ruined his appetite, leaving him feeling as though everything he consumed was bland and tasteless.","Lady Shen, on the other hand, could make an ordinary meal seem like a rare delicacy. Her expressions were so vivid and amusing that merely watching her was enough to whet one’s appetite. The only trouble was that... before one knew it, one ended up eating a little more than usual.","Once the two of them had rinsed their mouths and washed their hands, the palace attendants quickly cleared the table.","Taking a walk after a meal to aid digestion was Shen Yanshui’s habit, and today was no exception. But with the two of them together, they ought to find something to talk about. Just as she was racking her brains for a topic, a faint, plaintive melody suddenly drifted into her ears.","She instinctively asked softly, “Where is that qin music coming from?”","There was no need for anyone else to answer. After listening for only a moment, she recognized its source: the courtyard next door.","She had a pretty good idea who it was and could not help smiling.","Catching the smile on her face, Cui Yu glanced at her. “What are you smiling about?”","Shen Yanshui’s eyes curved with amusement. “I was just thinking that taking a walk while listening to this music is rather pleasant.”","Cui Yu said, “Pleasant?”","As if on cue, the melody suddenly changed. A winding, sorrowful quality filled the air, and the space between his brows twitched uncontrollably. He frowned and cast a cold glance at Zheng Yuande.","Zheng Yuande’s plump body immediately moved forward. Reacting with great speed, he turned around and ordered, “Go see who is playing the qin. How dare they disturb His Highness’s ears for no reason?”","An eunuch hurriedly acknowledged the order and rushed out. Before long, the music stopped.","Seeing the glance the Crown Prince had given him, Shen Yanshui could not help feeling a little sheepish. She had not expected the Crown Prince to have such exacting standards when it came to music. She genuinely thought Lady Wu’s playing had sounded quite lovely.","Back when she had been in the Palace of Gathering Elegance, even the palace matron had praised her qin skills.","After their walk, the sky gradually darkened, and the two of them returned to their chambers.","The western side hall opposite them kept a close watch on the Crown Prince’s every move. Seeing them return, Yinping entered the room and reported the matter in a low voice.","Lady Liu closed the window beside the couch with controlled force, her expression unpleasant.","No matter how envious she felt, she had just been given a warning by what had happened earlier. She had naturally heard the commotion from Lady Wu’s chambers next door, separated by only a single wall, but she did not dare do anything.","Hearing the sound of water being summoned from the eastern side hall, she felt a surge of resentment. Secretly gritting her teeth, she thought, “She is relying on nothing but her looks. His Highness is hardly such a shallow man. This freshness will only last a few days. Once the novelty wears off, His Highness will surely recognize my virtues...”","Whether the Crown Prince was shallow or not, Shen Yanshui did not know. But she felt that she certainly was—greedy for both food and beauty.","And there was one more thing she wanted to confirm."]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: Reward","paragraphs":["Compared with the night before, Shen Yanshui felt that the Crown Prince was proving remarkably quick to learn. As a result, the pleasure they shared—or perhaps the pleasure her body experienced—had grown all the more intense.","After this encounter, she was certain of it: whenever she and the Crown Prince became one, the faint supernatural ability within her would automatically begin circulating. It made her feel as though she were absorbing his yang energy to nourish her yin.","Bah. Judging by the Crown Prince’s condition, it was clearly more like dual cultivation.","The time they spent together seemed to have grown longer, too...","She simply couldn’t understand why this was happening.","Little by little, she began to enjoy it. At first, she had still forced herself to remember the rules and keep her voice down.","But later, all she could remember was the lean, muscular body beneath her, its smooth lines concealing powerful, explosive strength, while hot sweat rolled down...","The next morning, when Shen Yanshui opened her eyes, the person beside her was already gone. She wasn’t surprised. But when she saw the bedding, fresh and completely changed, she remembered the sheets that had been removed the night before—drenched in moisture, marked with patches of varying shades, and covered in all sorts of chaotic traces.","Her waist felt even more sore and weak than it had the previous night. She shifted position, closed her eyes, and gathered her focus. After sensing the supernatural ability within her and skillfully circulating it through her body once, the weariness gradually faded. When she opened her eyes again, she felt refreshed and invigorated.","According to the ranking system of her previous life, she had only just reached the early stage of Rank One.","There were no crystal cores from animals or plants in this world for her to absorb and use to advance. She could only cultivate by drawing upon the faint energy in nature and following the energy-circulation method promoted by the authorities in her previous life. She had no idea how long it would take before she could break through to Rank Two.","Only upon reaching Rank Two would her strength against enemies improve by leaps and bounds.","Otherwise, all she could do was regulate the body and slowly hasten the growth of plants.","“Why has the mistress sat up?”","Chunping came around the screen. Before she had time to be surprised by Shen Yanshui’s posture, she saw the quilt casually wrapped around her mistress. Through the slightly open gap, the marks beneath that fair collarbone were clearly visible, and Chunping’s cheeks flushed faintly.","Shen Yanshui asked about the Crown Prince. After learning that, just as yesterday, he had left at the third quarter of the Hour of the Tiger, she wasn’t surprised. Once she confirmed that the Crown Prince truly held no displeasure toward her laziness in the morning, she simply allowed herself to fall back asleep.","She threw off the quilt and rose. Since she had just circulated her supernatural ability, she did not feel cold.","Although this was not the first time Chunping had seen her, she still couldn’t help flushing and feeling her heart race at the sight of her mistress’s fair, delicate, shapely body.","Especially the peach-colored undergarment before her, which seemed barely able to contain...","Chunping dared not look any longer. She hurriedly and deftly helped her mistress get dressed.","Once everything was in order, she studied Shen Yanshui carefully before saying softly, “Mistress, the size of your undergarments and clothes seems to be a little small. Shall I have Xia’an and the others make you two new outfits?”","Shen Yanshui also glanced at herself in the mirror. The front of her bodice did seem a little tighter than before. The few outfits she currently owned had all been newly made by her birth mother’s embroiderers before she entered the palace, according to her measurements.","“Forget it. I expect the weather will grow warmer soon. We can save the fabric and use it to make summer clothes later.”","The clothing of the Great Yong Dynasty fell somewhere between the styles of the Tang and Song eras of her previous life. There were high-waisted ruqun skirts and waist-high ruqun skirts, as well as beizi jackets, half-sleeved garments, and wide-sleeved outer robes. A single set of spring clothing required quite a lot of fabric.","She received fabric as part of her monthly allotment, but not much. Given her rank, it would not be anything particularly fine, and it was nowhere near as comfortable as what she was wearing now.","As soon as she finished speaking, a commotion came from outside. Xia’an hurried into the inner room, her face full of delight, and whispered, “Mistress, please come out quickly to receive the decree. Her Majesty the Empress has sent gifts!”","Shen Yanshui did not dare delay. Seeing Matron Zhao, a familiar face from the courtyard, she knelt according to protocol and waited to hear the decree. Lady Liu had already knelt down as well.","Matron Zhao discreetly looked Lady Shen over carefully. Only after everyone had gathered did she smile and say, “By Her Majesty the Empress’s oral decree: to Crown Prince Lady Shen, a pair of gold pomegranate-patterned ruyi hairpins, a pair of tortoiseshell bracelets set with gold and jade beads, one bolt of brocade satin, two bolts of cloud satin, and two bolts of plain gauze.”","“To Crown Prince Lady Liu, a pair of jade butterfly hairpins set in gold, a pair of silver ruyi hairpins with pomegranate designs, two bolts of cloud satin, one bolt of blue plain satin, and one bolt of plain gauze.”","Having finished, Matron Zhao looked at the two women with a smile. “May you both conduct yourselves properly, observe your duties, and ease the burdens of His Highness the Crown Prince. May you soon bear branches and leaves for His Highness and extend his line.”","Shen Yanshui kowtowed and offered her thanks. “Thank you for Her Majesty’s gifts. I shall respectfully heed Her Majesty’s instructions.”","Lady Liu naturally kowtowed and gave thanks as well. However, when she heard that Lady Shen had received the additional tortoiseshell bracelet set with gold and jade and the brocade satin, she couldn’t help feeling a pang of jealousy.","The bracelet was one thing, but the brocade satin was an exceptionally fine material. Even the daily allotments of low-ranking consorts like them did not include it.","And yet... as she looked at Lady Shen, whose clothes had always been made from fine materials, her mood grew even more sour.","Without Shen Yanshui needing to say anything, Chunping smiled and slipped a purse into Matron Zhao’s hands. Silver Screen followed immediately after. This was an unspoken rule in the palace.","As someone trusted by Her Majesty the Empress, Matron Zhao naturally did not care about this small amount of silver, but she accepted it with a smile nonetheless.","Shen Yanshui said warmly, “You’ve gone to such trouble, Matron. Why not come inside and have a cup of tea and rest your feet?”","Matron Zhao smiled. “Thank you, Lady Shen, but I’m afraid I must decline. Her Majesty the Empress is waiting for me to report back. This servant will take her leave.”","Shen Yanshui inclined herself in a half-bow and returned the courtesy with a smile. “Then I won’t keep you today. Chunping, see Matron Zhao out.”","“Yes, mistress.”","With a smile on her face, Chunping bowed and said, “Matron, this way, please.”","After Chunping escorted Matron Zhao away, Shen Yanshui looked at the jewelry and bolts of fabric set aside nearby, unable to contain her delight. Afraid she might laugh outright, she exchanged a few words with Lady Liu before turning and returning to the room.","Only after there were no outsiders present did she finally laugh.","Looking at the “silver” that had come to her for free, she sincerely sighed, “Her Majesty the Empress truly has the heart of a bodhisattva. She really is a wonderful person. May Her Majesty enjoy good health and happiness, and live to a hundred years!”","*","“Did she really say that?”","The Empress looked rather surprised.","Matron Zhao, who was reporting in the hall, replied respectfully, “In answer to Your Majesty, that Lady Shen did indeed say those words.”","The Empress had originally been surprised to learn that the Crown Prince had not gone first to Lady Zhang’s residence. She was even more astonished when she discovered that he had spent both nights in a row in Lady Shen’s room.","That was why, taking advantage of the customary distribution of gifts to the palace’s new arrivals, she had deliberately sent Matron Zhao on this trip.","The Empress asked, “What do you think of this Lady Shen, Matron Zhao?”","Matron Zhao replied respectfully, “In answer to Your Majesty, this servant feels that Lady Shen’s temperament is rather unlike that of Lady Shen the Jieyu, despite the two of them being sisters.”","She did not beat around the bush and continued with a smile, “Lady Shen the Jieyu is clearly a high-born noblewoman at first glance. Although she is accomplished in music, chess, calligraphy, and painting, she cannot help being somewhat competitive, proud, and haughty.”","As she spoke, the image of Lady Shen came to mind. No matter the occasion, she always wore a bright smile, as though nothing in the world could trouble her. Lady Shen had also once taught the palace rules to the young women in the Palace of Gathered Elegance, so Matron Zhao knew her to some extent.","“As for Lady Shen, she doesn’t appear to be a complicated or scheming person. Back when she was in the Palace of Gathered Elegance, the thing she cared most about each day was what she would eat and drink. Her temperament is somewhat mild and placid. From what I saw today, Lady Shen is still much the same as before. I couldn’t discern any changes in her.”","The Empress was somewhat surprised. Still, she had considerable faith in Matron Zhao’s judgment of people. Lady Shen was merely the daughter of a concubine from the Loyal Righteous Earl’s manor, and it was hardly strange that her temperament differed from that of her legitimate elder sister.","With that, she let the matter go and paid it no further mind. At the end of the day, she trusted her son more. He was not some fool who would lose his head over a woman; he knew perfectly well what he ought to do and what he ought not.","*","Zheng Yuande waited until the Crown Prince and the two officials had finally finished discussing official matters. Only after the others had withdrawn did he quietly step forward and report, “Your Highness, the Crown Princess’s gifts have also been delivered.”","Cui Yu took a sip of tea to moisten his throat. His long, well-defined fingers rubbed the smooth, delicate surface of the celadon cup in his palm. After a moment, he raised his eyes and ordered, “Open the private treasury and select some things to send to Lady Shen.”","“Ah?” Zheng Yuande froze for an instant. When he caught the glance his master cast in his direction, he hurriedly smiled and said, “Yes, Your Highness. I’ll have someone see to it at once.”","Cui Yu suddenly seemed to think of something. “Wait.”","“Your Highness?”","Cui Yu said, “Choose several bolts of fine fabric as well and send them over.”"]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: Happily Accepting Them All","paragraphs":["Zheng Yuande obediently acknowledged the order without letting his lips lag, but inwardly, he was rather astonished.","His Highness had never been particularly interested in women. Naturally, he paid even less attention to the secondary consorts in the inner palace. The affairs of court already kept His Highness busy enough; he truly had little time or inclination to concern himself with women.","Moreover, although His Highness was the Crown Prince and possessed the most exalted status, he was neither extravagant nor wasteful in his daily expenditures. In fact, he was quite frugal. As for the secondary consorts in the inner palace, he had always rewarded them according to the rules, with very few additional gifts.","For instance, when Her Majesty the Empress and the Crown Princess bestowed gifts upon a newcomer according to custom, Lady Shen—having only just attended His Highness—would naturally receive somewhat more than the others, both as a sign of favor and as befitted the Crown Princess’s graciousness.","Yet this time, His Highness had not only given additional gifts but had specifically ordered that some fine fabrics be selected...","Zheng Yuande was rather puzzled. Had His Highness forgotten Lady Shen’s identity, or did he simply not care about it at all?","Naturally, Cui Yu could not possibly have forgotten Shen Yanshui’s identity. It was just that...","To him, Shen Yanshui was merely a woman whose temperament and appearance, at present, were not unpleasant and were even somewhat pleasing to the eye.","If any random woman could make him regard the situation as a grave threat, he might as well hand over the position of Crown Prince to someone else.","*","When Shen Yanshui received the Crown Prince’s gifts, she felt that her eyes had practically turned into sparkling stars from smiling so much that day.","One reward after another—there was so much to delight in that it was almost dazzling!","This time, Zheng Yuande had come in person. Seeing Lady Shen looking radiant, her brilliant smile blooming like a flower, even he could not help but stare for a moment. He then greeted her with a beaming smile. “This servant pays his respects to Your Ladyship.”","Shen Yanshui shifted slightly to the side and stepped forward to return half the courtesy with a sincere smile. Only then did she say, “Eunuch Zheng, you are too polite. What brings you here in person?”","Eunuch Zheng answered cheerfully, “This servant has come especially to convey His Highness’s verbal decree.”","This was the third time Shen Yanshui had knelt that day. However, if kneeling once earned her so many wonderful things, she felt that her knees were actually quite sturdy. She could withstand a few more kneelings without any trouble!","As with the previous two rewards, the formalities began with a few official-sounding words of praise. Only then did Eunuch Zheng recite the list of gifts:","“...one pair of jade-inlaid gold ruyi scepters; one set of hair ornaments adorned with red coral and pearls; one bolt of Floating Light silk; one bolt of Soft Mist gauze; one bolt of cicada-wing gauze; one bolt of snow satin; one bolt of scattered-flower damask; two bolts of plain gauze; and two bolts of blue plain satin.”","As Shen Yanshui listened to that long list of exquisite fabrics, she instinctively lifted her eyes to look at Zheng Yuande in astonishment—only to see his plump, fair, round face beaming with a genial smile.","“These were all specially selected for you by His Highness the Crown Prince. Your Ladyship, please rise,” he said.","His Highness had personally instructed him to choose some fine fabrics, so naturally he had not dared cut corners. He had even deliberately selected lightweight, high-quality materials. As for the last few bolts of plain gauze and satin, even if Lady Shen had no use for them, she could always give them to her servants.","Upon hearing this, Shen Yanshui thanked His Highness for the gifts and slowly rose to her feet. She then exchanged a few more sincere pleasantries with him before seeing him off and returning indoors.","Only then did she begin examining the gifts bestowed by the Crown Prince one by one. The snow satin and scattered-flower damask were one thing, but fabrics such as shimmering brocade, soft mist gauze, and cicada-wing silk were not only scarce but exceedingly expensive.","She had never been particularly demanding when it came to clothing. Among the sisters in her family, she had only ever seen her legitimate elder sister wear such costly and beautiful fabrics.","A short while later, Quanfu returned after seeing Zheng Yuande off. Dongyi and Quanshou stood guard outside the door, while Chunping brought over a cup of warm tea.","“My lady, please rest and have some tea.”","Shen Yanshui sat on the daybed and drank more than half the cup. Lost in thought, she lightly tapped the side table with her fingertips. After a long moment, she suddenly raised her eyes and asked, “What gifts did Her Majesty the Empress, the Crown Princess, and the Crown Prince bestow upon the other residences today?”","Quanfu immediately broke into a smile. “In reply to my lady, this servant paid close attention today. Her Majesty the Empress’s gifts to the various ladies of the Eastern Palace were mostly distributed according to their rank and established palace custom. However... the gifts the Crown Princess gave you were two degrees more lavish than those sent to Lady Zhang and Lady Wu. By now, the other courtyards have most likely heard of it as well.”","“But the Crown Prince’s gifts were sent only to our courtyard.”","As soon as Quanfu finished speaking, the expressions of master and servants alike changed.","A flicker of surprise appeared in Shen Yanshui’s eyes. As for the Crown Princess’s gifts, she had already understood the situation from the two remarks Matron Zhou had deliberately made when delivering them.","The Crown Princess wanted to set her up as a target for everyone else—and even expected her to feel grateful for it.","At first, however, the Crown Princess had probably intended to use Lady Wu as that target.","As for the Crown Prince’s gifts, though they suddenly made her look even more like the conspicuous one, what was she supposed to do now that they had arrived? Throw them out?","Of course she would accept them happily!","Qiuru gazed at the room full of exquisite, costly fabrics, gold, silver, and jewels, her face beaming. “His Highness the Crown Prince treats you so well, my lady. He bestowed gifts on you alone. It is clear that His Highness holds you in his heart.”","Shen Yanshui looked at the lavish gifts filling the room and smiled faintly, not taking Qiuru’s words to heart.","Rather than believing that the Crown Prince held her in his heart, she would sooner guess that their nightly activities over the past two evenings had become increasingly harmonious, and that the Crown Prince had been quite pleased—hence these rewards.","“All right, put everything away.”","“Yes, my lady.”","Quanfu led the others in sorting the gifts and placing them in the storeroom. Chunping, however, said with a smile, “This is wonderful. With so much fabric, we can make several more outfits for you, my lady.”","Now that there was more than enough material, Shen Yanshui naturally did not mind having a few more clothes made. “Then make two sets of spring clothes first, and four sets for summer. It is indeed time to prepare summer garments.”","Chunping agreed with a broad smile.","*","The Crown Princess was the first to learn that the Crown Prince had bestowed gifts upon Lady Shen alone, and her expression immediately darkened.","“What does the Crown Prince mean by this?”","Matron Zhou also furrowed her brow. In the past, the matter of distributing gifts among the various courtyards had always been decided by the Crown Princess. The Crown Prince had never intervened before.","“Your Highness, please do not be anxious. Lady Shen’s status is plain for all to see. His Highness the Crown Prince is wise and discerning; he must have his own considerations. Perhaps there is some deeper meaning behind his deliberate bestowal of gifts.”","The Crown Princess’s brows remained faintly furrowed, showing no sign of relaxing. It was all because of Lady Shen’s face—far too striking, far too threatening for her to ignore.","Matron Zhou smiled and soothed her. “Though Lady Shen was blessed with a fine appearance, she is shallow-minded, greedy for food and money. And look at how, after receiving the Crown Prince’s favor for the first time yesterday, she quarreled with Lady Wu and made such a spectacle of her. Even if she has caught His Highness’s eye, it will only be a passing novelty. It cannot last.”","After thinking it over, the Crown Princess’s expression eased somewhat. “By now, I imagine the others have all heard as well. I would like to see whether she can bear the consequences.”","*","The moment Eunuch Zheng, the Crown Prince’s chief personal attendant, entered the rear chambers with the rewards, the rest of the household learned of it before long.","Still, no one was truly foolish. Today, Her Majesty the Empress, the Crown Prince, and the Crown Princess had all bestowed gifts upon them. Whatever they might think in private, they could not make a move now—would that not amount to displaying dissatisfaction with their superiors?","As a result, Shen Yanshui spent several peaceful days without incident. During that time, the Crown Prince did not return to Lotus Heart Court.","Every day, she slept until she woke naturally. After rising and having breakfast, she would practice a set of the Eight Brocades indoors to loosen her body, then stroll through the garden—the place within the entire Eastern Palace with the most flowers and greenery.","At the moment, she sat on a swing in the garden, casually plucking a red apricot blossom bud. In the space of a single breath, as her wrist turned, the bud in her palm had fully bloomed into a pink-white apricot flower. Its petals unfurled, carrying a faint fragrance.","Dongyi smiled in surprise. “Mistress, your eyesight is truly excellent. This servant thought that seemed to be the only apricot blossom in bloom.”","Shen Yanshui looked at the pink-white flower resting quietly in her palm and smiled in excellent spirits. “My luck is rather good. Later, order a few more dishes from the kitchen.”","Her cultivation over the past few days had yielded modest results, but... compared with the effects of “dual cultivation” with the Crown Prince, it still fell far short.","“Yes, Mistress.” Dongyi was delighted at the words. Their mistress had always been generous, especially where food was concerned. Every time, she would order an extra dish, and whatever remained uneaten would be shared among them, allowing them to enjoy meat almost every day.","Not to mention the assorted pastries—her mistress was never stingy with those, either.","The meals provided to palace maids and eunuchs were generally large-pot fare prepared by apprentices. How good could such food possibly be? It was already fortunate if it merely kept them from going hungry.","If they wished to eat better, they had to spend their own silver to have the kitchen prepare something separately. Even then, it was nowhere near as fine as the meals their mistress ate every day.","“It smells so good, so good!” A sudden, somewhat peculiar voice rang out. Dongyi had barely lifted her head when she saw a beautiful little bird, emerald green all over with a touch of orange-red on its forehead, dart past and snatch the pink-white apricot blossom from her mistress’s palm in a flash.","“Ah! That bird—” Dongyi regretted not noticing it sooner and chasing it away. It had nearly startled her mistress.","“It’s nothing.” Shen Yanshui watched the pretty little parrot fly onto an apricot blossom branch and begin pecking eagerly at the petals of the flower she had ripened with her ability. She could not help smiling. Plucking another leaf, she infused it with a trace of her power and laid it in her palm before holding out her hand. “Come here.”","The little parrot had eaten every last petal and even the flower’s center. Hearing her voice, it cocked its head at her. Its tiny, bead-like eyes fixed on the tender leaf in her palm, and it immediately swaggered over on broad little wings. “Like it! I like it!”","Dongyi stared in surprise. “Mistress, this bird can actually speak? Is it... a parrot?”","Shen Yanshui nodded with a smile. “It is.” And clearly one that had been well cared for by someone, though she had no idea who its owner was. “It’s rather adorable.”","“Rather adorable! I’m rather adorable! Greetings to Your Highness, may you enjoy ten thousand blessings and peace! Ten thousand blessings and peace! Food, food! Give me more, give me more!”","Dongyi burst out laughing. “Mistress, this parrot is truly amusing.”","“Amusing, amusing! More, more!”","“You mustn’t eat too much of this.” Smiling, Shen Yanshui stroked the glossy feathers of the little parrot, which was obviously exceptionally well looked after, then gently rubbed its forehead.","The parrot contentedly pressed its forehead against her fingertip. “More, more!”","“Who’s making such a racket up ahead? How utterly lacking in manners.”","“Oh~ Who do we have here? Why, it’s Sister Shen...” Lady Wu approached in a begonia-colored, vine-patterned, fitted three-panel skirt, with a powder-white trimmed short jacket over it. A round fan rested in one hand while the other lay lightly on her maid’s arm, her every step graceful and poised.","Shen Yanshui’s expression remained calm as she bowed. “Greetings, Lady Wu.”","“Sister Shen, you’ve been rather free lately, haven’t you? You come to the garden every day to pass the time. As for me, I’ve been busy attending to His Highness the Crown Prince, and it feels as though I haven’t seen you in ages. Who would have thought we’d happen to meet today? What a very fortunate coincidence.”","She leisurely fanned herself. Only after she had finished speaking did she seem to realize that Shen Yanshui was still bowing. She raised her fan to her lips in exaggerated surprise. “Oh my, Sister, why are you still kneeling there? Get up, get up.”","Shen Yanshui inwardly raised a brow at Lady Wu’s theatrical performance. Such petty attempts to make things difficult for her hardly amounted to anything. So long as no one expected her to put on a performance in return, she could not be bothered to care.","Dongyi’s lips pressed into a tight line, her expression darkening. The moment she rose, she hurried to help her mistress up.","Shen Yanshui said, “Then I shall not disturb you any longer.” She could go back and prepare for dinner now; there was no need to waste time on someone unimportant.","“Wait.” Lady Wu extended her fan to block her path. Chin slightly raised, she looked at Shen Yanshui from the corner of her eye. “Why are you in such a hurry, Sister? You’ll only be going back to an empty room all alone. What fun is that? Why not stay and chat with me?”","Over the past ten days or so, His Highness the Crown Prince had visited the rear quarters only twice in total: once to Lady Zhang’s rooms, and once to hers. Yet two or three days had already passed, and there had been no reward or gift from His Highness, which only made her feel increasingly unsettled."]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: Birds Fly, People Jump","paragraphs":["\"Oh? What business does Lady Wu have to discuss with me?\" Shen Yanshui's tone was flat, sounding almost perfunctory, yet no one could point to any outright disrespect in her words even if they tried.","Lady Wu's eyebrows pinched together slightly, before she let out a proud cold snort. \"The Dragon Boat Festival is just a few days away. Every year on this occasion, His Majesty and the Empress lead the entire imperial court and the inner palace to the Jinling Pond to watch the dragon boat races. I've heard it's an incredibly lively, spectacular event.\"","She glanced at Shen Yanshui as she spoke, her tone thick with undisguised smugness. \"Every year, the Crown Princess brings two companions with her to the event. Just yesterday, the Crown Princess specifically mentioned this to me. It's such a pity, though—it seems this year, younger sister won't have the good fortune to attend.\"","Shen Yanshui lifted an eyebrow in response, but before she could say a word, a familiar bird cry rang out of nowhere.","\"Shut up, so noisy, so noisy!\"","Lady Wu's face immediately darkened. She pointed furiously at the little creature darting around over her head, daring to scold her out loud. \"Insolent thing!\"","She spun around and snapped at the palace maids and eunuchs waiting at her side. \"You fools! What are you all standing around for? Hurry up and knock this little beast down!\"","\"Help! Help!\" The bird's cry was piercingly loud, sending the whole scene into chaos of flapping wings and panicking people.","\"Little me is so scared! Danger, danger! Fly fast, fly fast!\"","Shen Yanshui: \"......\" The person who raised this little parrot must be a total chatterbox.","She had originally been thinking of helping the little creature out, but seeing how high and fast it was flying, she relaxed. Though this little thing was undeniably a little annoying in its cheekiness.","\"Someone come, someone come! Ugly people are trying to kill the bird! Kill the bird! Save the bird's life! Save the bird's life!\"","Lady Wu was so angry she nearly lost all her poise. \"Use stones! Smash this little beast down!\"","One of the palace maids looked worried, leaning over to whisper in her ear. \"My lady, this parrot clearly belongs to someone of status. If we really injure it...\"","No one who served close to their master in the palace was truly stupid. These little creatures, if they belonged to the right master, were far more valuable than the lives of ordinary palace maids and eunuchs. No one dared to actually lay a heavy hand on it.","Lady Wu barely listened to her personal maid's reminder, but she still frowned tightly, holding back her anger until her chest ached. \"Fine, forget it...\"","Plop. Something warm landed right on her forehead.","Shen Yanshui watched with her own eyes as a small, unmistakably stinky blob of droppings landed right on Lady Wu's forehead. She stared as Lady Wu lifted her hand in bewilderment, and then touched a whole handful of...","\"Ah——!\" The second Lady Wu realized what had landed on her forehead, she broke down and screamed at the top of her lungs.","\"Kill this little beast! Kill it!\" Her face twisted with unbearable disgust, she scrubbed at her forehead frantically with her handkerchief.","\"M-My lady...\" The several maids and eunuchs had never expected such a bizarre coincidence. Faced with their master who had clearly lost her mind in rage, the three of them were flustered for a moment, unsure what to do.","Smack! Lady Wu slapped the palace maid standing in front of her hard across the face. \"What are you all still gawking at?! If you don't kill this little beast today, I'll have the Crown Princess send every last one of you to the Palace Supervisor's Office!\"","Shen Yanshui had just started to frown, about to step in, when the sound of approaching footsteps reached her ears.","\"Who are you sending to the Palace Supervisor's Office?\"","The man who stepped into view wore a dark black informal robe embroidered with subtle silver cloud and thunder patterns, his hair held back by a jade crown, a leather belt cinching his waist. His voice was low and icy, radiating a bone-deep cold that made people want to shrink back the moment they laid eyes on him.","It was none other than the Crown Prince.","In an instant, everyone in the vicinity had knelt to the ground.","\"Little me is scared to death! Scared to death! Your Highness is blessed, Your Highness ten thousand blessings!\" The little parrot landed right on his shoulder, squawking noisily.","Cui Yu frowned instinctively.","Shen Yanshui curtsied in greeting. \"This servant greets Your Highness, may Your Highness be well.\" She wondered if he had just happened to arrive, or if he had been watching from the shadows for a while, and a faint wariness rose in her chest.","She had never expected this cheeky, loudmouthed little parrot to belong to the Crown Prince...","Lady Wu's face flushed bright red then drained of color, then flushed again. A faint dark stain still marked her forehead, ruining her once beguiling, begonia-like beauty and making her look utterly disheveled.","\"Your Highness...\" Tears began to roll down Lady Wu's cheeks like a broken string of pearls, her voice trembling, sounding so pitiable.","But Cui Yu was completely unmoved, not the slightest bit swayed. The look he gave her was nothing short of impatient.","Face burning, Lady Wu bit her lip. \"Your Highness, please forgive me. I had no idea this parrot was yours. It was only because... because...\"","She could not bring herself to admit out loud in front of the Crown Prince that the bird had defecated on her forehead, and she ended up sobbing in frustration. \"Your Highness, I truly did not mean any harm. That bird offended me first, I simply lost my composure for a moment.\"","\"Bad person! Bad person!\" The parrot squawked on.","Cui Yu suddenly frowned, and said coolly, \"Shut up, noisy thing.\"","Shen Yanshui: \"......\" Alright, that explained it. The bird really did learn that line from its master.","This time, the parrot stopped its cheeky squawking, pacing back and forth on his shoulder in silence. It clearly had plenty of practice behaving itself when told off.","Cui Yu glanced at the palace maid kneeling on the ground, one side of her face already swelling up bright red, and his brows twitched slightly.","He had been walking along the corridor outside the Fangyao Garden when he heard his familiar parrot cry \"Help——\" so he had come to investigate. He glanced at Lady Wu's forehead, which she had rubbed raw, then looked away, and said in a deep, steady voice, \"Help your lady back to her quarters.\"","Lady Wu heaved a huge sigh of relief. The Crown Prince had not punished her—he still cared for her!","She could not bear to stay looking like a mess in front of the Crown Prince anyway, so she blinked back her tears, her voice soft and delicate, the kind that was supposed to tug at people's heartstrings. \"Your Highness is most just. This servant takes her leave~\"","But seeing that the Crown Prince was not looking at her at all, she was left with a strange mix of feelings, half relieved that she could leave, half disappointed by his indifference.","Once everyone else had finally left, Cui Yu noticed that Shen Yanshui was still holding her curtsy. He glanced at her, reached out, wrapped his hand around her forearm, and personally helped her to her feet.","His palm met warm skin, separated only by a thin, smooth layer of fabric, and he felt a handful of soft, delicate, almost boneless softness.","Shen Yanshui tilted her head up to look at his face, and smiled. \"Thank you, Your Highness.\" Her voice was clear and melodious.","Shen Yanshui took the chance to wrap her hand around his for a moment, then stepped back with a grin. \"Did Your Highness notice? This is a new dress I made, using the Luminous Brocade that Your Highness bestowed on me. It's the first time I've ever worn such fine material. It's so comfortable and beautiful—don't you think it looks lovely on me?\"","As she spoke, she turned her body slightly to let him get a full look at it.","The moment their palms pressed together, Cui Yu felt a flicker of unfamiliarity. Just as he was about to pull his hand back, he caught sight of the bright, sunny smile on her face. He hesitated for a beat, and in the end, did not move to withdraw his hand at all.","Listening to her voice brimming with pure joy, he looked her over carefully from head to toe. The sun was gentle and bright that day, its soft glow spilling over her figure. The fabric of her dress shimmered with every small movement she made, and the graceful sway of her slender, supple waist as she turned was delicate and stunning. For a split second, his throat felt tight, and his voice dropped a little deeper, \"Yes, it looks good.\"","\"Pretty! So pretty!\" The little parrot suddenly flew from his shoulder and landed right on the pearl hairpin in her hair.","Dongyi's heart jolted with alarm! She was terrified that this parrot would blurt out one of its crude lines in front of their master too — that would be a total disaster!","Cui Yu held out his hand to the parrot with a blank, unamused expression. \"Come here.\"","\"Your Highness, blessings and prosperity! Your Highness, long life and good fortune!\" The little parrot hopped nimbly to another wooden hairpin in her hair instead, its obvious evasive manner both stubborn and cowardly at the same time.","Cui Yu frowned.","Shen Yanshui said, \"Your Highness, let me try to get it, if you would allow.\"","Cui Yu looked down and met her smiling eyes. Seeing that she was not the slightest bit frightened, he gave a low \"mm\" of assent.","Hidden by the sweep of her wide sleeve, Shen Yanshui reached out and plucked another apricot blossom bud. This time, she channeled a smaller amount of her special ability into it, and what settled in her palm in the end was a half-bloomed pink apricot blossom. \"Your Highness, what is its name?\"","Cui Yu paused for a moment, and said nothing right away.","\"I'm Little Jade! I'm Little Jade! Pretty lady, pretty lady, I'm Little Jade!\"","\"Pfft!\" Shen Yanshui could not hold back a laugh. She was amused by the deeply folksy, unrefined name Little Jade, which could not be more mismatched for the grand, regal status of the Crown Prince standing right in front of her. No wonder the man had looked like he would rather say nothing at all just a moment earlier.","Cui Yu: \"...\""]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14: Sturdy","paragraphs":["Little Jade flew to the branches of the apricot tree with a petal in her beak, then immediately lowered her head and began pecking at it furiously!","Shen Yanshui glanced over and found herself smiling. Looking at Cui Yu, who had already recovered his composure, she asked curiously, “Your Highness wasn’t the one who named Little Jade, was he?”","Cui Yu replied, “No.”","The disdain in his eyes was unmistakable, though it was tinged with a hint of helplessness. Judging from the way he had treated Little Jade just now, it was clear enough.","He had allowed Little Jade to hop onto his shoulder without the slightest reaction, looking as though he had long since grown accustomed to it. Either he truly liked birds, or he was fond of the person who had named—or given him—the parrot.","Cui Yu’s brows relaxed slightly. “My maternal uncle gave her to me three years ago. He was the one who named her, too.”","Shen Yanshui’s peach-blossom eyes curved into a smile, and her voice was light, though tinged with surprise. “I never imagined Great General Qi would be such an interesting person.”","She was rather surprised. This seemed to be the first time she had heard him refer to himself as “I.” It appeared that the Crown Prince and his maternal uncle truly were very close.","“Big Nephew! Big Nephew!”","Cui Yu’s brow twitched violently. “Zheng Yuande.”","“Give me some silver to spend! Give me some silver to spend!”","“Oh dear, my little ancestor! Come here, I have something you like to eat...” Zheng Yuande hurriedly rose onto his tiptoes and stretched out his hand, coaxing the little ancestor perched above him.","Shen Yanshui did not dare laugh this time. Pretending she had heard nothing, she cleared her throat and said, “Your Highness, it’s nearly time for the evening meal. Why don’t you return with me and dine together?”","Cui Yu glanced at her slightly curved eyes, nodded, and gave a soft “Mm” before striding away ahead of her.","Watching his unusually swift footsteps, Shen Yanshui could not help but chuckle. She had not expected this man to be capable of embarrassment. His skin was surprisingly thin.","After musing over it for a moment, she followed him.","By the time the two of them returned to Lianxin Court, everyone there had already received word and was waiting at the entrance.","“This servant pays respects to the Crown Prince. May Your Highness enjoy good fortune and peace. This servant pays respects to Our Lady.”","Cui Yu barely glanced at them. He raised a hand and said, “Rise,” completely ignoring the distinctly different voice mixed in among the others’ greetings. Without pausing, he continued straight toward the eastern side hall.","Shen Yanshui noticed that Lady Liu’s eyes had suddenly reddened. Her footsteps faltered for a moment, but she still stopped and helped her up. For a while, she did not know what to say. At a time like this, anything she said would probably sound as though she were showing off.","Lady Liu’s body stiffened slightly. She suppressed the urge to shake Shen Yanshui’s hand away, drew a small breath, and thanked her with a composed smile. “Thank you, Elder Sister. I shall not disturb you and the Crown Prince.”","She turned and returned to the western side hall with the palace servants attending her.","“Close the door!” she said quietly.","The young eunuch behind her hurriedly shut the door tight.","Lady Liu unconsciously twisted the silk handkerchief between both hands. Her eyes held shame, anger, panic, and confusion as she asked in a low voice, “Yinping, why do you think the Crown Prince didn’t even look at me?”","“Could it be... that I’m truly not worthy of catching the Crown Prince’s eye?”","As she spoke, she sat down before the dressing table. Staring at her reflection in the mirror, she absently touched her cheek. She might not be as beautiful as Lady Shen or Lady Wu, but she considered herself no less attractive than Lady Zhang. Why, then, was she the only one the Crown Prince neglected?","When she had first been bestowed upon the Crown Prince, she had been thrilled and expectant, filled with pride and conceit. Yet in the short span of half a month, her heart—once floating in the clouds—had gradually sunk back down.","Yinping said cautiously, “Your appearance is certainly not lacking. Otherwise, you would never have been chosen over so many high-born young ladies by the various esteemed consorts.”","As her mistress’s personal maid, Yinping naturally hoped that Lady Liu would win the Crown Prince’s favor. But Lady Shen’s beauty was simply too overwhelming, making her mistress seem rather dim by comparison.","Lady Liu pressed her lips together, raised a hand, and wiped away the tears on her face. There were still many days ahead. No matter how beautiful a face was, there would surely come a day when the Crown Prince grew tired of looking at it.","* * *","Shen Yanshui had already felt hungry when her ability first broke through.","Now that she was dining with the Crown Prince, not only was the food abundant, but the portions were generous as well. Her chopsticks flew back and forth so energetically that there was no need for anyone else to serve her. This made Cui Yu glance at her several times.","He had known for a long time that she had a considerably larger appetite than ordinary women. Even so, he was still slightly shocked when she finished five bowls of rice and showed no signs of stopping.","Beside her, Chunping’s eyes were practically twitching from the effort of trying to signal her mistress, yet she still failed to stop her mistress from accomplishing the feat of eating five bowls of rice in front of the Crown Prince. In the end, her eyes filled with despair.","Across the table, Zheng Yuande’s mouth had fallen open in astonishment, forming a perfect “O.”","When Shen Yanshui began filling her sixth bowl, she could no longer bear the increasingly astonished looks around her. She looked at Cui Yu with pleading eyes and said softly, “Your Highness, I’m still hungry...”","During the apocalypse, she would not have such a huge appetite whenever she had crystal cores to absorb. But at present, she had none.","She couldn’t possibly keep pretending in front of the Crown Prince just for the sake of appearances, could she?","Wouldn’t that be a loss? Why refuse free food and spend her own silver to buy more?","Although the cooks in the Eastern Palace would not make things difficult for her—in fact, they would sometimes send over a few extra fresh dishes—her appetite was simply too large.","Cui Yu glanced at her and instructed, “Tell the kitchen to prepare a few more dishes. Also, summon an imperial physician from the Imperial Medical Academy.”","Shen Yanshui fell silent. Fine, then.","She gave him a tight-lipped smile. “Thank you, Your Highness.”","After she finished her sixth bowl and set down her chopsticks, Chunping cleared the table at a speed that could only be described as astonishing.","Shen Yanshui was speechless. It seemed she had truly frightened Chunping this time.","She had barely finished a cup of tea when the imperial physician arrived.","“This subject pays respects to the Crown Prince.”","Cui Yu slightly furrowed his brows. “Rise. Examine Lady Shen.”","The imperial physician stood and acknowledged the order.","Shen Yanshui cooperatively extended her wrist. Seeing the Crown Prince’s furrowed brows, the imperial physician could not help but feel his heart tighten. He examined her pulse with even greater care.","Yet after only a short while, the vertical crease between his brows slowly smoothed out, and an expression of surprise even appeared on his face.","At last, he withdrew his hand and bowed. “Reporting to Your Highness, the young lady’s health is perfectly fine. Her pulse is strong, and her qi and blood are abundant. Such a robust and healthy constitution is something this old physician has rarely seen in all his years.”","These days, young ladies all pursued a delicate, willow-like appearance. Most achieved it by starving themselves.","The noble ladies in the palace were even worse. They rarely exercised and had to maintain their figures. After years of this, how healthy could their bodies possibly be?","Shen Yanshui was speechless. “Robust” was really not necessary. Truly.","Cui Yu was slightly surprised by the physician’s words. After examining her carefully, he looked toward the imperial physician and said, “She just ate six bowls of rice.”","The unspoken meaning was clear: Is that really normal?","Shen Yanshui was speechless again. What was wrong with eating six bowls of rice? Was she eating his family’s rice?","Well, she was indeed eating rice from his household.","Imperial Physician Hu smiled. “Your Ladyship has a strong pulse, and naturally a robust appetite as well. I imagine you’re usually quite active, which is why you eat more and digest your food quickly. It won’t have any adverse effect on your health.”","Shen Yanshui hurriedly nodded. “The physician is right. Not only that, I’ve been stronger than most people since I was little, so naturally I eat a little more than they do.”","After the physician left, Cui Yu glanced at her, then turned to Zheng Yuande and instructed, “From now on, if Lady Shen’s daily food and provisions aren’t enough, take what’s needed from my allowance.”","Since she served in his Eastern Palace, he couldn’t very well let her go hungry.","Zheng Yuande glanced at Lady Shen, whose face had instantly lit up with delight. He couldn’t help mulling it over for a moment before respectfully replying, “Yes, Your Highness. This servant will remember.”","Shen Yanshui was genuinely happy now—overjoyed, in fact!","Her eyes sparkled at him as though they were shining with a dazzling “bling, bling,” and in that moment, he seemed especially tall and imposing to her. Especially charming!","She clasped one of his hands in both of hers and said with heartfelt sincerity, “Thank you, Your Highness. You’re truly wonderful!”","This wasn’t just about one or two meals. It was about every meal from now on.","At last, she no longer had to worry about where she would find the money once the two thousand taels of silver ran out.","Her exuberant happiness seemed almost infectious. Without realizing it, the corners of Cui Yu’s lips lifted slightly as well, and for a moment, he forgot the unpleasant events that had taken place at court."]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15: ...Delicate.","paragraphs":["Cui Yu glanced down at the slender, soft, fair hands that were clutching his palm tightly. The moment his fingertips stirred slightly, Shen Yanshui noticed his gaze. She quickly pulled her hands back, smiling brightly and saying, \"Your subject wife got carried away by joy just now and lost my manners. I hope Your Highness will not hold it against me~\"","Cui Yu gently curled his palm into a fist, as if the soft warmth from a moment ago still lingered on both the inside and outside of his hand.","He glanced around the room, then finally turned his eyes back to her and asked, \"What do you usually do on a daily basis?\"","Shen Yanshui did not catch his subtle little gesture. At his question, she proceeded to recount all her daily routines in detail.","To sum it up, she would get up in the morning, have meals, practice Baduanjin twice to stretch her body, (do her cultivation), and wander around the garden, and just like that, the whole morning would be gone.","After that, she would take a siesta, have lunch, read books and listen to storytellers' scripts, tend to the flowers and plants in her courtyard, think about what delicious food to have next, finish her dinner, and the whole afternoon would slip by too. Then she would take a walk to aid digestion, (do her cultivation), and go to bed.","She told him everything truthfully except for the part about cultivation.","And that was the perfect end to her day.","Cui Yu paused for a moment after listening to her account, and said, \"So every day... you are quite 'busy'.\"","Her simple, straightforward description gave off a sense of leisurely coziness, making it feel like she took each day unhurriedly, living her own little life earnestly.","That said, Baduanjin was indeed quite effective in warding off illnesses and keeping fit. If she had practiced it for years, and added activities like cuju and horse polo to that mix, it would hardly be strange that she had such a healthy body.","Shen Yanshui had intentionally mentioned Baduanjin because she knew this form of exercise already existed in the Great Yong Dynasty.","At his words, she pretended to ponder for a moment, then nodded at him seriously, \"Yes, I really am quite busy.\"","Busy cultivating, busy planting flowers and melons, busy sleeping, busy eating good food, and busy enjoying this little life where she had no worries about food or drink, and no one pointing fingers or ordering her around.","All of a sudden, Cui Yu lifted his hand and tapped her forehead with his knuckle, saying in a faint, calm tone, \"I think you are just far too idle.\"","Shen Yanshui covered her forehead with one hand, her tone full of feigned grievance, \"That hurt~\"","The attendants waiting on them inside the room were very observant, and quietly moved far away to give them space.","When Shen Yanshui lowered her hand, Cui Yu saw a small red mark on her originally fair, glossy forehead. He could not help but be slightly stunned for a second. He had not used any force at all, who would have thought her skin was so delicate. Hmm... it was not just her forehead either. It seemed every part of her was always so fragile, that the lightest touch could leave a patch of red...","His gaze deepened for a brief moment, before he pulled his eyes away from her. He casually picked up a book that had been left on the soft couch, his voice lowering slightly, \"What book is this?\" The moment the words left his mouth, a little colorful object slipped out from between the pages.","Cui Yu picked it up, turned to look at her, and said, \"This is... a luck braid? For me?\" His voice sounded perfectly even, giving no hint of what he was thinking.","Shen Yanshui was only stunned for a split second, before she nodded with a perfectly natural expression, \"That's right! The Dragon Boat Festival is in a few days. I wove this specially for Your Highness. This colorful silk braid can ward off evil spirits, and bless you with smooth, safe days. I just never expected you would stumble across it today.\"","She did not mention at all that this had originally been something she had been practicing her weaving on, which was why it was a little wider and larger than usual, as she was still clumsy when she first started.","Chunping, who was standing by the room door, lowered her head even further the moment she heard those words.","Cui Yu eyed the intricately woven concentric-pattern sash before him, crafted from multicolored silk threads and about a finger's width wide. He set it casually on the side table, not seeming to pay it much mind at all.","Shen Yanshui did not take offense. After all, it was just a little trinket she had made as a beginner for fun—how could something so crude catch the eye of a man who had seen countless fine treasures in his life?","The two chatted idly for a while before stepping out to take a stroll to aid digestion. Cui Yu had assumed Shen Yanshui would bring up the trip to Jinling Pool on the Dragon Boat Festival, either directly or subtly, but much to his surprise, she did not mention a single word about it the entire walk.","After they had bathed and changed into fresh robes, all the attendants withdrew, leaving only a single candle by the bedside, its flame flickering gently in the night breeze.","That night, Shen Yanshui was unusually passionate.","Hadn't he called her too idle? Well, here she was, pulling a \"night shift\" even now—though she did not mind this particular shift at all. But how dare he say she had nothing better to do?","Looking at the strong, sturdy form hovering over her, Shen Yanshui did not hold back—there was no need to. She reached out to run her hands over him, and watching the shifting expressions in his eyes, she grew even bolder in her teasing.","Cui Yu's gaze darkened abruptly. The next moment, Shen Yanshui was jolted so hard that her head nearly slammed into the bedpost, only to be tugged back into his arms just in time.","Though she had plenty of stamina, staying in one position for too long grew uncomfortable...","When her head sank once more into the soft propped-up pillow at the head of the bed, her breath came in uneven little gasps. Her voice trembled softly, sounding as if she were pouting in gentle grievance. \"Your Highness, my head hurts from all the bumps...\"","Cui Yu's movements came to a brief halt.","He shifted his hands from where they rested on her body, curling his fingers around her ankles. Shen Yanshui lifted her leg, the rounded tip of her foot pressing lightly against his solid shoulder, her tone laced with faint reproach. \"My back is sore too, from all the rubbing.\"","Cui Yu paused again. His gaze grew heavy, his voice tight, low, and hoarse. \"...Spoiled thing.\"","Before she could say another word, he swept her up into his arms, holding her entire body against his chest.","Startled, Shen Yanshui instinctively wrapped her legs around his lean, powerful waist, her slender, graceful arms clinging tight around his neck.","Cui Yu's breath caught sharply, his face suddenly sinking into the soft, yielding warmth of her skin.","Shen Yanshui: \"...\" Her fair, jade-like cheeks flushed bright red in an instant.","Outside the chamber, Chunping stood rooted to the spot, her face burning bright red as she listened to the faint, muffled rustlings coming from inside the room, punctuated by the occasional soft creaking sound that made her worry for a good long while.","But after a while, the little creaks died away. The room fell almost quiet, yet no one called out for water, which left her quite confused.","Shen Yanshui soon discovered that beneath the Crown Prince's cold, dignified, and gentle exterior, his arm strength was far greater than she had expected. He could carry her while moving so vigorously without showing the slightest sign of strain.","It was a pleasure unlike any other...","The next morning, when Shen Yanshui woke up, the first thing she saw was a strikingly handsome, elegant face, sharp-featured and fair.","She thought for a moment, and then remembered—wasn't today a day off from official duties?","But why was she in his bed? Every time before, after they finished, they would clean up quickly and sleep under their own separate quilts. She had always thought that arrangement was perfect, nothing beat the comfort of having your own quilt to yourself. But now... there was a large, warm hand resting on her chest. No wonder she had felt a heavy weight there all night.","She tried to shift her position, but the moment she moved, Cui Yu opened his eyes.","His palm shifted unconsciously, and a soft, alluring little hum brushed past his ear. That was when Cui Yu finally woke up completely.","Shen Yanshui fixed her pair of peach blossom eyes on him, her tone soft and lingering as she said, \"Your Highness, you were holding my hand far too tight...\" Seeing the faint, unseemly flicker of discomfort cross his face, Shen Yanshui could not help but chuckle inwardly. Before he could utter a single word in response, she added, \"Your Highness, this concubine is feeling a little hungry.\"","Cui Yu calmly and unflappably withdrew his hand as if nothing out of the ordinary had happened. He gave a low grunt of acknowledgement, then lifted the quilt, got out of bed, and walked around the screen to call Zheng Yuande in to attend to him.","Through the faintly translucent screen, Shen Yanshui watched him from behind. The sunlight streaming through the window lattice gilded half of his back, and under the soft pale golden glow, the defined lines of his arms stood out all the more sharply.","As he moved to get dressed, the muscles along his back shifted in smooth, flowing undulations. The only difference was that his otherwise elegant back now bore several faint, thin red marks that looked as if they had been left accidentally by fingernails, lending him a strangely disheveled, alluring charm.","The next moment, he pulled on his white undershirt to cover his body. Only then did Shen Yanshui rise, throw on a loose outer robe, casually tie a sash around her waist, and step forward of her own accord. With a soft, smiling voice, she said, \"Your Highness, allow this concubine to help you dress.\"","Zheng Yuande quickly ducked his head, presented the Crown Prince's outer robe, and stepped a respectful distance away.","Cui Yu lowered his gaze slightly, looking at her half-done attire without saying a word for a moment.","Shen Yanshui's mind raced back to the dressing procedures the nannies had taught her in the Palace of Elegant Virtue, and she followed each step slowly to dress him properly. The leather belt around his waist proved a little tricky to fasten, but she bent over, lowered her head, and eventually managed to tie it neatly, if a little clumsily.","No one rushed her the whole time, which was a relief.","She felt a small swell of satisfaction at the task done. \"There we go,\" she said with a bright smile, and as she lifted her head, she saw the Crown Prince turn his head to stare intently at the bamboo branch on the incense table, as if a full bloom had sprouted right out of the twig.","Cui Yu kept a stern, straight face, only uttering a curt \"Mm\" before he turned and stepped out of the room.","Shen Yanshui watched his departing back, and by chance, her gaze landed on the tips of his ears, which were bright crimson. She paused for a moment in confusion, then suddenly glanced down at her own clothes.","Since she had tied her sash in a rush, the lapels of her robe had fallen loosely open, and she had not even put on her inner chemise beneath it... But thinking back to how he had acted just now, she felt a strange mix of amusement and surprise well up in her chest.","The Crown Prince... could it be that just a glance at that was enough to fluster him so much his ears turned red?","It was not as if his own hands had been anything but unruly earlier, right after they woke up.","Even so, she could not help but think that this version of the Crown Prince, all stony-faced with bright red ears, was unexpectedly quite endearing."]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16: Father and Son of the Heavenly Family","paragraphs":["With the help of Chunping and Xia'an, Shen Yanshui got herself ready in no time. When she walked into the outer room, she saw a line of palace attendants filing in, setting the breakfast spread on the table.","She looked over to Cui Yu, the Crown Prince, who was sitting on the soft couch holding a book, and stepped forward with a smile to pay her respects.","Cui Yu lifted his gaze, as if he had only just noticed her.","The weather that day was lovely, with sunlight streaming into the room early on. Shen Yanshui was wearing a rose-purple soft smoke gauze dress, a white jade crabapple pendant fastened around her slender waist that looked so narrow it could be circled with one hand, with a thin layer of cicada-wing gauze draped over the whole outfit, making her look exceptionally gentle and pretty.","Only her hair and hair ornaments were far too simple.","Cui Yu spoke in a light, calm tone, telling her to rise.","Shen Yanshui noticed that his gaze had lingered on her hair for an extra moment just now, but she did not pay it any mind. Unless she was going out, in her own chambers, she usually only asked Xia'an to twist her hair into a simple bun, securing it with a single hairpin or a hair ribbon, as it was the most comfortable way to wear it.","Of course, this was also her gradual way of testing the limits of what the Crown Prince would allow her to do. So far... the results of her test seemed pretty good.","The two of them began to have their meal. Shen Yanshui was not picky about food at all, so even though all the dishes on the table were originally prepared by the imperial kitchen for the Crown Prince, she ate with great enjoyment.","When Cui Yu set down his silver chopsticks, he saw her glance at him, blink her eyes, and say, \"Your Highness, your concubine hasn't had her fill yet.\"","Cui Yu said gently, \"From now on, when you have meals, you can eat as much as you like. There is no need to hold back on account of me.\"","\"Thank you, Your Highness. You are so kind.\" Shen Yanshui looked at him with bright, sparkling eyes.","After saying that, she served herself another bowl of green vegetable and minced meat porridge and continued to eat.","Though Shen Yanshui ate quite a lot, her manners were not rude or unrefined at all. After all, when a person was as beautiful as she was, every little thing she did was a pleasure to watch.","Seeing how good her appetite was and how happy she looked while eating, Cui Yu let out a soft chuckle, lowered his head to take a sip of tea, then suddenly frowned slightly and put the teacup down.","Zheng Yuande had long since seen through everything. This Lady Shen was truly a simple, silly soul who took every word the Crown Prince said completely seriously.","His Highness had told her to eat freely, and she had really settled in to eat without a second thought, leaving the Crown Prince sitting there waiting for her. It was almost as if tending to His Highness was less important than the two bowls of food in front of her...","Zheng Yuande was left completely speechless.","Still, it was a good thing he had been quick-witted and specifically told the imperial kitchen to make extra portions earlier, otherwise he would have been worried that there would not be enough food left for the Crown Prince to eat.","As for the serving maids Chunping and Xia'an, no matter what complicated thoughts they had in their hearts, none of them dared to say a word. After all, they had tried to gently persuade her before, but... it had not worked at all. In the end, they could only keep a steady, polite smile on their faces.","Shen Yanshui did not keep anyone waiting for long. She finished her meal soon after, and rinsed her mouth.","Cui Yu looked at her and suddenly said, \"In a few days, it will be the Dragon Boat Festival. Would you like to go to Jinming Pool to watch the celebrations?\"","Shen Yanshui was a little surprised, not expecting him to take the initiative to ask her such a question. But right then, her eyes sparkling, she answered without the slightest hesitation, \"This concubine would love to go.\"","Who would not want to go and see all the lively fun?","Zheng Yuande: \"...\" He was now fully certain that this woman was truly a simple one.","Chunping and Xia'an: \"...\"","My lady, even if you really do want to go, you cannot say it so straightforwardly in front of the Crown Prince. You could at least be a little more tactful about it!","Cui Yu nodded at her answer, as if he had not found it unexpected at all. Listening to her speak openly of what she wanted, without using that soft, timid tone to hint and beat around the bush, or take the chance to throw subtle digs at the Crown Princess or other concubines to badmouth them, made the deep, calm light in his eyes soften into a faint, gentle smile. His voice was clear and rich, unhurried as he said, \"I understand.\"","Shen Yanshui curtsied to see him off, and at the same time, she began to look forward to the upcoming Dragon Boat Festival.","Lady Liu watched the Crown Prince leave, his tall, graceful figure receding from sight. She suppressed the sour feeling in her heart, lowered her head, and curtsied to the Lady Shen beside her. \"Sister Shen, I will head back to my chambers first.\"","Shen Yanshui nodded with a smile, pretending not to notice the dark circles under Lady Liu's eyes, and did not say anything extra. There were so many women in the imperial harem. If Lady Liu did not learn to look on the bright side and make an effort to live a better life, she would only end up suffering for it.","Back in her own room, Shen Yanshui picked up the book that was left on the soft couch to continue reading. It was a geographical record of the northern border of the Great Yong Dynasty, filled with the author's accounts of the local customs and conditions there, and she had found it really interesting to read.","\"Eh?\" Shen Yanshui flipped through the pages of the book, then looked all around the soft couch, before lifting her head to ask Chunping, \"Where is my multicolored braided charm?\"","Before Chunping could reply, Xia'an, who was in the middle of ironing clothes, suddenly pressed her lips together and snickered, whispering, \"Your mistress, this servant saw it. The Crown Prince took it with him just now.\"","Shen Yanshui: \"......?\"","*","It was Cui Yu's day off. He did not have to attend court hearings, nor did he have to go to the capital administrative office to handle official duties. But as soon as he arrived at Changqing Palace and before he could even sit down, he turned to give an order. \"I remember that last year, the Southern Ocean tributed a set of hibiscus pink crystal headpieces inlaid with pearls?\"","Zheng Yuande was taken aback for a moment, then replied, \"Your Highness, that is correct. I heard that kind of hibiscus pink crystal is extremely rare and precious.\"","Cui Yu said, \"Deliver that set of headpieces to Lady Shen.\"","Zheng Yuande quickly bowed to acknowledge the order. But before he could step out, he heard His Highness add, \"Also go to the Inner Palace's flower nursery and pick out some well-bloomed flowers and plants.\" He paused for a brief moment, then said in a light tone, \"Have the Palace Attendants Bureau...\"","After Zheng Yuande withdrew, someone came to report that Chen Qian, the Junior Supervisor of the Imperial Household who was an official of the Eastern Palace, was already waiting in the Dunben Hall. Cui Yu's brows drew together slightly.","Chen Qian was just over forty years old, wearing a vermilion official robe with a leather belt fastened around his waist. His features were dignified, and he wore a small goatee. But his expression at the moment was far from pleasant. He was ushered into the Crown Prince's study after his presence was announced.","Chen Qian bowed to pay his respects. \"This subject greets Your Highness, the Crown Prince.\"","Cui Yu said in a calm voice, \"Lord Chen, there is no need for formalities.\"","After Chen Qian straightened up, his brows furrowed into a deep frown. He said in a heavy tone, \"Your Highness, early this morning, His Majesty suddenly issued an order for Marquis Xuanyi to lead forty thousand of the elite Tiger Wing troops under Great General Qi's command. This way, half of the military power has been split off. The Great General has also been ordered to remain at home to rest and recuperate. Your Highness, are we just going to wait for our doom like this?\"","The Duke Fengguo, the maternal family of the Crown Prince, used to hold military power. But ever since the Crown Prince's young uncle Great General Qi rose to prominence on the battlefield, the old duke, who had seemed hale and hearty before, suffered a recurrence of an old injury and could no longer go to the front lines.","Great General Qi was brilliant at fighting wars, but when it came to court politics, he was not as seasoned and experienced as the old duke, so he could not offer much support to the Crown Prince.","After he finished speaking and saw that the Crown Prince did not say a word, he frowned even harder and added, \"Your Highness, word has it that Marquis Xuanyi and Great General Qi have never gotten along, and he is also related by marriage to the He family, the maternal clan of the Fourth Prince. His Majesty is clearly paving the way to elevate the Fourth Prince. We cannot just sit back and do nothing any longer!\"","\"I heard that the arrangements for the Jinming Pool celebrations during the upcoming Dragon Boat Festival have been assigned by His Majesty to the First Prince and the Fourth Prince. We could place some of our men to make some secret moves there...\"","Cui Yu suddenly cut off his next words, his expression turning slightly grim. \"Lord Chen.\"","Chen Qian: \"Your Highness?\"","Cui Yu's brows drew tight. \"I understand Lord Chen's intentions, but the Duanwu Festival gathering at the Golden Bright Pond will draw attention from all across the court and the general public. This matter concerns the imperial family's reputation, so there is no need to discuss it further.\"","In the end, this Lord Chen left with a rigid, stony expression on his face.","Cui Yu's own countenance remained perfectly calm. The matter of military power had long been discussed and planned between him, his maternal grandfather, and his young maternal uncle, so this turn of events was no surprise to him.","His father, the Emperor, was no foolish, incompetent ruler. When Cui Yu was young, he had always looked up to his father as his role model, and he had dreamed of becoming a wise, enlightened sovereign just like him.","Yet, as the Emperor's health faded day by day, and his sons grew older and more capable with each passing day, the Emperor's temperament grew increasingly unpredictable and suspicious.","It was at this exact juncture that foreign tribes from the northern border invaded. Cui Yu's young maternal uncle won instant fame through a decisive battle, and over the following years, he accumulated one brilliant military achievement after another.","As successive reports of victory arrived in the capital from the frontier, Cui Yu gradually noticed a distinct shift in the Emperor's attitude toward him.","Several years on, the original Crown Prince's Household Administration Office had become nothing more than an empty name. The former officials assigned to serve the Eastern Palace had all been dismissed or transferred away. Now, many of the officials holding posts in the Eastern Palace are just like Chen Qian -- good for nothing but show, short-sighted, or eager for quick gains at any cost.","There were a few of them with real talent and ability, but without exception, each of them held multiple concurrent official positions, all serving as the head of a government ministry in the imperial court. Their nominal post as a member of the Eastern Palace's staff was nothing but a meaningless, empty title to them.","It was true that Cui Yu could summon them if he needed something done, but... there was no point in doing so.","They were not the Crown Prince's men. They were the Emperor's men.","Cui Yu's gaze fell on a white jade paperweight at the edge of his desk.","It was one of the birthday gifts the Emperor had personally carved and given to him when he was three years old, the year he began his formal studies. The jade was warm and smooth to the touch, carved with simple, unadorned cloud patterns.","He still remembered the Emperor holding his small hand, guiding him stroke by stroke to write his very first character -- \"yong\", meaning forever.","\"Yu'er, writing is just like being a person. Your brush must be held straight, and your heart must also be straight.\"","Back then, the Emperor's voice had carried a bright, hearty laugh, none of the suspicion and wariness that marked it now. Cui Yu could even recall being too small to reach the desk, so the Emperor had lifted him to sit on his lap, letting him curiously grab the heavy imperial private seal to play with.","The Emperor had not been angry at all, and had simply let him treat the royal seal as a toy, stamping random patterns all over sheets of paper.","Cui Yu slowly closed his eyes, the pad of his index finger unconsciously stroking the smooth edge of the jade paperweight.","Among the sons of heaven, it was far from unheard of for father and son to end up facing each other on the battlefield, fighting a life-and-death struggle.","But... he did not want that to happen between him and his father."]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17: Quite... thoughtful","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui did not practice the Eight Brocades today. She ordered everyone to leave and began cultivating on her own.","First-rank abilities were extremely weak. Take fire abilities, for example: at the first rank, one could initially produce only a tiny flame. After becoming more proficient, one might be able to launch a fist-sized fireball, but its power and duration were still rather limited.","The same was true of wood abilities. They were generally even weaker than fire abilities. Fortunately, there were no mutated beasts like those in the apocalypse, so being weak was not particularly important.","When her wood ability had been at the first rank, she could only hasten the growth of plants in a small area. In a confrontation, it was practically useless.","All these years, she had never given up exercising her body. It was only that her inexpensive parents had strictly forbidden her from learning martial arts, which had always been a source of regret.","In any case, if she encountered danger, she might not be able to defeat her opponent, but escaping with her life should not be a problem.","She was pondering this when the tips of her ears twitched.","At the same time, the courtyard rang with greetings of varying pitches, along with Zheng Yuande’s voice.","The moment Chunping entered the room, she saw that her mistress had already come out, fully dressed and ready. Chunping could not help but beam with delight. “Mistress, Eunuch Zheng has arrived.”","Shen Yanshui stepped outside and saw the plump, round-faced Zheng Yuande smiling cheerfully at her, along with the long line of people and gifts behind him.","After the two exchanged polite greetings, Zheng Yuande cleared his throat and explained the purpose of his visit. He had indeed come to deliver gifts from the Crown Prince to Lady Shen, but among those gifts was something inconvenient to mention in public—a bed.","Shen Yanshui understood at once. Thinking back, she seemed to have heard the wooden bed creak last night when things had gotten rather intense. She had not expected the Crown Prince to remember such a detail.","Pressing her lips together in a smile, she said, “I suddenly remembered that the paint on the bed in my room has started to peel. I’ll have the Imperial Household Department replace it with a new one later.”","Zheng Yuande let out a sigh of relief. It seemed Lady Shen was not quite as foolish as she appeared.","If the Crown Prince had directly bestowed a bed upon her, what would people say about him once word got out?","Satisfied, he glanced at the items being carried behind him and said, “The Crown Prince heard that you enjoy tending to flowers and plants, Lady Shen, so he specially sent you six pots each of peonies, weeping crabapples, qionghua, and lilacs. There is also some tea for you to sample.”","Shen Yanshui looked at the flowers in full bloom, her eyes curving into delighted crescents. She had not expected the Crown Prince to be so thoughtful with his gifts. As for the tea... Though she did not know why he had suddenly thought to send her tea, anything that came from the Crown Prince was unlikely to be ordinary.","“The flowers bestowed by His Highness are even more beautiful than those in the Imperial Garden. I’ll choose a few to place on my desk later and admire them every day. I certainly won’t fail to appreciate His Highness’s kindness.”","Zheng Yuande chuckled. “I’m glad you like them. If there is nothing else, this servant will take his leave.”","Shen Yanshui exchanged a few more polite words with him before saying, “Take care, Eunuch Zheng.” As usual, she had Quanfu see him out.","Afterward, she first looked over the flowers and plants, then examined the jewelry bestowed by the Crown Prince. A smile spread across her face, and her eyes curved into crescents.","Could it be that the Crown Prince thought... she had no jewelry to wear? Was that why he had given her all these gifts?","Still, this lotus pink crystal was truly beautiful. Even someone like her, who had never cared much for dressing up, found it so lovely that her heart stirred at the sight of it.","“Rain-Season Dragon Well, Silver Needle, Lushan Cloud Mist, Biluochun?” After admiring the jewelry, Shen Yanshui opened each of the white porcelain tea jars, taking a look inside before leaning closer to smell them.","She more or less understood why he had suddenly sent her tea. Perhaps the tea he had drunk at her residence had not suited his taste, so he had remembered to send some of his own here.","Quanfu happened to return after seeing the visitors out and heard her words. He smiled and said, “These are all fine spring teas. Outside the palace, they would probably be worth a fortune.”","Dongyi was astonished. “They’re really that expensive?”","Chunping said, “We must store them carefully, or we’ll end up ruining something so precious.”","Qiuyi’s face was full of smiles, and her eyes were filled with envy. “His Highness is truly good to our mistress.”","Shen Yanshui smiled.","He was indeed very good to her. Although the Crown Prince seemed somewhat aloof, he was not difficult to get along with. He was not overly rigid or formal either, and he was even... rather considerate.","She liked drinking tea as well. She did not have any particular preference, but in this life, she had at least been born into an earl’s household, so she knew the value of fine tea.","With such good tea on hand, she could even make milk tea if she had the opportunity.","However, she felt that if the Crown Prince bestowed gifts upon her two or three more times, she might become the target of everyone’s resentment.","But there was rarely a way to have the best of both worlds. How could one obtain good things without also bearing the risks that came with them?","Thus, she took it all in stride.","“Come, brew me a cup of Biluochun to try. Then go to the kitchen and bring back two plates of pastries.” She gave the order with a beaming smile.","“Yes, Mistress!” Dongyi replied, her face lighting up with delight.","*","The moment Eunuch Zheng left, everyone in the courtyards of the rear quarters learned that the Crown Prince had bestowed more gifts upon Lady Shen.","The flowers and plants were one thing. What shocked everyone was the news that the Crown Prince had even given Lady Shen an entire set of lotus pink crystal jewelry!","Lady Chu’s delicate face darkened, and her expression turned ugly. “That was tribute from the South Seas, an exceptionally rare and precious treasure. His Highness actually gave it to Lady Shen just like that?”","She had once tactfully asked His Highness about it, yet he had refused to give it to her!","The palace maid beside her hurriedly sent the young eunuch who had delivered the news away, then lowered her voice and said, “Please don’t be angry, Mistress. The two matrons are still here.”","Lady Chu took several deep breaths before barely suppressing the resentment and jealousy in her heart. “Forget it. They’re only a few pieces of jewelry. They’re nothing important.”","At present, nothing mattered more than the child in her womb. Once she gave birth to a royal son, there would be plenty of time to settle accounts.","At Begonia Court—","Lady Wu directly smashed the fine celadon cup in her hand after hearing the news.","She said furiously, “That vixen! Who knows what kind of spell she cast on His Highness, or what sort of medicine she gave him!”","Ever since she was young, she had relied on her beautiful face. As long as she wanted something, things generally went smoothly for her.","Yet after entering the Eastern Palace, the beauty she had always taken pride in seemed to have lost its effect. Not only was there now a Lady Shen whose looks were in no way inferior to hers, but that woman also opposed her at every turn.","The Crown Prince was not as attentive and eager toward her as other men had been.","Yesterday, she had even made such a huge fool of herself in front of the Crown Prince!","After returning and looking in the mirror, she had only to remember that she had appeared before His Highness looking like that for her chest to tighten and her breathing to grow labored.","It was all that scheming vixen, Lady Shen’s, fault!","She said indignantly, “Why doesn’t Her Highness the Crown Princess discipline her?! If I were the Crown Princess, I would have dealt with that Lady Shen long ago!”","Her personal maid hurriedly tried to console her, but Lady Wu was clearly in no mood to listen. She continued complaining angrily, occasionally mixing in a few curses and insults.","Living in Begonia Court, Lady Lu, one of the Crown Prince’s long-serving women who occupied the eastern side hall, merely lifted her eyelids when she heard the commotion erupting once again from the main hall. She then continued staring at the begonia blossoms she was embroidering, her gaze gradually growing deeper and more inscrutable...","The palace maid serving beside her heard the disturbance as well. Frowning, she said in a low voice, “I never would have thought Lady Wu had such a temperament. The things we sent her before were probably wasted.”","They had originally planned on befriending the new Lady Wu, thinking that with her beauty, she ought to win the Crown Prince’s favor. If that happened, he would naturally visit Begonia Court more often, making it all the more worthwhile to establish a good relationship with Lady Wu.","But seeing Lady Wu’s disposition now, their plans were likely to come to nothing.","Lady Lu raised her eyes toward the vividly blooming begonias outside the window and said gently, “There’s no need to hurry. Let’s wait a little longer.”","News traveled even faster in Xiefang Hall than it did from the rear quarters. After all, there was no way to conceal the Crown Prince opening his private treasury, and the Crown Princess naturally had people and informants of her own stationed throughout the Eastern Palace.","Matron Zhou had just entered with a bowl of medicinal soup. Taking one look at the Crown Princess’s expression, she knew that Her Highness was in a poor mood.","“Your Highness, please don’t let anger and distress harm you. It’s only a set of jewelry. You must take care of your health.” Matron Zhou was somewhat helpless. The Crown Prince was the heir apparent; it was perfectly ordinary for him to bestow gifts upon his women.","It was simply that, in the past, the Crown Prince had rarely rewarded the women in the rear quarters. Whenever he did give them something, he would usually inform the Crown Princess first and have her present the gifts on his behalf.","The Crown Prince’s attitude should have made them even more vigilant.","Matron Zhou continued, “Your Highness, perhaps the Crown Prince is behaving this way because what happened last time caused him to harbor some resentment toward you. Once a few more days have passed and the Dragon Boat Festival is over, how could His Highness continue holding a grudge against you?” Her words carried an unmistakable implication.","The tension between the Crown Princess’s brows eased slightly, and she instinctively stroked her abdomen.","Matron Zhou went on persuading her. “Your Highness, at most, this is merely a passing novelty for the Crown Prince. Why not go along with his wishes? However you put it, she is no more than a concubine who serves through her beauty. At present, nothing is more important than your health.”","The Crown Princess pressed her lips together. “I understand.”","Although she had long grown accustomed to being “virtuous and accommodating,” that had only been because the Crown Prince had treated everyone more or less equally, without showing any special preference.","But now, she truly needed to win back the Crown Prince’s favor. She could not allow the rift between them to take root."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18: Sleep, sleep, I'm sleepy.","paragraphs":["Two more days passed. One day, just before the evening meal was served, a messenger was sent by the Crown Princess to invite the Crown Prince to share dinner with her at the Hall of Blossom Gathering.","Cui Yu lifted his head from the stacks of official documents, twisted his stiff neck, and glanced out the window at a sprig of blooming plum blossoms. As if suddenly remembering something, he tossed his brush into the brush holder, stood up, and said, \"Let us go.\"","\"His Imperial Highness the Crown Prince has arrived —\"","\"Greetings to Your Highness the Crown Prince —\" All the servants in the Hall of Blossom Gathering knelt to pay their respects.","The Crown Princess was dressed in a flowing pale purple robe with wide sleeves, her hair adorned with a peony pearl coronet and a golden peony-patterned step sway that glinted with every small movement. Noble, poised, and elegant, she had been waiting respectfully right at the entrance long before he arrived.","When she saw him walking toward her, tall and straight, she greeted him with a soft smile and a curtsy. Cui Yu lifted his hand in a slight gesture to help her rise, then withdrew his hand once she stood.","The two of them stepped into the main hall of the Hall of Blossom Gathering one after the other. Silence during meals and rest was a rule the Crown Princess had been taught to follow since childhood, so as long as Cui Yu did not speak, the dining table remained perfectly quiet, save for the occasional soft clink of chopsticks against bowls.","Cui Yu had a good appetite these days, so he ate heartily at first. But when he noticed that the Crown Princess had only taken two bites before putting down her utensils, her face looking slightly pale and unwell, his brows furrowed. \"Are you feeling unwell, Crown Princess?\"","Though he had been angry with her over an incident some time ago, in the days following his warning, the Crown Princess had conducted herself quite well. He assumed she had learned her lesson and repented of her mistakes.","After all, she was his Crown Princess, and he could not pretend not to notice her obvious discomfort.","Cui Yu asked, \"Has your disharmony of the spleen and stomach not healed yet? Have you summoned the imperial physician to examine you?\" He had noticed her taking medicine occasionally these past days, and had asked once before, which was why he inquired now.","The Crown Princess froze for a moment at his question, then set down her silver chopsticks, a faint, bitter ache rising in her eyes. \"To answer Your Highness, there is nothing serious wrong with my body. My cold is almost fully recovered. It is just that I indulged in too much tea and fruit at noon, so I am not very hungry now. You need not concern yourself with me, Your Highness. Let me attend to you as you eat.\"","Cui Yu glanced at her and said, \"There is no need. You may rest as you like.\"","Even so, the Crown Princess sat by his side, repeatedly placing choice morsels onto his plate, while she herself barely ate a few bites.","Cui Yu had been rather hungry when he arrived, but now his appetite was gone. He only finished one bowl of rice before setting down his chopsticks and bowl. The Crown Princess did not find this strange at all, assuming the Crown Prince must have eaten something else before coming to her hall.","Their conversation inevitably turned to their child, who was still too young, being held and nursed by his wet nurse. After confirming that the child was in good health, Cui Yu nodded in satisfaction. Though the little prince was still not as robust as ordinary children his age, with careful upbringing, he would surely grow stronger and healthier over time.","The Crown Princess chatted on for a while more about the child, before smiling and saying, \"By the way, Your Highness, the Dragon Boat Festival is three days from now. As per usual custom this year, we are to bring two of the younger consorts to the Golden Bright Pond. Have you decided on who the two will be? I was thinking that Lady Zhang —\"","\"Lady Shen shall go with you,\" Cui Yu cut in abruptly.","The Crown Princess's smile froze at the corners for a split second, before she regained her composure and laughed as if nothing was amiss. \"Your Highness is quite right. I had thought that since Lady Zhang holds the highest rank among the new consorts, we might bring her and Lady Chu along. But the Lady Shen you speak of, I have always found her to be a gentle, obedient soul. We shall bring her along as well.\"","Cui Yu nodded. \"She is simple and straightforward by nature. You must look after her well.\"","The Crown Princess's fingers curled tightly inward, her neatly trimmed nails digging deep into the soft flesh of her palms, yet her face remained wreathed in a gentle smile. \"Rest assured, Your Highness. I shall take good care of both of the younger sisters.\"","Cui Yu frowned slightly. \"Lady Chu is with child now. She ought not to go to such crowded, noisy places. Let her stay in the palace and rest peacefully to nurture her pregnancy.\"","The Crown Princess nodded and smiled in agreement, then added in a light, half-joking tone, \"It is just that for the past two years, Sister Chu has joined us every time. If she cannot come this time, I am afraid she will blame me for leaving her behind.\"","Cui Yu's eyes turned cool, his tone steady and unyielding. \"You are the Crown Princess. You hold the authority to assist in managing the affairs of the Eastern Palace. No one else has the right to question your decisions.\"","At his words, the Crown Princess's lips curved into a bright, pleased smile.","That same evening, the Crown Prince went to Lady Chu's quarters. Most of the servants who heard the news in the back suite could not help but feel a flicker of disappointment.","When the news reached the servants in Lotus Heart Courtyard, they exchanged glances with one another. Finally, Chunping stepped forward softly and said, \"Master, the Crown Prince has gone to Bright Moon Retreat.\" As she spoke, she stole a glance at her mistress, her eyes full of quiet worry.","Shen Yanshui lifted her gaze from the book she was reading, looking at Chunping's worried expression, and the rest of the maids who had suddenly become so cautious and tense. She could not help feeling a little amused. Did they really think she was so fragile?","If she could not accept such things, she might as well go off to a nunnery and become a nun. Otherwise, what was the point? Could she ever hope to find a man in this palace who would swear to be devoted only to her, to live a lifetime of perfect fidelity, and stay chaste for no one but her?","She herself could not even guarantee that she would only love one man for her entire life, let alone promise to remain chaste for a single man. No one could tell what the future might bring.","If that was the case, why waste her time pining after such impossible, unrealistic fantasies?","Seeing their anxious faces, she said, a little helplessly, \"What on earth are all of you looking so glum for?\"","Chunping saw that she did not look sad, lost, or angry at all, and felt a little sheepish. \"We were all worried that you would be in a bad mood...\"","Shen Yanshui could not help but ask curiously, \"Back when the Crown Prince visited other courtyards before, why were none of you so worried then?\"","Just looking at their faces, she could easily guess what they were thinking. They assumed that because the Crown Prince had treated her a little differently than the others, she had started to care for him more deeply, and so would grow more and more upset whenever he gave his attention to someone else.","\"Ah, never mind —\" She yawned, her voice soft and drowsy. \"Time for bed. I am sleepy.\""]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19: Cui Yu: \"...glib-tongued.\"","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui slept wonderfully, without a single dream, until dawn.","When Chunping, Xia’an, and the others attending her helped her rise, they saw her bare, unpowdered face glowing with health, its fair skin flushed with color. Smiles appeared on their faces as well.","While she was having breakfast, Shen Yanshui saw Dongyi hurrying in with a smile. She first offered her respects. “This servant greets Mistress.”","From Dongyi’s expression, Shen Yanshui could tell that she had learned some new news from outside. She asked, “What is it?”","Dongyi’s eyes shone brightly. “A moment ago, this servant heard from the little eunuch guarding Haoyue Residence that Lady Chu won’t be attending the Jinming Lake gathering for the Duanyang Festival this time. On my way back, I already saw quite a few of the young ladies heading to the Crown Princess’s residence.”","“Oh?” Shen Yanshui arched a brow. She was not surprised. Lady Chu did not seem like a foolish woman, and now that she appeared to be seven months pregnant, naturally she would put the child first.","Qiuyi, standing to the side, covered her lips and smiled. “With His Highness’s word, Mistress will certainly be able to go. There’s no need for her to rack her brains trying to curry favor with Her Highness the Crown Princess like the others.”","Dongyi lifted her chin and beamed. “Exactly. Our Mistress is the one His Highness favors.”","Chunping glanced at her, but she merely smiled without saying anything to dampen her spirits. She knew that Dongyi was quite composed in front of outsiders. It was only among their own people that she acted this way.","Not counting today, there were only two days left until the Duanyang Festival. But being able to accompany the Crown Prince and Crown Princess to the Jinming Lake gathering meant more than simply watching the festivities—it was also an excellent opportunity to make an appearance.","The Crown Princess would certainly be seated beside the Empress then, while the people of the Eastern Palace would naturally sit together with her.","If they could make themselves known before the Empress and win Her Majesty’s favor, His Highness the Crown Prince would presumably regard them with greater favor as well.","Not to mention that appearing at such an occasion would bring honor to their parents, sisters, and brothers back home. Their families would value them even more.","Therefore, during this period, while the list of those accompanying them had yet to be announced, everyone who wanted to go was using every means at their disposal.","Now that it had been confirmed Lady Chu would not be attending, their chances of going had clearly increased. Naturally, they became even more eager to curry favor.","Shen Yanshui merely treated it as a bit of gossip. After all, there had never been a shortage of people trying to ingratiate themselves with the Crown Prince and Crown Princess. Dongyi had said that the various residences had been sending the Crown Prince soups, snacks, and all sorts of food without pause.","At first, Chunping and the others had urged her to send something as well. She had indeed sent someone to inquire at the kitchen, but after learning how expensive it was to prepare food that would be served to the Crown Prince, she immediately abandoned the idea.","Besides, considering the Crown Prince’s appetite, he probably couldn’t finish everything anyway. What a waste...","*","It was nearing noon. The sky was clear from horizon to horizon, and the sun shone brightly.","“Godfather, Lady Wu from Haitang Court sent another soup just now. Should I take it in to His Highness?”","Zheng Yuande kicked him in the butt. “You’re foolish, and you truly live up to it. If His Highness had to eat everything people sent over, wouldn’t he be stuffed to death? Besides, you’ve been here for several days now. When have you ever seen His Highness touch any of this?”","Aside from the food the Crown Princess had sent in the past, which the Crown Prince would occasionally sample, he had never touched anything sent by the other women. After inadvertently drinking a bowl of deer-antler soup, His Highness had never again consumed any food sent by another woman.","That day, as was customary, when the Crown Prince finished handling official matters and left the study, she softly reported, “Your Highness, Qiefang Hall, Haitang Court, Zhuxiang Residence, and Lianxin Residence have all sent over soup, fruit, and pastries. Would Your Highness care to try some?”","If the Crown Princess had not sent something today, there would have been no need to ask. The food would simply have gone into his belly later.","“You can have it all.”","Cui Yu flicked his robe aside and tucked its hem into the leather belt around his waist. He was just about to practice his martial arts and loosen up in the courtyard when he suddenly glanced to the side and asked, “What did Lianxin Residence send?”","Zheng Yuande paused for a moment, then quickly understood. Smiling broadly, he reported, “In reply to Your Highness, Lianxin Residence sent a Chinese yam and goji berry soup. This servant has someone keeping it warm over a stove. Would Your Highness like to try it?”","Cui Yu nodded indifferently. “I’ll drink it later.”","After practicing as usual until a thin sheen of sweat covered him, he bathed and changed clothes. Zheng Yuande promptly brought him the soup at just the right temperature.","Cui Yu drank half a bowl and showed no intention of having another. But after meeting with several Eastern Palace officials to discuss matters, he glanced at the sky outside, rose, and ordered, “Go to Lianxin Residence.”","“Yes, Your Highness.”","Before Cui Yu had even stepped onto the corridor leading to the rear chambers, a little eunuch was already peering around near Moonlight Gate. From afar, he spotted the Crown Prince approaching. Delighted, the little eunuch hurried back toward Lianxin Residence.","He nearly collided with Quanshou upon entering.","Quanshou was startled and quickly tightened his hold on the things in his arms. These were grapevines and strawberry plants that Mistress had just obtained from the Directorate of Palace Servants!","“What are you running so fast for?” he asked with a frown.","This was Little Xing, an attendant who served Lady Liu. Usually, he was unfailingly respectful and eager to please the people in their eastern side hall. Why was he being so careless today?","Little Xing hurriedly apologized several times, but he did not even wait for Quanshou to say anything before quickly entering the western side hall.","Quanshou was not the sort to press his advantage. Seeing that Little Xing really was in a hurry, he did not hold it against him.","Dongyi happened to witness the scene. She had just begun to frown when, a moment later, the door opposite opened. Lady Liu emerged, elegantly and meticulously dressed, leaning on the arm of Yinping. Her expression even held a hint of excitement.","Dongyi was somewhat puzzled. It was already nearly time for the evening meal. Where was Lady Liu going at this hour?","She watched as Lady Liu slowly made her way toward the entrance, then scratched her forehead. Since she couldn’t figure it out, she decided not to think about it.","Just then, Quanshou suddenly ran over and said, “The Crown Prince is here!”","Dongyi had only just brightened at the news when she heard Eunuch Zheng’s voice beside the Crown Prince. But in the next instant, she saw Lady Liu nearly throw herself into the Crown Prince’s arms.","Dongyi immediately cursed inwardly: Cunning woman! So that was what Lady Liu had been planning.","“Your Highness?”","Lady Liu wore a light garment made from the fabric bestowed upon her by Her Majesty the Empress. Turning her most beautiful angle toward the Crown Prince, she spoke in a soft, delicate voice, feigning surprise and timidly saying, “This concubine has offended Your Highness. I beg Your Highness’s forgiveness.”","She could not contain her excitement.","Earlier that afternoon, she had learned from the eunuch she had recently spent a great deal of silver bribing that the Crown Prince had been the only one to drink the soup she sent. Ever since then, she had been quietly anticipating this moment.","That was why she had sent Little Xing, who served in her residence, to keep watch and find out what was happening. Even then, she had not been entirely certain that the Crown Prince was coming to Lianxin Residence.","His Highness had finally remembered her. He had truly come to see her at Lianxin Residence.","This time, she had to make him stay.","Cui Yu disliked strangers coming too close to him.","Glancing at the woman who had thrown herself straight into his arms, his voice turned icy cold. \"You have lost all sense of decorum. Tomorrow, the Crown Princess will send a senior palace maid to re-teach you the proper rules of conduct.\"","Lady Liu's face instantly drained of all color. Her slender frame swayed unsteadily, and the gaze she lifted to him was brimming with utter shame, fury, and disbelief.","Then, trembling all over and her face flushed bright red, she begged through tears, \"Your Highness, I know my wrongs now. I beg for Your Highness's mercy and forgiveness. I will never dare to do such a thing again!\"","Cui Yu's expression remained impassive, his voice even colder. \"Two months of confinement.\" With that, he turned on his heel and left, paying her no more heed.","\"Tha- thank you for Your Highness's mercy.\"","Zheng Yuande frowned and waved a hand in slight displeasure. Immediately, a pair of inner eunuchs stepped forward to lead the terrified, pale-faced Lady Liu, who had gone limp with shock, quickly into the side west hall. The entire Lotus Heart Garden fell silent at once.","Such a cheap little trick, and she dared to pull it in front of His Highness the Crown Prince? It was simply laughable. If that sort of thing ever worked, His Highness would never be able to walk a single step unimpeded. There would be hordes of fawning women throwing themselves into his arms every day.","Shen Yanshui had witnessed nearly the entire scene from start to finish, but the situation was clearly not one where it was appropriate for her to step forward. So she had stayed right where she was by the doorway, holding her respectful bow the whole time. After all, she had just seen the consequences play out right in front of her.","From what she had observed of the Crown Prince over the past while, she suspected Lady Liu had deliberately orchestrated the whole incident. If it had truly been an accident, he would never have punished her so severely.","Cui Yu climbed the stone steps, and when he saw Shen Yanshui still half-crouching there, holding her respectful greeting to him perfectly and unwaveringly, the slight displeasure he had been feeling softened into helpless amusement. He chuckled to himself, what a truly earnest, no-nonsense girl she was.","He lifted his hand to give her arm a light, supporting gesture to help her rise, but just as he was about to pull his hand back, his palm was gently wrapped by a soft little hand. His movement froze right there.","Shen Yanshui stood up naturally following the light pressure from his hand, and did not let go of him. She thought his hand was very nice to look at, and she loved the feeling of holding it.","The Crown Prince's hand was large, dry and firm, with long, well-defined knuckles. It was a strikingly handsome hand, the sort you would expect to see on a refined scholar, yet the palm bore a faint layer of calluses, and it always carried a subtle, pleasant scent of ink.","\"Your Highness has such a beautiful hand,\" she said to him with a sincere bright smile, as she met his downward gaze.","Cui Yu: \"... You are such a smooth talker.\" Even so, he did not pull his hand away.","Shen Yanshui murmured quietly under her breath, \"That's not being smooth-tongued, that's giving a sweet compliment.\" She did not believe there was anyone in the world who did not enjoy being praised.","Cui Yu glanced at her, his tone light as he said, \"Silver-tongued, that's what you are.\"","Shen Yanshui: ... She studied his expression carefully, and once she was certain he was in a good mood, she could not help but feel a little amused. She had never expected this man, who always looked so dignified and cold on the outside, to have a little tsundere side to him."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20: Simply... absurd, absurd","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui promptly changed the subject. Blinking, she asked with a smile, “Your Highness, are you hungry? Shall I have the servants bring in the meal?”","It wasn’t that Shen Yanshui had nothing else to say to the Crown Prince. First, she truly didn’t know him well enough to think of any profound topics. Second, she was feeling a little hungry herself—and he came by right around mealtimes every time. Wasn’t that a clear sign that he wanted to eat here?","So she felt there was nothing wrong with her question at all.","Wasn’t she simply showing concern for his well-being?","Cui Yu gave a slight nod. “Have the meal brought in.”","As usual, the table was laden with an array of exquisite dishes: meat, vegetables, soup, cold dishes, and fruit. As expected, Cui Yu ended up feeling a little overfull.","Looking at the goji berries floating in the chicken soup before him, he suddenly remembered something and said, “Don’t send me Chinese yam and goji berry soup next time.”","Seeing her look up from her bowl in apparent surprise, he fell silent for a moment. Realizing that his words might have been misunderstood, he added, “If you truly wish to send something, send fruit or the like instead.”","He simply wasn’t very fond of soups and other such watery dishes.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","But she had never sent him any soup at all, had she?","Could he have mistaken a soup sent by someone else for one from her?","She said nothing, but Cui Yu narrowed his eyes slightly at her expression. His voice immediately turned as cold as a gust of winter wind.","“That soup wasn’t sent by you?”","Shen Yanshui didn’t think there was anything wrong with not having sent him soup. After all, she wasn’t the only one who hadn’t sent him any. But still... being caught in such a misunderstanding made her feel inexplicably embarrassed—and a little uneasy.","She even began to wonder whether Lady Liu’s unusually bold actions earlier that day might have something to do with this...","Zheng Yuande’s heart gave a lurch. This was bad!","Who had sent the soup had originally been unimportant. But after the Crown Prince assumed it was from Lady Shen and even told her his preferences, learning that it had not been sent by her meant that the Crown Prince had just embarrassed himself, didn’t it?","Just as he was thinking this, a sharp, icy glance fell upon him. Zheng Yuande was instantly close to tears. His knees went weak, and he was about to plead guilty.","But at that moment, Shen Yanshui suddenly put on an astonished expression and said, “So Your Highness likes fruit? I know of a novel and delicious pastry. I’ll make some myself tomorrow and have someone deliver it to Your Highness for you to try. Would that be all right?”","Cui Yu: “...”","He had felt a faint trace of embarrassment and displeasure earlier, but it could hardly be called anger. More than anything, he felt that his last two remarks had made him look rather foolish.","It was all Zheng Yuande’s fault. The fool couldn’t even explain two simple sentences clearly!","Now that she had offered him a way out, he naturally took it, no longer pressing the matter.","“Mm,” he replied coolly.","Seeing this, Shen Yanshui quietly let out a sigh of relief.","The Crown Prince didn’t seem so difficult to placate after all.","After taking a walk to aid digestion, bathing, and changing clothes, the others withdrew. By then, the faint embarrassment Cui Yu had felt earlier had almost completely faded.","But as the two of them became entangled, he suddenly found himself inexplicably dissatisfied. Clasping her slender, supple waist, he thrust her hips forward with a sharp, forceful motion. Hearing the abrupt change in her voice, he asked hoarsely, “If tomorrow’s fruit doesn’t suit my tastes, what do you intend to do?”","A faint sheen of sweat dampened Shen Yanshui’s temples. Looking into his dark, heavy gaze, she couldn’t help taking a deep breath.","Honestly, why was this man still thinking about that? It was only a bowl of soup, wasn’t it? How could he possibly remember it even at a time like this? Was he looking down on her?","As Shen Yanshui watched the little bean swaying before her eyes, she immediately opened her mouth...","Cui Yu suddenly froze. His body shuddered, then tensed all at once, his sharp eyes growing even wider. “You... How dare you!” he scolded in a low, restrained voice.","The corners of Shen Yanshui’s eyes lifted slightly. His body certainly wasn’t saying the same thing.","And he still had the nerve to call her outrageous.","Was this outrageous? She hadn’t even begun to show him what outrageous really meant.","She decided to let him see for himself.","It was the middle of the night. The wind outside carried a faint chill, but the temperature inside the eastern side chamber of Lianxin Court continued to rise.","Shen Yanshui not only refused to stop, but also made him truly experience what it meant to have a silver tongue and a sharp wit.","Taking advantage of the moment when his self-control faltered, she quietly exerted a little force and, pressed against his taut body, turned and climbed on top.","Cui Yu’s abdomen jolted violently.","He was so shocked that he even forgot to scold her.","This... this was simply too absurd!","Yet when Shen Yanshui saw the astonishment in his eyes, she couldn’t help wanting to laugh.","But she absolutely couldn’t laugh aloud now. Otherwise, this man would surely become embarrassed and furious, and then she would have taken things too far.","Compared with his stubborn mouth, his body was far more honest.","After all, if he truly hadn’t wanted it, she couldn’t have so easily turned them into another position.","Besides, if one was going to work overtime at night, wouldn’t adding a little variety make it even more enjoyable?","It was an experience that stretched him more than any before, and the visual stimulation was something he had never encountered. As a result, Cui Yu surrendered faster than he ever had.","In an instant, his handsome face darkened, then flushed, then darkened again.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Though she was only momentarily stunned, Cui Yu still noticed.","The next moment, Shen Yanshui felt the world spin before her eyes. She was flipped completely over, ending up on her knees with her back to him...","There was an indescribable eagerness in Shen Yanshui’s heart, but she couldn’t see the dark, somber, turbulent look in Cui Yu’s eyes.","It wasn’t long before she discovered that beneath the refined, gentle exterior this man wore, he was actually more like a ferocious beast...","A man’s pride was truly terrifying.","Cui Yu had never before been so... utterly unrestrained.","Shen Yanshui cried out in bliss. “Wuwuwu... Your Highness... wuwuwu...”","Cui Yu: “...”","He had never seen a woman cry like that in front of him.","When Shen Yanshui noticed the faint look of disdain in his eyes, anger instantly surged through her. Wrapping her arms around his waist, she rubbed her entire tear-dampened face against him!","Cui Yu’s body went rigid in an instant, and his expression changed completely.","Forget it. His body certainly wasn’t lacking for this little bit of her tears now.","“I see you’ve truly grown bold enough to eat the heart of a bear and the gall of a leopard.” Cui Yu reached over from beside her and tugged free a rouge-red undergarment, wiping her face with it somewhat disdainfully.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Was he deliberately taking revenge on her? It felt as though he had rubbed her skin raw.","Hearing her call out in a soft, slightly hoarse voice that it hurt, Cui Yu paused. He immediately lightened his touch, though his tone remained cold and disdainful. “So delicate.”","With that, he casually tossed aside the small piece of rouge-red fabric in his hand.","Shen Yanshui muttered under her breath, “Has Your Highness never heard that women are made of water? The skin on my face is delicate and tender. How could I possibly compare with rough-skinned, thick-fleshed men like you?”","Cui Yu lifted his eyelids and gave her a sidelong glance, then looked over the disarray covering the bed. She truly was made of water—just the slightest touch, and water came spilling out...","He said nothing, yet Shen Yanshui somehow understood exactly what his gaze meant.","She glanced at the messy bedding, which was frankly too embarrassing to look at, and immediately gritted her teeth as she scrambled off him. “Your Highness had a hand in this too!”","Without even having time to put on her shoes, she ran as quickly as her weakened legs could carry her toward the bathing room, eager to save herself.","As she passed the clothes rack, she did not forget to snatch up one of his outer robes and wrap it around herself, calling for water as she went.","Cui Yu: “...”"]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21: Disposition","paragraphs":["Above the horizon, rosy clouds billowed and surged. Pale golden morning light broke through the layers of cloud, pouring down over the Great Yong imperial palace and enveloping it in a dazzling radiance.","All around the palace, the various residences had long since begun their new day. The courtyards of the Eastern Palace were likewise filled with their own stirrings, but Lotusheart Court remained steeped in silence.","The doors of the western side hall were shut tight, and its occupants had been confined within. The servants attending them had therefore grown even quieter and more cautious.","Chunping could not help glancing at the sky. It was almost past the time for breakfast, yet there was still no sign that the Crown Prince or her mistress intended to rise. She turned to look at Eunuch Zheng, who wore an utterly composed, unruffled expression.","She respectfully asked, “Eunuch Zheng, it’s almost past the time for breakfast. What do you think...?”","Zheng Yuande continued to maintain his calm expression. “Just wait.”","Last night, the Crown Prince and this young mistress had carried on until well into the night. He had already lost count of how many times they had shocked him.","Dark circles had formed beneath his eyes. Since His Highness had not rested, naturally he could not rest either.","And today was a day off from court... If there was still no movement after another quarter of an hour, they truly could not delay any longer. They could not let it upset His Highness’s stomach, after all.","Seeing that he was not in a hurry, Chunping felt reassured as well.","Shen Yanshui had actually been awake for a little while. Her body was soft and languid, however, and she did not feel like moving in the slightest, so she continued lying there with her eyes closed. But after a while, she gradually began to feel hungry...","Cui Yu had also awakened early. Yet for some reason, holding the person in his arms, he found himself unusually reluctant to rise as he normally did. Thinking of the previous night, he felt they had indulged themselves a little too much. In the future, he absolutely could not let things go so far again.","But since it had already happened, there was no need to get up just yet. Thus, he went back to sleep for a while.","When he awoke again, he heard someone calling out beside his ear with a trace of deep grievance, as though summoning his soul.","“Your Highness? Your Highness? Time to get up~”","Shen Yanshui tilted her head slightly and leaned close to his ear, calling to him in a soft voice.","When he finally lifted his eyelids, Shen Yanshui immediately looked at him with a radiant smile.","Thus, the first thing Cui Yu saw upon opening his eyes was her exceptionally bright and dazzling face.","Then, the next moment, a somewhat muffled “Gurgle~ gurgle~” came from beneath the covers.","Cui Yu: “...”","Meeting his gaze, Shen Yanshui said in a perfectly justified little voice, “Last night left me completely exhausted. Aren’t you tired too, Your Highness?”","She possessed an ability, and even she had ended up like this. She refused to believe he was not tired at all. After all, he had been the one to expend more effort.","“Not tired.” Cui Yu’s tone was calm and utterly certain.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Hah. Men. Even if the sky fell, they would still prop it up with their mouths.","With a sweet smile, she said gently, “I know Your Highness is vigorous and strong, with a robust constitution. Of course you wouldn’t be tired. But it should be nearly the Hour of the Dragon by now. It’s time to get up and eat.”","Cui Yu gave a faint hum.","Seeing this, Shen Yanshui immediately smiled and pulled the bell beside the bed.","Outside, Zheng Yuande had just been making preparations to enter and wake them. When he heard the movement inside, he immediately waved his hand. A procession of eunuchs and palace maids entered the room, carrying the things prepared for washing up.","The two of them each had servants attend to them as they dressed and washed. They were soon properly groomed, and after eating breakfast together, Cui Yu prepared to leave.","Just before departing, however, he suddenly turned his head toward her. Seeing the confusion in her clear eyes, he instructed her in a deep voice, “You will be going to Golden Bright Pool early the day after tomorrow. You must behave yourself that day and be obedient. Do not act recklessly again.”","Shen Yanshui’s eyes gleamed as she looked at him, her smile warm and radiant. “Yes. Thank you, Your Highness!”","Only after Cui Yu had left and she could no longer see him did Shen Yanshui rise and return to her room.","Chunping brought over a cup of warm tea and could not help smiling happily. Although the Crown Prince had previously asked whether her mistress wished to go watch the Dragon Boat Festival festivities at Golden Bright Pool, it had not been set in stone. Only now that the Crown Prince had spoken of it directly could it be considered certain.","It was just that the Crown Prince’s final words before leaving had been rather strange.","Although their mistress seemed somewhat bold in front of the Crown Prince, she was still very proper before the Crown Princess. She had never liked causing trouble, either. As for acting recklessly—her mistress did not seem to have done anything particularly outrageous, did she?","As she was thinking this, Xia’an asked in confusion, “Mistress, what did the Crown Prince mean by those last words?”","The Crown Prince had seemed to be in a good mood during the meal, yet there had been something inexplicably frightening about his tone when he left.","Shen Yanshui smiled but did not answer at once.","On the surface, it sounded as though he was telling her not to be too bold and cause trouble.","But in reality, was the Crown Prince also hinting—or warning her—to keep to her proper place and not get involved with Noble Consort Lan and the others?","Whatever. It was not worth worrying over.","She gave a light laugh and said, “Don’t let your imaginations run wild. Perhaps the Crown Prince simply saw that this is my first time attending such a royal banquet and was worried that I might accidentally cause trouble, so he offered a reminder. As long as we behave honestly and properly, then even if something does happen, it will have nothing to do with us.”","*","Zheng Yuande spent the entire journey back to the Hall of Eternal Celebration with his heart in his throat. The instant he returned and saw His Highness sit down, he dropped to his knees to beg forgiveness. His round, pale, plump cheeks trembled like steamed buns.","With a sob in his voice, he said, “Your Highness, this servant knows he was wrong. Please punish me.”","Cui Yu gave him an expressionless, cold glance. Seeing the dark circles beneath his eyes, he let out a cold snort.","“This time, I will let it pass. But if there is a next time...”","Zheng Yuande immediately took the hint and thanked him. “Thank you, Your Highness! Rest assured, there definitely will not be another time. If there is, this servant will go and receive thirty strokes of the cane!”","Cui Yu’s expression remained calm. “Go and find out who gave Lady Liu the information.”","Zheng Yuande’s heart instantly tightened. He no longer dared to act pitiful or curry favor before his master, and immediately went out to begin the investigation.","He already had a few suspects in mind.","The Eastern Palace appeared relaxed on the surface, but was tightly controlled underneath. He knew exactly what sort of people worked in the Hall of Eternal Celebration.","Since His Highness had never issued any special instructions before, and those few people had behaved well enough, he had not dealt with them. He had never expected that one of them would nearly trip him up!","Zheng Yuande’s heart hardened.","It did not take long before he returned, bent at the waist and treading lightly. Entering the study, he reported cautiously, “Your Highness, this servant has found the culprit. It was one of the Crown Princess’s people. This servant... does not know how she should be dealt with.”","At his words, Cui Yu showed no surprise. Although he had already suspected as much, his expression was still far from pleasant, and his voice turned even colder.","“Was it ordered by the Crown Princess?”","Zheng Yuande’s body trembled. He replied carefully, “It should not have been. The servant confessed everything just now. It was because she had become lovers with one of the palace maids serving in the Crown Princess’s residence and was short of money. In a moment of foolish greed, she accepted money from the Lady and passed along the information in advance.”","What His Highness ate and used—how could such things be casually revealed to outsiders?","Cui Yu’s expression softened somewhat, and he said calmly, “Deal with her according to palace regulations.”","Eunuch Zheng hurriedly acknowledged the order. “Yes, Your Highness.”","“Also, Lady Liu is to be confined to her quarters for half a year.”","Eunuch Zheng respectfully accepted the order, though inwardly he couldn’t help thinking, Serves her right!","Considering that Lady Liu had dared to bribe one of the servants attending the Crown Prince, her punishment was anything but undeserved."]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22: Milk Tea Egg Tarts","paragraphs":["In Lotus Heart Court, Shen Yanshui had just finished a set of Baduanjin exercises and cultivated for a while longer when she saw a lovely little parrot, bright green all over with a spot of orange-yellow on its forehead, flying toward her with obvious familiarity.","“Great beauty! Great beauty!”","Shen Yanshui held out a finger to tease it. “Such a sweet-talker, aren’t you? How come your master didn’t learn even a fraction of your way with words?”","Little Jade pecked lightly at her fingertip with its sharp beak. “Great beauty! Great beauty! This young master is hungry, hungry! Give me something to eat, something to eat!”","Shen Yanshui tapped its little head, then plucked two roses from the vines along the courtyard wall and infused them with a trace of her ability. “Here.”","But she had other things to do today, so she could not spend all her time playing with the bird.","“Come on. Let’s take a look at the main kitchen.”","The Eastern Palace kitchens were not located in Changqing Palace, but in a palace compound next door, separated only by a wall. They were large, spacious, and immaculate—her first impression at a glance.","A plump chief eunuch, round and smiling like the Maitreya Buddha, hurried over. Dressed in the neat uniform of a chief palace attendant, he beamed when he saw mistress and servant at the door.","“Oh my, this must be Lady Shen? This servant greets Lady Shen and pays his respects.”","Shen Yanshui smiled and replied politely, “Chief Steward Tang, there is no need for such ceremony. Please rise. I’ll be troubling you today.”","Chief Steward Tang’s face split into an even broader smile. “Lady Shen wishes to make some pastries for His Highness the Crown Prince. All you needed to do was send word and instruct us. Why come personally to a grimy place like the kitchen? What if your clothes or shoes should be soiled?”","Smiling, Shen Yanshui said, “From what I can see, the kitchen is managed by Chief Steward Tang in excellent order. It is very clean and tidy indeed. I only wonder whether I might hold up the kitchen’s work?”","Her words pleased Chief Steward Tang greatly. With a genial smile, he waved a broad hand. “What are you saying, Lady Shen? It’s only a matter of freeing up one stove. I’ll send two people to assist you and follow your instructions. Would that be acceptable?”","Shen Yanshui thanked him with genuine warmth. “That will be more than enough. Thank you for your trouble, Chief Steward Tang.”","Chief Steward Tang chuckled. “Lady Shen is far too polite.” With that, he immediately ordered two of his apprentices to go and help her.","Shen Yanshui had deliberately worn a short-sleeved, close-fitting top today, making it convenient to work in.","She planned to make egg tarts and milk tea.","In her previous life, she had loved milk tea, egg tarts, and all kinds of small cakes. She had even watched many online tutorials and learned to make them herself.","She had not had any in a very long time. Once the kitchen staff learned how to make them, she would be able to enjoy milk tea and egg tarts whenever she wished!","The most important parts of an egg tart were the custard filling and the flaky puff-pastry shell. The Eastern Palace kitchen had everything needed for both.","Anything they lacked could be made by hand. For molds, she used flower-shaped ones supplied by the kitchen. They were only half the size of modern egg tarts, and looked quite lovely.","As for the final baking, she had previously eaten the baked pastries from the kitchens and asked Dongyi about them. Learning that the Eastern Palace kitchens had an oven capable of baking egg tarts, she had decided to make these.","Otherwise, she could hardly ask the Eastern Palace kitchens to build a usable oven in a single day just so she could bake a few egg tarts, could she?","She began working in the kitchen with calm, orderly efficiency.","At first, the other kitchen staff had been rather restrained, but seeing that Lady Shen seemed even more at ease than they were, they gradually relaxed as well.","This was a relatively quiet time in the Eastern Palace kitchens. Most of the staff had been temporarily sent to the Imperial Kitchen to wrap rice dumplings, and over the past two days, the Eastern Palace kitchens had become much less crowded.","Quite a few people watched in secret, curious.","Chief Steward Tang was curious too. Early that morning, Quanfu from Lotus Heart Court had come to tell him that Lady Shen wished to borrow the kitchen’s oven. Naturally, he had no reason to refuse.","After all, Lady Shen currently held a certain degree of favor with His Highness the Crown Prince.","Had no one noticed that when Lady Shen’s allotted meals proved insufficient, the extra portions were taken from the Crown Prince’s own allowance? Though the Crown Prince had not permitted the matter to be publicized, and few people knew of it.","That fact alone was enough for him to wait upon this young mistress with the utmost care.","Still, he did not hold much hope that Lady Shen could make pastries that were truly delicious. He had even secretly instructed someone to prepare a portion of pastries that the Crown Prince particularly liked. Should they be needed later, it would make for a useful favor, would it not?","Shen Yanshui had no idea that someone had quietly arranged such a safeguard for her. Seeing that the two young eunuchs assigned to assist her neither watched closely to see how she worked nor did anything beyond what she instructed, she quickly understood why.","In these times, every household guarded its recipes and secret techniques closely. They likely thought she was making a Shen family specialty and thus did not dare watch too openly, lest she accuse them of trying to steal her craft.","Shen Yanshui turned and instructed them, “Remember how this is made. That way, you can make it for me in the future.”","The two young eunuchs froze.","Though they were nominally apprentices to the kitchen masters, those masters had many apprentices, and the two of them had not yet earned the qualifications to prepare food or pastries for noble masters. But now Lady Shen was going to teach them how to make pastries?","Their expressions shifted between shock and delight, though they could not help wondering whether they had misheard.","Yet in the next moment, Lady Shen began explaining the process to them, holding nothing back...","The pair immediately perked up and listened with rapt attention.","Seeing this, the others could not help pricking up their ears as well.","After Shen Yanshui finished explaining how to make egg tarts, she continued, “This is the tea I brought. Steep it in boiling water, then strain out the leaves, keeping only the rich, concentrated tea. Start another pot and pour in fresh milk. Simmer it slowly over low heat—do not let it boil over. Once tiny bubbles begin to form around the edges, remove it from the heat. Slowly pour the brewed tea into the milk, stirring as you pour, so that the tea and milk blend together.”","“...Add a little honey or condensed milk to adjust the sweetness, allowing it to balance the fragrance of the milk and tea... Once it is done, strain it once more through fine gauze...”","“Next, take the finest tapioca flour and scald it with boiling water. Knead it into a firm, smooth dough, then pinch it into tiny pearls no bigger than a fingertip.”","“Boil them until they turn translucent throughout and have a pleasing chew. Scoop them out and rinse them once in cool water, then toss lightly with honey to keep them from sticking together. They must be chewy yet tender—neither undercooked nor overboiled.”","“...Choose taro with a soft, floury texture. Peel it and cut it into thick slices, then steam them until they collapse at the slightest poke. Take them out and let them cool slightly before pressing them into a fine, smooth paste with the back of a spoon. There must not be the slightest impurity. Mix in a little milk and honey, stirring until it is dense and velvety, melting on the tongue without a single lump...”","Some listened with rapt attention, but others were unimpressed and found Lady Shen’s ostentatious behavior rather hard to stomach.","Fan Chuan was one of those who looked down on Lady Shen most of all.","He was one of the Crown Princess’s people. His position alone set him apart from the lesser ladies who lived in the rear quarters, and he held himself in high regard. In the kitchens of the Eastern Palace, apart from Tang Hai—that damned fat man—who could faintly overshadow him, he feared no one.","Fan Chuan frowned and curled his lip disdainfully, deeply displeased by Lady Shen’s actions.","Was she not merely relying on the few favors the Crown Prince had bestowed upon her to behave this way?","If every woman who gained a measure of the Crown Prince’s favor acted like her—using the excuse of preparing food for His Highness to come and go from the Eastern Palace kitchens whenever she pleased—would that not utterly ruin the rules?","And if something were to happen to the food intended for the Crown Prince or the Crown Princess, who would bear the responsibility?","That damned fat man Tang Hai was so eager to bow and scrape, yet he could not even tell whom he ought to curry favor with. How laughable.","But then... his eyes shifted, and an idea came to him. He untied the apron at his waist, gave his apprentice a few quiet instructions, and, while no one was paying attention, slipped out of the Eastern Palace kitchens and headed in the direction of Xiefang Hall."]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23: An inexplicable discomfort in my heart","paragraphs":["The Crown Princess was dressed in a dark-purple long robe with wide sleeves, embroidered with peonies and gold scrolling vines, and crowned with a gold-inlaid red-jade peony headdress. At that moment, she sat upright and meticulously composed in a rosewood chair, watching the person standing in the middle of the hall. Her brows drew together slightly.","“Is what you said true?”","Fan Chuan bowed deeply and answered respectfully, “In response to Your Highness, even if this servant had a hundred times the courage, he would never dare deceive you. The Eastern Palace kitchens are in quite an uproar at the moment. Your Highness need only send someone over to investigate and you’ll know.”","“That Lady Shen is, at any rate, the daughter of an official household. How could she truly know how to cook? Isn’t she merely putting on an act to vie for His Highness’s favor? Who knows what a mess she’s made of the kitchens by now.”","At this, the Crown Princess’s brows knitted even more tightly. Though her expression was displeased, she did not speak immediately. She merely waved for Fan Chuan to leave.","Fan Chuan was puzzled, but he did not dare question his mistress’s decision. As he departed, he felt the purse Hongling had given him tucked inside his sleeve. One squeeze of his fingers told him roughly how much it contained, and a satisfied smile spread across his face.","This trip had certainly been worth it!","The Crown Princess’s expression remained displeased. “Whenever Lady Shen comes to pay her respects, she appears obedient enough and never takes the initiative to cause trouble. But she has never been the sort to suffer a loss in silence. It hasn’t even been a month, yet His Highness has already spoiled her into becoming increasingly presumptuous.”","Matron Zhou frowned beside her. “Your Highness is right. Lady Shen is likely hiding wickedness beneath that obedient exterior.”","“Lady Wu may appear ostentatious in her daily conduct, but she has never once managed to show off in front of Lady Shen. On the contrary, she has suffered no small losses at Lady Shen’s hands every time.”","“It seems we were all deceived by her meek and deferential appearance and mistook her for someone docile.”","“Now that she has revealed her true colors, she is no longer anything to fear.” After all, the favored Lady Shen in the palace was her elder sister by birth, and she had always been a thorn in the Crown Prince’s heart.","“If she truly becomes more and more presumptuous now that she has His Highness’s favor, then given His Highness’s temperament, he will soon grow tired of her,” Matron Zhou continued, suddenly lowering her voice. “Moreover, during the Dragon Boat Festival gathering at Golden Bright Lake the day after tomorrow, as long as she and Lady Shen speak privately for a few more words...”","What would the Crown Prince think then?","A flicker passed through the Crown Princess’s eyes.","*","It was noon, and the sky was clear and blue beneath the blazing sun.","Zheng Yuande carefully carried a purplewood, black-lacquered, mother-of-pearl-inlaid, eight-sided box decorated with flowers and birds. He stepped forward and bowed slightly as he reported in a quiet voice, “Your Highness, these are the pastries and drink Lady Shen has just delivered herself. She said that Your Highness must taste the pastries while they’re still warm, as they won’t be as delicious once they cool. This servant didn’t dare delay. Please take a look...”","Under ordinary circumstances, while the Crown Prince was handling official business, Zheng Yuande would never dare interrupt him with food sent by one of the lesser ladies living in the rear quarters. But today, Lady Shen’s matter was clearly different from usual.","After all, he had also been at fault for yesterday’s incident. Naturally, he ought to lend her a hand now.","Cui Yu raised his head from the documents and instinctively pressed his fingers to his brow.","With a smile, Zheng Yuande said, “Your Highness, these pastries and this drink were made personally by Lady Shen using ingredients borrowed from the Eastern Palace kitchens. It’s clear she put great thought into them.”","Cui Yu lifted a brow at that. “Made personally by her?”","Zheng Yuande’s smile instantly widened. He hurriedly affirmed it, then placed the box on a nearby table. He opened the container holding the still-steaming golden pastries, and a rich, enticing fragrance of eggs and milk filled the room.","“Your Highness, please have a taste.”","Cui Yu looked at the golden pastries and picked one up. After taking a bite, his brows rose slightly.","Zheng Yuande watched him nervously. Although he had already tested the food himself, he had no idea whether it would suit His Highness’s taste...","Just as he was thinking this, he saw the Crown Prince eat another, and then a third before finally stopping.","Zheng Yuande immediately put on a broad smile and promptly offered him a clean towel that had just been rinsed.","Cui Yu accepted it and slowly, unhurriedly wiped his fingertips. His tone was indifferent.","“Acceptable.”","Zheng Yuande was even more delighted. Lady Shen truly knew how to please His Highness. Not only had she made something fresh, but His Highness clearly enjoyed it as well.","Cui Yu then glanced at the sweet white porcelain jug nearby. Zheng Yuande quickly poured the Crown Prince a cup, then opened two small porcelain containers and said with a beaming smile, “Your Highness, Lady Shen said this drink is called milk tea. She made it using the tea leaves Your Highness bestowed upon her. She specifically instructed this servant to have Your Highness taste it first and see whether the sweetness is suitable. If it seems too bland, Your Highness may add some of the tapioca pearls and taro paste.”","Cui Yu took a sip. It was smooth and velvety as soon as it entered his mouth, sliding gently down his throat. It was neither bitter nor overly rich, leaving only the full fragrance of milk and tea. The sweetness was just right—sweet without being cloying, mellow and gentle.","He scooped a spoonful each of the tapioca pearls and taro paste into the cup.","The pearls were springy and chewy, carrying a faint sweetness. Mixed with the dense, soft taro paste, they were powdery, sticky, and delicate, melting in his mouth.","By the time he came back to himself, more than half the jug of milk tea had already been emptied.","Only then did he slowly set it down. Suddenly remembering something, he asked in a casual tone, “What sort of food did she send before?”","Yesterday’s incident had merely been an accidental misunderstanding that had cost him a little face. He was not so petty as to hold a grudge over it.","He had never cared about what food any woman sent him. But now that he knew she had been so sincere, he suddenly thought it a pity that the pastries she had made herself, piece by piece, had likely all ended up in Zheng Yuande’s stomach.","“Ah?”","Zheng Yuande froze. He had not expected His Highness to suddenly ask such a question—and it was truly rather difficult to answer...","Cui Yu’s voice deepened. “What is it? Did all the food go into your head instead?”","Zheng Yuande’s plump, fair body trembled in fright. Seeing that His Highness was still staring at him with furrowed brows, he replied awkwardly, “In response to Your Highness, Lady Shen... she... she has never sent any food before.”","After saying this, he wished he could bury his head in his chest. He did not dare look at His Highness’s expression at all.","The study instantly fell so silent that one could hear a pin drop.","Zheng Yuande felt the pressure around the Crown Prince growing heavier and heavier. His legs suddenly went weak, and he dropped to his knees.","After a long moment, Cui Yu cast him a glance and asked in his usual calm voice, “Why are you kneeling?”","Zheng Yuande cautiously raised his head. “...Your Highness?”","That was it? He was no longer angry?","Cui Yu raised a brow. “Do you wish to kneel?”","Seeing his expression and demeanor, Zheng Yuande’s heart immediately relaxed. He scrambled to his feet and hurriedly thanked His Highness.","Still, he remained deeply puzzled inside. His Highness’s moods seemed to be changing faster and faster lately...","Cui Yu noticed the confusion in his eyes but had no intention of explaining.","At first, he had naturally felt uncomfortable upon hearing the answer. Though he did not know where that inexplicable discomfort had come from, he had not thought deeply about it.","Then he suddenly remembered that, in the past, even Lady Shen’s regular allowance had not been enough to feed her. She had needed to spend additional money every day just to supplement it and eat her fill. She was only a concubine-born daughter of her family, so even if she had some private savings, she could not possibly have had much.","Moreover, she was straightforward and sincere by nature. It was only natural that she had not thought of currying favor in this way.","Over the past month or so, of the four newcomers, she alone had done nothing unnecessary. She had never secretly spent money to curry favor with people and make inquiries about the Eastern Palace, nor had she sent anyone to find out about his whereabouts or preferences. Every day, she simply lived her own quiet little life, keeping well within the rules.","That was good.","He turned his gaze toward the sky outside, set aside the documents before him for the time being, and rose to his feet. “Let’s go to Lianxin Court.”","Zheng Yuande hurriedly acknowledged the order, but inwardly grew even more puzzled. Unable to help himself, he scratched the back of his head. Why did he feel that he was becoming less and less able to fathom the Crown Prince’s thoughts?"]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24: So soft and gentle, as if acting cute","paragraphs":["After Shen Yanshui returned to Lotus Heart Court, she had Dongyi distribute the little egg tarts she had specially brought back among Chunping, Quanfu, and the others. She had already eaten in the kitchen, so she kept a cup of milk tea with tapioca pearls and taro paste to drink later.","Looking at the golden pastries and breathing in their sweet, tempting fragrance, everyone smiled and bowed in unison.","“Thank you for the reward, Mistress.”","They were still on duty, however, and none of them were ignorant of proper etiquette. Naturally, they would wait until they took turns going off duty before eating in their own rooms, or warm the tarts in the tea room first.","At ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍any rate, they could not disregard the rules and eat them right in front of their mistress.","Shen Yanshui then had some water brought in and took a bath. Although she had not needed to do everything herself in the kitchen, she had nevertheless picked up some of its mingled odors.","As she sat before the dressing mirror, her gaze fell upon the hibiscus-pink crystal jewelry set beside her, which glittered even more brilliantly beneath the sunlight. Suddenly inspired, she said, “Xia'an, redo my hair and put this set on me.”","Xia'an smiled and stepped forward to acknowledge the order.","After a while, once the styling was complete, Xia'an could not help exclaiming at the sight of her mistress in the mirror, “Mistress, you truly look like a celestial beauty...”","Even though she saw her every day, she was still occasionally stunned by her mistress’s beauty.","Chunping and Qiuru, standing nearby, blushed faintly and hurried to echo her praise. Shen Yanshui was so delighted that her heart bloomed with joy, and she could not help admiring herself thoroughly in the mirror.","What a pity—if cameras had existed, she would absolutely have taken several pictures to keep as mementos.","Only after she had finally admired herself to her heart’s content did Shen Yanshui turn her attention to the things in their hands. Chunping smiled and reported, “Mistress, tomorrow is the Duanyang Festival. We were just preparing to decorate the courtyard, so we can ward off evil and avert calamity for you.”","Shen Yanshui smiled. “You’ve all been very thoughtful.”","Then she looked toward the pile of small items in Qiuru’s arms and casually picked up a brightly colored cloth toy.","“Who made this little tiger?”","Xia'an replied with a smile, “Mistress, Qiuru made it. We never realized before that she was so skilled at making cloth tigers.”","Shen Yanshui praised her without reservation. “It really is beautifully made.” In any case, it was far better than anything Shen Yanshui herself could have made.","During the Duanyang Festival, families often placed tigers around the house to drive away evil and ward off misfortune. Many even dressed their children in tiger robes and tiger hats, making them look like little tigers in the hope of protecting them from evil and keeping them healthy and strong.","Qiuru pressed her lips together shyly. “It’s only a crude little craft. I hardly deserve your praise, Mistress.”","Shen Yanshui smiled. “If it’s well made, then it’s well made. Why shouldn’t you be praised for it?”","As she spoke, she looked down at the little tiger in her hand. It had an impressively fierce expression, though it was also rather adorable. She played with it lovingly for a while before setting it down.","Seeing the things they were holding, and finding herself with nothing else to do, Shen Yanshui decided to find herself a task. She smiled and said, “Bring the ladder over...”","When Cui Yu arrived, he happened to see her holding calamus leaves and mugwort, standing atop a tall ladder and hanging them above the doorway.","“This servant greets Your Highness.”","Qiuru, who had been about to scatter realgar powder at the courtyard gate, was startled when she saw the Crown Prince. She hurriedly dropped to her knees and paid her respects.","The others, hearing this, hastily set down their work and followed suit.","Shen Yanshui naturally turned around as well. A flicker of surprise crossed her face. “Your Highness?” she said, immediately preparing to climb down.","Cui Yu’s heart clenched at the sight. His Adam’s apple bobbed faintly as he said in a low voice, “There’s no need to hurry. Come down slowly.”","Shen Yanshui failed to notice anything amiss and nimbly descended the ladder.","Quanshou, who was still prostrated on the ground, had been hesitating over whether he could get up to receive his mistress before the Crown Prince dismissed them. Then a corner of a dark robe, embroidered with subdued silver patterns of four-clawed pythons, suddenly appeared before his eyes. He immediately lay still, obediently keeping his face pressed to the ground.","Cui Yu reached out and gripped Shen Yanshui’s forearm. Only then did she realize that he seemed to be holding her rather tightly...","Once he saw that she was safely on the ground, Cui Yu’s expression darkened. Turning toward the servants kneeling throughout the courtyard, he said coldly, “What are you all good for? You allowed your mistress to put herself in danger. What use is there in keeping any of you?”","Everyone instantly grew terrified and knocked their heads against the ground, begging forgiveness.","Shen Yanshui had not expected him to lose his temper so violently. She was startled before she came to her senses. Seeing his grim expression, as though his next order would be to punish them all, her heart gave a frightened leap.","But she soon realized that he was angry because he had been worried she might fall, and her composure returned.","If Chunping, Quanfu, and the others were punished merely because she had climbed a ladder, that would be far too unjust.","She tentatively caught hold of a corner of his sleeve, cautiously peeking at his darkened expression as she said in a hesitant, pleading tone, “Please don’t be angry, Your Highness. I was the one who insisted on climbing up there. How could they, as servants, have stopped me?”","Cui Yu cast her a sidelong glance. Only then did he notice that she had changed into a hibiscus-colored, high-waisted silk skirt.","The light fabric, as soft as smoke in the fifth month, carried a delicate hue like a lotus just beginning to bloom, setting off her skin to appear even more luminous and pale.","The high-waisted bodice wrapped snugly around her full breasts, outlining her lush, undulating curves and soft, supple skin.","The hibiscus-pink crystal ornaments in her hair, at her ears, and around her neck radiated a gentle, crystalline glow. The stones were clear as water, shimmering with a faint sheen of sunlight as they sparkled among her cloudlike locks. Their radiance mingled with the hibiscus hue of her dress until it was impossible to tell whether her beauty illuminated the fabric or the jewels lent their glow to her features.","She resembled a water lotus fresh from the stream, its morning dew not yet dry—a sight that made it impossible to look away.","Cui Yu’s eyes shifted faintly, but he continued to keep his face cold and said nothing.","Shen Yanshui secretly hooked her finger around his little finger and gave it a gentle tug. When he still did not react, she grew even bolder and wrapped both arms tightly around one of his.","Then she tipped her chin up and gazed at him imploringly. “Your Highness, I know I was wrong. I shouldn’t have relied on my agility and climbed up and down without regard for the danger.”","However, she changed her tone, a hint of grievance showing on her face. “You know I used to play cuju and polo all the time. I’m very nimble, and I hardly ever fall. Please don’t let it upset you so much that you make yourself ill~”","Her voice was soft and sweet, as though she were acting spoiled. Yet there was an unmistakable note of grievance in it, and the lingering lilt at the end of her words curled like a little hook, burrowing straight into Cui Yu’s ears.","The softness pressed firmly against his arm made his muscles tense unconsciously. He lowered his eyes to look at her, his gaze dark and fathomless. His usually cool voice carried an unfamiliar, low rasp. “You’re quite skilled? Nimble, are you?”","Shen Yanshui met his deep, turbulent gaze and suddenly had the inexplicable feeling that something was not quite right...","Cui Yu stared at her darkly for a long while before turning his eyes toward the servants of Lianxin Court kneeling in the courtyard. His voice was cold as he said, “This time, your mistress pleaded for mercy on your behalf, so I will let it go. But if there is a next time, you needn’t remain at Lianxin Court.”","Chunping, Quanfu, and the others immediately trembled as they kowtowed and thanked him for his mercy.","Shen Yanshui breathed a sigh of relief, but at the same time, she became even more wary.","Just then, she noticed him glance in her direction. His crow-black lashes lowered, concealing his dark eyes. She heard him say coldly, “Come inside with me.”","His voice sounded icy and distant. With that, he turned and walked into the room.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Something seemed vaguely amiss, but for the moment, she couldn’t put her finger on what.","In the end, she followed him inside.","“Close the door.”","Shen Yanshui paused, then obediently turned around and shut the door.","“Your Highness?” She felt a little uneasy. He sat upright on the couch, his expression blank as he watched her, and she had no idea what he meant to do.","Cui Yu looked at her and said in an even tone, “Come here.”"]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25: Shy and Bashful","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui walked over lightly. Only when she drew close, under the somewhat dim light, could she clearly make out his expression. Something about him seemed a little strange...","“Your Highness, what’s wrong? Are you feeling unwell?” she asked with concern.","Cui Yu glanced up at her but did not answer for a moment.","He had never expected his body to react simply because she came so close to him. Naturally, he would never say such a thing aloud.","Seeing his cold, expressionless face, Shen Yanshui had initially felt somewhat uneasy. But when her gaze inadvertently swept over a certain place, her mind went blank for a moment.","Shen Yanshui: “...” What happened? Had someone drugged the Crown Prince?","A foolish thought suddenly flashed through her mind. Fortunately, she only thought it and did not say it aloud. After all, this was the Eastern Palace. Who would dare drug the Crown Prince? Did they have a death wish?","In the blink of an eye, she quickly racked her memory and finally realized what was probably going on.","But looking at his cold, impassive face as he sat there in silence, she suddenly felt an irresistible urge to tease him.","With a worried look on her face, she went over and sat down beside him. Resting one hand lightly on his shoulder, she asked gently, “Your Highness, what’s wrong? Are you still angry?”","Before he could answer, Shen Yanshui lightly patted his somewhat tense chest. “Anger is bad for your health. Please don’t be angry, Your Highness. How about I massage your shoulders as an apology?”","When Shen Yanshui saw his ears suddenly turn red, she found it immensely amusing. At that moment, she felt just like a little temptress clinging to him, eager to see how long this Crown Prince—always so serious and aloof by day—could keep enduring it.","Suddenly, her wrist was seized by a large, finely jointed hand. Cui Yu’s gaze was deep and dark.","“An apology?”","Shen Yanshui’s heart jolted. For some inexplicable reason, she felt as if she had suddenly fallen under the dangerous gaze of a ferocious beast.","Before she could respond, the force of his hand pulled her abruptly into his arms, leaving her seated on his lap.","The next moment, she felt it with startling clarity.","Shen Yanshui: “...” That change was a little too fast, wasn’t it?","Cui Yu had never considered himself a gentleman. It was simply that he had never been particularly interested in matters of the bedchamber.","Yet at some point, something seemed to have changed.","Cui Yu raised a hand and pulled at her sash.","Shen Yanshui’s hand shyly slipped through the opening in the hem of his black robes. At the same time, unable to resist the sight of his handsome features, she lowered her eyes and kissed him.","Cui Yu: “...”","The instant their lips touched, Shen Yanshui noticed that his entire body suddenly stiffened. He stopped moving.","Shen Yanshui: “...?”","She looked at him. His brows were slightly furrowed as he lowered his eyes to stare at her, his gaze as black and fathomless as an abyss. She suddenly felt that perhaps she could not continue kissing him...","Uneasily, she drew back a little. Sure enough, being close to the ruler was like sleeping beside a tiger—the ancients had not been wrong!","Her fingers also unconsciously began to slow.","“Your Highness?”","She truly could not tell whether he was refusing her or what he meant. His inexplicable reaction left her completely bewildered.","Cui Yu caught the hand she was preparing to withdraw. “Continue.” His voice was so hoarse that it was almost unrecognizable.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","What was he trying to say? Was he treating her like nothing more than a tool, yet refusing even to kiss her?","For once, she was furious—but in the end, she only dared to be furious for a moment...","Then she suddenly remembered that, the last few times, he had never kissed her on the lips either. Every time, he had started from...","She let out a cold huff inwardly. Hmph. Men!","She ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍couldn’t help grumbling to herself: If you’re so capable, then don’t use your mouth anywhere at all! I haven’t even complained about you, and you’re already finding fault with me?","As if she cared about kissing him!","Shen Yanshui secretly cast a glance at his neatly arranged clothing, then opened her mouth and bit him on the neck. Listening to the change in his voice from its usual cool composure, she began tormenting him with her hands, taking a rather malicious pleasure in getting her revenge...","Then she suddenly felt his entire body stiffen like stone, the muscles in his legs becoming especially taut.","Cui Yu buried his face against her shoulder to regain his composure. After a long while, he put an arm around her slender waist and slowly straightened up.","A fine sheen of sweat covered his forehead, yet the expression on his face had already returned to normal—calm and unruffled as ever. Shen Yanshui secretly curled her lips.","As though by accident, she waved her still-moist hand beneath his eyes and said, with a bashful, troubled air, “Your Highness, what are we to do?”","As she spoke, she cast a pointed glance at the noticeably darker patch spreading across his clothing.","Fortunately, he was wearing dark robes today. Unless one looked closely, it was impossible to notice.","There was a fleeting trace of awkwardness on Cui Yu’s face, though it vanished almost at once. After all, this was the first time they had indulged themselves in broad daylight...","He calmly reached for the teacup. Glancing at her flushed palm, he said without batting an eye, “Rinse it.”","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Fine. At least this counted as the Crown Prince personally attending to her while she washed her hands.","After she had quickly rinsed her hand, she saw him pour another cup of tea over himself with the same smooth, natural efficiency.","The tea immediately soaked into the fabric, leaving his clothes thoroughly damp. The indescribable scent lingering in the air was diluted considerably by the fragrance of the pre-rain Longjing tea.","Shen Yanshui merely gave him a soft snort at this entire cleanup operation and said nothing. She hurriedly slipped down from his lap.","Though, truth be told, her own clothes were hardly in any better condition.","Her cross-collared jacket had somehow become a front-opening garment, while the begonia-red bodice beneath it had long since been pulled far from where it belonged. Her clothes were wrinkled everywhere, and she could hardly bear to look at herself. She felt a pang of distress as well—these garments were made from fine, expensive materials and needed to be carefully tended. Now they had been ruined by him...","Cui Yu looked up and caught the faintly accusing glance in her eyes. Then he looked at her clothes...","Cui Yu: “...”","He turned his head away and coughed lightly before saying in a low voice, “I’ll have some fabric sent to you later.”","Only then did Shen Yanshui finally smile. “Thank you, Your Highness. Please summon Eunuch Zheng to attend to you at once. You mustn’t catch cold. I’ll go inside and change first.”","With that, she swayed gracefully into the inner room.","Cui Yu: “...”","However, he did not immediately summon someone to attend to him. Instead, as though something had suddenly occurred to him, his brows drew together slightly, and he raised a hand to touch his lips without thinking.","He had never kissed anyone on the lips. Yet he knew of such things; he had seen men and women feeding one another with their mouths and tongues. Even a single extra glance had disgusted him, as though it sullied his eyes.","Nor had he ever entertained such a thought.","Cui Yu unconsciously pressed his lips together. Yet that brief sensation just now... seemed not to have repulsed or disgusted him as much as he had imagined it would.","Still, deep down, he instinctively felt that it was somehow unclean.","“Your Highness?” Zheng Yuande’s cautious voice suddenly sounded from outside.","Cui Yu’s voice darkened. “What is it?”","Zheng Yuande promptly replied, “Your Highness, Cao Zhongda has just sent word that Lord Xiao is currently waiting in the front hall.”","Cui Yu frowned. Lowering his eyes and finding that there was nothing obviously amiss, he rose and left the room. Before departing, he turned to the eunuch waiting deferentially to one side and said, “Tell your mistress that I have official business to attend to in the front hall, and will be leaving first.”","He had not intended to leave any particular instruction. But he had originally come here to have lunch with her, and in the end... If he finished and left immediately, it would make it seem as though he had come solely for that purpose.","Quanfu did not dare raise his head. Bowing deeply, he answered respectfully, “Yes.”","But the moment Zheng Yuande caught sight of the disheveled state of the Crown Prince’s clothes, he cried out in alarm, “Oh dear! Your Highness, what happened to your garments? How did you get tea spilled all over yourself?”","Cui Yu frowned. The damp fabric clung tightly to his body, making him uncomfortable, and he was even less inclined to listen to Zheng Yuande’s fussing. “It is nothing. I accidentally spilled some tea just now. Let us go.”","Zheng Yuande repeatedly assented, then hurriedly instructed someone to return and prepare a fresh set of clothes. How could the Crown Prince possibly meet anyone while wearing wet garments?","He could not help grumbling inwardly. What was Lady Shen doing? Did she not know how to attend to His Highness properly? Honestly...","Then he remembered that, before leaving, His Highness had specifically instructed that little eunuch to inform Lady Shen. That was something he had never done before...","Zheng Yuande forcibly swallowed his dissatisfaction. Forget it, forget it. If His Highness himself was not angry, what right did he have to be angry on his behalf?"]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26: Who on earth made up this rumor","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui did not need Quanfu to pass the message along. She had heard every word clearly from inside her inner chambers, yet she did not rush out immediately. Instead, she changed her clothes at a leisurely pace, taking her time to adjust her attire properly.","A moment later, Chunping stepped in softly to help her finish dressing, though her face could not hide her tense, anxious expression. She had no idea what had transpired between the Crown Prince and her mistress inside the room. All she had seen was the Crown Prince storming in with a dark, heavy look on his face, only to walk out moments later, his whole body splattered with tea, before leaving without a word...","And her mistress had not even come out to bow and see him off properly.","Fretting with worry, she said, \"My lady, about the Crown Prince...\"","Shen Yanshui looked as calm and composed as ever, smiling at her gently. \"It's nothing. Don't worry.\"","Chunping fell silent. Who would not be trembling with fear after seeing the Crown Prince in such a state? Especially since he had come out of their mistress's room looking that way, how could she not be anxious?","Shen Yanshui was actually in a rather good mood. The thought of that man walking off unaware that the teeth mark she had left on him was still there, and that he would have to meet his subordinates like that, made her wonder what kind of expression he would make once he noticed it. Truly, her mood was excellent.","Cui Yu was indeed meeting people right then, and more than one person at that.","But during the entire meeting, the two men before him kept their heads bowed, staring at the ground and not daring to lift their eyes. Frowning in confusion, he asked after they had finished discussing official matters, \"Is there anything else you wish to report?\"","Yu Qinghe immediately bowed deeply. \"Your Highness, there are still some official duties at the Prefectural Magistrate's Office that I must attend to. This official shall take his leave now.\"","Cui Yu nodded to dismiss him, then turned his gaze to Xiao Zhengshan, the commander of the Eastern Palace guards.","Xiao Zhengshan fell silent, watching the man who had been standing right beside him just a moment ago scurry away like a frightened mouse. He gritted his teeth inwardly, that old fox can run faster than anyone else!","\"Speak. What is it?\"","Xiao Zhengshan lifted his eyes slightly, only to catch a glimpse of a faint teeth mark peeking out from under the hem of the Crown Prince's collar. He immediately lowered his head even further, and his sun-tanned face flushed a deep shade of red. How on earth was he supposed to say such a thing to the Crown Prince?","He cursed the fleeing old fox in his heart again.","Cui Yu furrowed his brows. \"Speak.\"","Xiao Zhengshan flinched, and finally, stammering and bright red in the face, he said with his head still lowered, \"Your Highness, your... your appearance is slightly improper. Perhaps you should call Eunuch Zheng in to help you tidy up?\"","Cui Yu's brows shifted. Seeing the odd look on Xiao Zhengshan's face, a bad premonition crept into his mind. He waved his hand to dismiss everyone.","Xiao Zhengshan let out a huge sigh of relief and quickly scurried away.","He could not help but wonder, what bold woman would dare to bite the Crown Prince...","Cui Yu did not call for Zheng Yuande. Instead, he went to the inner chamber of his study alone.","Because of his clothes, he had not allowed any palace attendants to help him change after returning to the Changqing Palace, and had changed his garments all by himself before coming to meet the two men who had been waiting for him.","But when he stood in front of the bronze mirror, his eyes suddenly froze. He tilted his head slightly, pulled down the collar of his robe to expose his neck, and his face instantly turned dark, then flushed bright red, shifting through a whole range of colors...","Finally, his face dark and stormy, he roared, \"Zheng Yuande, get in here this instant!\"","At the sound of that voice, Zheng Yuande's whole plump, pale body trembled in fright. He stumbled and rolled his way into the room.","\"Y-your Highness...\"","In the Changqing Palace, any matter related to the Crown Prince, even the smallest hint of gossip, would be probed and pored over endlessly by everyone.","It was even more so today. In the afternoon, the Crown Prince had gone to the Lotus Heart Courtyard in a fury, and had gone inside the room with Lady Shen for a very long time. He had not even stayed for the noon meal, and had instead emerged from the Lotus Heart Courtyard soaked all over in tea, looking utterly disheveled.","The news had spread not just to the back quarters, but almost the entire Changqing Palace. No one could remember the usually fastidious Crown Prince ever looking so much in disarray before. Everyone was guessing that Lady Shen must have been so spoiled and arrogant that she had offended and enraged the Crown Prince.","This very reasonable-sounding speculation made countless people eagerly wait to see what would happen next.","The Crown Princess frowned, deep in thought. \"This Lady Shen...\"","Matron Zhou smiled. \"Your Highness, I'm afraid we won't even need to wait until tomorrow. Lady Shen will likely have already lost the Crown Prince's favor.\"","A faint smile tugged at the Crown Princess's lips. She was more than happy to see that happen.","When Lady Wu heard the news, her eyes lit up with delight, and she could barely hold back a laugh.","\"She was so arrogant and smug! Now there's a wonderful show to watch! Go, find out more details.\" She even had the audacity to personally go to the palace kitchen to make snacks for the Crown Prince, acting like she was so special!","Even Lady Liu, who was confined to her quarters, felt some of the pent-up frustration in her chest dissipate when she heard the news.","She had only found out after being confined that the Crown Prince had mistakenly thought the bowl of Chinese yam and wolfberry soup she had sent over was from Lady Shen across the courtyard, which was why he had gone to visit her in the first place.","When she learned that, she had been so furious that her head had spun, and she felt like spitting blood.","That soup was hers! And what had happened? It had indeed drawn the Crown Prince's attention, but through a stupid misunderstanding, he had thought Lady Shen had made it. Lady Shen had stolen all the credit, and on top of that, she, Lady Liu, had ended up being confined by the Crown Prince!","She could have torn Lady Shen's heart out with her bare hands.","It was only later, when the Crown Prince had sent a eunuch to reprimand her for snooping on his movements and bribing his personal attendants, that she had broken out in cold sweat, suddenly realizing how much danger she had landed herself in.","She had been completely quiet after that. But now, hearing the news that Lady Shen might be in trouble soon, she was still overjoyed. If she had fallen out of the Crown Prince's favor, why should that woman who had reaped all the benefits of her hard work still be enjoying his grace?","But as they waited and waited... word came that Lady Shen had sent people to the palace kitchen to fetch her noon meal, and was already eating peacefully.","The people who had been waiting eagerly were all confused.","A ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍little later, they heard that Lady Shen had taken her people out to stroll in the palace garden.","They were even more bewildered. Could it be that their guess was wrong?","After a while, news came that the Crown Prince, who had returned to the front hall, had suddenly flown into a rage.","Everyone perked up immediately, their eyes wide.","Shen Yanshui had taken a walk in the garden to aid digestion after her lunch. She had played with the cute, sweet-talking Little Jade for a while before heading back.","On her way back, she ran into Lady Wu by the Moonflower Gate unexpectedly.","Shen Yanshui stopped and curtsied to greet her. \"This servant greets Lady Wu.\"","Lady Wu was wearing a loose, lightweight large-sleeve gown of pale cyan, while her hair was styled in an elaborate, intricate updo dotted all over with glittering pearls and jewels that made her look strikingly elegant and imposing.","Lady Wu rested one hand on the arm of her maid, carrying herself with an air of utmost superiority. She looked at Shen Yanshui and smiled meaningfully.","Then she feigned surprise. \"Sister Shen, please rise. I heard that you personally went to the kitchen to make fruit drinks for the Crown Prince today? I never knew you had such excellent skills! When you have time, do come over to my courtyard more often to keep me company, and let me have a taste of your cooking too.\"","Shen Yanshui smiled, looking slightly shy as she pressed her lips together. \"Sister Wu, you are far too complimentary. I have already given the recipe for that fruit drink to Chief Steward Tang at the kitchen. If you would like to have some, you can just send someone to the kitchen to ask for it any time you wish.\"","With a tone of utter sincerity, she said, \"But if Sister Wu would only have a meal made personally by this little sister, I happen to be completely free right now. If it is convenient at Sister Chu's place, I can go over and make something for you to taste at once.\"","The smile on Lady Wu's face froze for a split second. What was wrong with this woman? Why wasn't she playing by the expected rules?","She was clearly humiliating her! How could this woman still keep a smile on her face?!","Wait a minute...","Her expression shifted sharply. \"Are you mocking me?\"","The very idea of going back to her courtyard to cook for her was ridiculous—her courtyard didn't have a small private kitchen permitted by the Crown Prince! In the entire Eastern Palace, only the Crown Prince, the Crown Princess, and the pregnant Lady Chu had small private kitchens in their residences.","Shen Yanshui looked at her with a perfectly innocent face and said, \"You've misunderstood me, Sister Wu. How would this little sister ever dare to mock you? Every word I said was truly from the bottom of my heart.\"","Lady Wu let out a cold snort, then lifted her chin to look at her with a mocking, smug expression. \"What do you have left to be proud of? You actually dared to splash tea all over the Crown Prince. Even if his Highness is broad-minded and chooses not to hold it against you, the Crown Princess and Her Majesty the Empress will never let you get away with it!\"","Shen Yanshui: \"...\" Who on earth made up such a baseless rumor? It didn't even have a shred of credibility!","Was she so tired of living that she would dare splash tea on the Crown Prince? Thinking back to how that cup of tea had actually ended up in the Crown Prince's presence, she couldn't help curling her lip in disdain. If that man dared to pin the blame on her and get her punished... hmph, she would make sure he regretted it.","As for exactly how she would make him \"regret it\", she would figure that out later.","Seeing that Shen Yanshui had gone silent, apparently shocked, Lady Wu's face lit up with smug satisfaction. She spoke in a lecturing tone, \"Are you scared now? It's good that you know fear. Don't think that just because you have a pretty face and have received a little favor from the Crown Prince, you can ignore all rules of hierarchy and propriety...\"","She was enjoying the sound of her own scolding so much that she failed to notice that the palace maid standing beside her had turned deathly pale and was trembling all over with terror.","Shen Yanshui had heard the familiar footsteps long ago, so she simply bowed her head quietly and listened to the lecture, pretending to notice nothing at all.","Lady Wu hadn't caused her any real, substantial harm so far, but that was only because Shen Yanshui herself was not the meek, yielding type who would let anyone walk all over her. Still, every time they ran into each other, Lady Wu would ramble on and on in front of her. At first, Shen Yanshui had found it somewhat amusing, but now even she was growing tired of it.","Clearly, Lady Wu hadn't learned her lesson from the last time they'd clashed. She'd gotten a tiny bit of gossip and couldn't wait to show off, gloat, and preen in front of her.","Lady Wu had been a little restrained at the start, knowing full well that she'd lost the verbal sparring with Shen Yanshui more than once before. But now that she thought Shen Yanshui had truly angered the Crown Prince and been scared speechless, she grew more and more excited, and her lecturing grew bolder and more unbridled.","\"...As the daughter of a distinguished military clan, it's only natural that this little sister might have poor manners, act a little roughly, and lack proper etiquette. Luckily, the Haitang Garden is right next door to my Lotus Heart Courtyard. I'll have plenty of time to teach you proper rules and decorum, so that you won't make a foolish mistake later and end up dragging the Crown Prince's reputation down with you...\"","\"I never imagined that a lowly Lady Wu would have the authority to lecture and discipline the imperial concubines of this palace.\" Cui Yu spoke in a cold, stern voice as he stepped out from behind the bushes, casting a dispassionate glance at Lady Wu, who had fallen to her knees, her face as white as a sheet."]}]);
